    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/reverse-engineering-lab-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant",
      "description": "Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant 495423 Student Department NIAR Reverse Engineering Lab Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Reverse Engineering Lab is looking for a student assistant to assist with the 3D scanning and processing of scan data. 3D Scanning equipment will be used in obtaining accurate 3D data from various aircraft to support programs within NIAR. There will also be tasks of reading CAD Drawings to be able to locate components and properly position scan data in CAD software. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties · Operating 3D Scanners and diligently capturing the geometry of aircraft parts. · Work may contain some lifting and moving heavy parts up to 50 lbs. · Working with 3D Scan data, processing, and positioning pieces in software relative to adjacent aircraft parts. · Report daily activities to the supervisor at the end of each shift worked. · All equipment and software training needed for this job are provided through the lob. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements · Excel spreadsheet experience · Excellent written and oral communication is a must · Must be detailed oriented · Must be able to work independently and in groups · 20hrs per Week required and up to 30hrs per Week allowed during regular semesters · Must have reliable transportation to and from work daily · Working in 3D modeling software, Reading drawings, blueprint reading Additional Information for Posting The job position will require both manual operation of various scanning equipment and software processing tools of scan data. Most scanning will require being on your feet most of the day and actively maneuvering around large items. Some scanning will require positioning scanners under, inside, and above aircraft and can require a good amount of physical activity to lift and move scanners and accessories into location and sometimes be in tight spaces. The position will also require computer skills for processing scan data and keeping the data organized. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) c3ebe76b Last Name (required) ba4508f8 Email (required) b4cac2c7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) fa0b1de0 Last Name (required) 013d6093 Email (required) 7b23278f Job Alert 0bab3cb4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories 