    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-wichita-kansas-united-states-2ce72a69-3f6b-489c-af7b-4a1b3a0b511c": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher - Wichita, Kansas, United States Postdoctoral Researcher - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Researcher College of Engineering | Staff Postdoctoral Researcher 498265 Staff Department: Mechanical Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary range is $45,000 to $50,000 annually Work Schedule: Generally 8am - 5pm, Monday - Friday. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Wichita State University invites applications for a postdoctoral researcher position focusing on the design, synthesis, and characterization of advanced inorganic nanomaterials for wastewater treatment, energy harvest, and environmental engineering-centric applications. This position is part of an NSF-funded program, and the successful candidate is expected to engage in a broad range of research and academic activities supporting the program’s goals. Key responsibilities include: • Design and synthesis of advanced inorganic nanomaterials (e.g., transition-metal-based nanoparticles) by adopting state-of-the-art chemical and physical techniques. • Structural characterization of synthetic inorganic nanomaterials through modern instrumentation techniques (e.g., XRD, BET, XPS, SEM, and TEM). • Development of functional membranes incorporated with enabling inorganic nanomaterials for wastewater treatment and energy harvest. • Collaboration with the modeling and simulation team on the design, engineering, and optimization of functional membranes and associated integrated application systems. Job Summary Administers a variety of studies within scientific or scholarly area of expertise. Performs research study analyses, writes reports and publications, and coordinates with others in carrying out research. Essential Functions Participates with others on research projects. Builds upon previous or concurrent research. Develops research projects through a variety of methods, collaborations and analyses. Gathers data and develops statistical analyses to assimilate and interpret research results. Resolves data and/or research issues. Researches, writes, and communicates research progress and outcomes. Maintains research facility data, equipment, and specimens to ensure compliance with applicable rules and regulations. May supervise the work of others. Job Duties The job duties include: conducting experimental syntheses of inorganic nanomaterials, characterizing synthetic nanomaterials, and fabricating functional membranes for water/energy applications, performing computational analyses, preparing technical reports, drafting scientific publications, and collaborating with interdisciplinary research team members. Required Education and Experience: Doctorate degree in a related field One (1) year of experience in research, laboratory, scholarly setting, or related field Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong written and verbal communication skills. Logical analysis and critical thinking. Proficient laboratory bench capabilities in materials synthesis and instrumentation characterization. Proven ability to work effectively in large collaborative teams. Preferred Qualifications: PhD earned in materials engineering, chemistry engineering, or a closely related discipline. Academic credentials (peer-reviewed journal publications) in the synthesis and characterization of advanced inorganic nanomaterials. Established expertise in the design, fabrication, and scale-up of functional membranes. Relevant experience in environmental engineering applications in areas such as wastewater treatment and energy harvest. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept"
