    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-composites-scheduling-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR Composites Scheduling Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR Composites Scheduling Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Composites Scheduling Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Composites Scheduling Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR Composites Scheduling Student Assistant 495510 Student Department NIAR Composites & Structures Lab Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The NIAR Composites & Structures Lab is looking for hard working student to help with tracking sheets, processes, organization, sending checklists, and so much more. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Communication and cooperation with coworkers • Reading and understanding of Tracking Sheets and processes • Familiarization with ASTM Standards • Creating Excel spreadsheets to organize and keep track of dates and processes • Assist staff with certain responsibilities that are required • Sending checklists to other internal groups dictating what needs to be done • Delivering extracted specimen to other internal groups • Handling/managing extracted specimen and various information Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications • GPA: 2.75+ • Year: Freshman/Sophomore • Strong attention to detail • Strong organizational and communication skills • Ability to effectively prioritize and manage workflow based on expectations 