    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/director-broadcast-maintenance-engineering-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering",
      "description": "Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering - Wichita, Kansas, United States Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Academic Affairs Direct | Staff Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering 499683 Staff Department: KMUW Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Old Town Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 9-5, M-F and on call outside of normal business hours; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs, and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Job Summary Provides leadership and strategic direction for the planning, development and implementation of all technical station maintenance, improvement, and system compliance efforts to ensure achievement or quality control objectives, compliance with regulatory agencies, and University goals. Essential Functions • Provides leadership for and execution of the maintenance and repair of broadcast studio equipment and systems. May supervise work of technicians. • Leads the continuous improvement of operational capabilities and supports the development of all revenue and audience producing efforts. • Records and produces live events, ensuring broadcast quality and compliance. • Provides support for audio, administrative, and industry specific software. • Develops, implements and maintains policies, objectives, projects and short- and long-range plans to accomplish goals. • Develops and manages annual engineering budget. • Maintains up-to-date knowledge and understanding of evolving industry advancements and requirements. Identifies and informs the department of the potential impact of trends and changes. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college coursework in media or broadcast engineering. Six (6) years of experience in engineer broadcasting or related field, with two (2) years of experience in a leadership role. An additional 60 hours of college coursework can be substituted for two (2) years of experience Required License/Certifications/Training: Society of Broadcast Engineering (SBE) broadcast technician certification or ability to obtain within 6 months of hire. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: FM Transmitter maintenance, knowledge of high voltage maintenance practices Facility maintenance skills (including but not limited to coordinating contractors) Satellite downlink repair and maintenance Windows and Mac configuration and repair IP and baseband audio setup and troubleshooting Equipment repair to component level Ability to plan, determine costs for and direct a project, including planning and appropriate and complete documentation, delegating assignments, directing contractors and follow-up. Preferred Qualifications: AOIP configuration / maintenance (Axia and STL gear) ENCO automation operation / configuration Some basic programming skills in: JavaScript, PHP, HTML, batch files Server and network switch configuration and maintenance Physical Requirements: Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Additional Physical Requirement: Heavy Work: Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 20 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Be able to lift 60lbs to shoulder height. Comfortable on ladders and roof tops. Able to climb onto satellite dishes. High Voltage in transmitters, loud environment in transmitter building and at concerts, temperature extremes during outside work for maintenance or concert recording. Safely work in the dark during power outages. Apply Now First Name (required) 957b4d15 Last Name (required) be910e0c Email (required) 5080331b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 61ff924f Last Name (required) c0cade4e Email (required) 91c367f4 Job Alert aba40806 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and