    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/talent-search-south-assistant-director-college-readiness-retention-programs-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Talent Search-South Assistant Director, College Readiness/Retention Programs",
      "description": "Talent Search-South Assistant Director, College Readiness/Retention Programs - Wichita, Kansas, United States Talent Search-South Assistant Director, College Readiness/Retention Programs - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Talent Search-South Assistant Director, College Readiness/Retention Programs Strategic Engagement & Planning | Academic/Student Support, Staff Talent Search-South Assistant Director, College Readiness/Retention Programs 499680 Academic/Student Support Staff Department: TRIO Talent Search-South Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range starting $42,000/yr, adjusted based on qualifications Work Schedule: Mon-Fri, 8a-5p, occasional overnights; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Some people are naturally good at keeping things organized. Others are naturally good with people. This role needs both. This position exists to ensure that program services are delivered as approved, documented accurately, and aligned with U.S. Department of Education TRIO regulations—while keeping students, families, and partner schools at the center of the work. Working closely with the Director, this position helps translate federal objectives into consistent, high-quality services that move students toward postsecondary enrollment and success. And while there is important program administration behind the scenes, this is not a desk-only role. A majority of your time will be spent at South High School, working directly with students. You’ll build relationships, answer questions, follow up when someone needs an extra nudge, and become a familiar, trusted person in the school community. You’ll help manage program schedules, recruiting efforts, budgets, documentation, and other administrative responsibilities while ensuring services are delivered as approved and align with U.S. Department of Education TRIO requirements. Organization and compliance matter, but so does knowing when to put down the spreadsheet and connect with a student. You’ll communicate with students, families, school personnel, university partners, program staff, and leadership, so being able to adjust your communication style and connect with people at different levels is essential. If you’re the kind of person who can manage the details, support leadership, communicate with just about anyone, and still have the energy to spend your day working with students, we want to meet you. Job Summary Manages assigned college readiness and/or retention program(s) to meet business objectives. Oversees the day-to-day program activities which may include project schedules, budget tracking and development, recruiting, and project and/or program administration. Essential Functions Collaborates with senior leaders to develop program goals and infrastructure to align with defined business strategy. Creates new or troubleshoots and improves upon existing processes, procedures or systems to meet program goals. Manages program through creation of program plans, grant proposals, management tools and/or reporting capabilities. Performs project research and develops plans to effectively use program resources. Develops metrics to measure program success against program goals. Manages, recruits, trains and/or leads cross-functional teams and ensures resources are appropriately assigned to meet program goals. Recommends program or project budget according to needs. Monitors and adjusts project and program plans as resource requirements change. Communicates and documents program quality outcomes and progress metrics to senior program leaders. Regularly contacts participants, counselors, and partners to ensure program success. Addresses and resolves major or complex issues to ensure program goals remain on track. Job Duties Assigned Schools: Truesdell Middle School and South High School (plus walk-in support as needed) Key Responsibilities -Support implementation of Talent Search services in compliance with federal TRIO guidelines and grant objectives -Serve approximately 360 students annually, ensuring each one receives meaningful, documented, and compliant federal TRIO services. -Assist with staff supervision, training, and service monitoring -Oversee student service delivery, progress tracking, and documentation -Support data management, evaluation, and Annual Performance Report (APR) preparation -Maintain partnerships with schools, families, and community stakeholders -Assist with budget monitoring and program operations -Maintain accurate records and preparing reports to support federal performance measures Required Education and Experience: Qualifications for this position are strictly defined by the approved grant proposal. See the education qualifications in the \"Additional Information for Posting\" section below. Qualifications for this position are strictly defined by the approved grant proposal. See the experience qualifications in the \"Additional Information for Posting\" section below. Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of TRIO Talent Search-South program purpose, objectives, and required services as defined by the U.S. Department of Education Familiar with federal grant administration, compliance, and recordkeeping requirements Knowledge of postsecondary education preparation, including academic planning, career exploration, and financial aid processes Capable of data collection, performance reporting, and confidentiality requirements Skilled in assisting with administration and coordination of federally funded educational programs Understand how to monitor delivery of required TRIO services and documenting participation and outcomes Capable in supervising and supporting staff engaged in student services Skilled in effective communication with students, parents, schools, and institutional partners Ability to ensure program services are implemented in accordance with approved grant objectives and federal regulations Familiar with or able to learn how to translate federal requirements into consistent daily program operations Support partnerships with secondary schools and families to promote college access Exercise sound judgment in matters involving compliance, confidentiality, and student support Preferred Qualifications: Prior TRIO/GEAR UP experience or other educational opportunity programs or organizations. Additional Information: Position Requirements: Master's degree in education, social service, psychology or related field. One year's experience developing programming and scheduling for students and staff. At least two years' experience working with low-income and potential first generation college students. Two years' or more supervisory or managerial experience. The chosen candidate is expected maintain membership in TRIO professional associations; write articles for the quarterly newsletter; and travel to local, regional, and national training seminars/conferences. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to travel in a vehicle for distances including but not limited to across city, county, and state. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) ed8deb07 Last Name (required) 515f0620 Email (required) 0c6c87fe Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 60268a5a Last Name (required) b31f3e05 Email (required) 3d52714a Job Alert 283e65f5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Staff Academic/Student Support Staff Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 36600503 Last Name (required) 86a7d10c Email (required) fdf27bea Send This Job To: ac321c3e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 892a4dba Last Name (required) e8935805 Email (required) 2b88fbab Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
