    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/custodial-lead-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Custodial Lead",
      "description": "Custodial Lead - Wichita, Kansas, United States Custodial Lead - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Custodial Lead Physical Plant | Staff Custodial Lead 499392 Staff Department: Facilities Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starting at $16.49 plus $.60 per hour shift differential and commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 3:00 pm - 11:30 pm Monday - Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff. As a Custodial Lead, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment. And the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Job Summary Performs specialized custodial services, such as maintenance and repair of custodial equipment, floor cleaning and finishing equipment, carpet and upholstery maintenance equipment in University buildings. Acts as a liaison between custodial staff and leadership to ensure service excellence. Essential Functions Maintains and performs minor repairs on custodial equipment, such as vacuums, floor and carpet cleaners, etc. Completes basic maintenance on floor care equipment. Performs specialized custodial services such as floor cleaning and finishing, carpet and upholstery maintenance, cleaning building furnishings and/or procedures using specialty cleaning chemicals. Cleans and services assigned areas in University buildings and maintains sufficient stock and supplies for the proper performance of these duties. Provides all floor care services including strip, wax, carpet cleaning and may provide disaster recovery for affected flooring. Utilizes cleaning machinery such as scrubbers, buffers, and carpet extractors for floor care maintenance. Performs regular inspections of all areas to determine need for services and/or quality of services performed. Communicates findings and recommendations to leadership. Provides guidance and coaching to custodial staff as needed. Conducts service recovery efforts in response to questions and/or concerns from faculty, staff, students, and visitors according to the department's customer service protocols. Assists supervisor with payroll, scheduling, education of department staff, budget and other duties as assigned. Shovels and removes snow and ice from designated areas such as roofs, sidewalks and entryways as required. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in custodial work Required License/Certifications/Training: Valid Driver's License Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of the materials, methods and practices used in housekeeping operations and operation, use care of vacuum cleaners, scrubbing machines, floor machines and other janitorial equipment; and the use of safe principles and safe techniques for Supervision. Familiarity with the principles of inventory control: sanitation and all practices and procedures. Ability to work and supervise effectively with fellow workers and others Ability to keep and maintain records. Ability to maintain and organize filing and record keeping systems, confidential information. Ability to supervise multiple custodial work units and various projects, work orders, and personnel. Physical Requirements: Ability to position self to clean designated areas, equipment and items. This includes but is not limited to the ability to clean in confined, elevated, and loud noise spaces. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to drive state vehicle. Ability to remove snow and ice from designated areas. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Additional Physical Requirement: Heavy Work: Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 20 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) 15bee836 Last Name (required) 4f364b5b Email (required) 19b337f3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 5ba6dcb4 Last Name (required) 8f19edc1 Email (required) d9d86235 Job Alert 07b46528 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Physical Plant Physical Plant Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 4785e2d8 Last Name (required) 4b1d925f Email (required) 6cd25f9e Send This Job To: e98e18c5 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 2f43c934 Last Name (required) f7452cd9 Email (required) 0d2abdda Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/program-counselor-college-readiness-retention-programs-wichita-kansas-united-states-07089b2a-68c1-4371-b5ff-afedb9b06bb4": {
      "title": "Program Counselor, College Readiness/Retention Programs",
      "description": "Program Counselor, College Readiness/Retention Programs - Wichita, Kansas, United States Program Counselor, College Readiness/Retention Programs - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Program Counselor, College Readiness/Retention Programs Strategic Engagement & Planning | Staff Program Counselor, College Readiness/Retention Programs 498700 Staff Department: TRIO Talent Search Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $18.00 - 19.06 based on experience Work Schedule: Mon-Fri, 8a-5p Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Be the Reason a Student Says, “I’m Going to College.” If you’re the kind of person who sees potential before others do… If you believe access to education shouldn’t depend on zip code… If you’re energized by mentoring youth and watching confidence grow in real time… TRIO Talent Search is looking for you! Assigned Schools: Marshall Middle School and North High School (plus walk-in support as needed) This isn’t a desk job. It’s boots-on-the-ground, sleeves-rolled-up, future-building work. You’ll work directly with middle and high school students, many of whom will be first-generation college students, guiding them toward academic persistence, high school graduation, and postsecondary enrollment. You’ll serve approximately 290 students annually, ensuring each one receives meaningful, documented, and compliant federal TRIO services. The heart of this job? Relationships. What You’ll Actually Be Doing: Collaborate with school administrators and community partners Identify eligible students for the program & monitor their academic progress (intervening when needed) Building partnerships & relationships along the way at various levels Maintaining accurate student records and ensuring federal compliance Yes, there’s documentation — because impact matters, and so does accountability. You'll Thrive Here If You: Connect easily with youth across diverse backgrounds Know how to balance encouragement with structure Can pivot quickly when student needs shift (because they will) Are organized enough to manage data while staying fully present with students Understand referral networks and aren’t afraid to collaborate Believe that mentorship can literally change a life trajectory You are intentional. Strategic. Consistent. In a world where conversations about equity, opportunity gaps, and educational access dominate headlines, this is where the real work happens, one student at a time. If you’re ready to build futures, we want to hear from you. Apply. Mentor. Advocate. Change trajectories! Job Summary Coordinates program participation which includes, but is not limited to, identifying program participants, facilitating program application, and providing counseling and advising services. Essential Functions • Identifies, recruits and selects new program participants. Facilitates the application process by assisting with application completion and coordinating the application selection committee. • Meets on a routine basis with program students to review academic progress and graduate school preparation. • Facilitates education to program participants on a variety of topics which assist with graduate school preparation. • Assists in the development and administration of program evaluation tools. Collects and supplies evaluation data necessary for grant submission. • Coordinates program communication to inform and educate the campus community and community at-large of program events and activities. Job Duties Recruitment of eligible students, including identifying and selecting students for relevant program services and activities. Educate and support students on the college admissions and financial aid process to enhance students’ chances of entering a postsecondary institution. Facilitate individual and group study sessions and conduct and/or present ACT, financial aid, and career workshops for students and their parents. Collaborates with public school personnel and establishes relationships with community agencies to identify students for program participation and to develop a plan of supporting services for students. Assists program staff and may teach one course during the Middle School Summer Enrichment Program for twenty-five (25) middle school students. Arranges and accompanies students on field trips, college campus visits, and other related activities. Required Education and Experience: Qualifications for this position are strictly defined by the approved grant proposal. See the education qualifications in the \"Additional Information for Posting\" section below. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of financial literacy, federal financial aid programs, and scholarships. Familiar working with student populations and/or similar educational opportunity programs. Strong communication skills, including presentations and/or public speaking. Understanding of problems faced by low income and potential first-generation college students. Competent with basic computer systems and software applications. Bilingual English/Spanish proficiency preferred. Additional Information: Per the requirements of the grant, eligible candidates must possess: A Bachelor's degree in education, social science, psychology or related field. One (1) year experience providing social services to and working with eligible participants. One (1) year experience in providing personal and/or career counseling. The chosen candidate is expected to maintain membership in TRIO professional associations; write articles for the quarterly newsletter; and travel to local, regional, and national training seminars and conferences. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Frequent 60-90% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Ability to travel in a vehicle for distances including but not limited to across city, county, and state. Rare 0-30% Apply Now First Name (required) c9cc96a8 Last Name (required) 59cf6b84 Email (required) a0e3cadb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 2db5b141 Last Name (required) d23f890e Email (required) ade2583b Job Alert c7962c17 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 413cdda7 Last Name (required) 65349bd7 Email (required) 4ae97c43 Send This Job To: 7ccb8ef8 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy