    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/executive-assistant-and-human-resources-generalist-wichita-kansas-united-states-80b2487d-382b-4e91-a02c-15ffe082c7e9": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant and Human Resources Generalist",
      "description": "Executive Assistant and Human Resources Generalist - Wichita, Kansas, United States Executive Assistant and Human Resources Generalist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Executive Assistant and Human Resources Generalist Culture and HR | Staff Executive Assistant and Human Resources Generalist 499767 Staff Department: Human Resources Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range beginning $23.68/hr, adjusted based on qualifications Work Schedule: Monday-Friday 8am-5pm, on site; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story We seek a professional that doesn't need a job with a predictable checklist, but prefers variety. We’re looking for an adaptable, people-oriented professional who enjoys being at the center of an active office, supporting executive staff, helping employees, coordinating daily operations, and figuring out what needs to happen next. That means interacting with people across different roles and levels, supporting HR services, helping keep business operations organized, and making sure the office itself functions smoothly. The ideal person for this role doesn't need someone standing over their shoulder telling them what to do next. This is a role for someone who can walk into a busy morning with five priorities, discover three more by lunch, and still know what needs to get done by the end of the day. You can look at a situation, gather the information you need, determine what matters most, and make a sound decision. Because you'll interact with people constantly, professional communication and genuine people skills matter. When something unexpected happens, your instinct is to figure it out not wait for someone else to hand you the answer. You’re organized, but flexible. You can prioritize competing demands, switch gears quickly, and keep important details from falling through the cracks. Who will thrive here? You may come from an office management, HR, executive support, administrative coordination, or similar background. If you were the person running an office almost single-handedly, knowing who needed what, which deadline was approaching, and what problem needed solving before anyone else noticed it, you're already a step ahead of the rest. What matters most is that you're resourceful, organized, approachable, and comfortable with controlled chaos. You can multitask without losing focus. You can prioritize without being asked. You can communicate with confidence. If you can handle all this & looking for a supportive team that figures out how to get things done, apply with us! Job Summary Provides support in delivering HR services and administrative support to executive staff. Coordinates the office activities of a department including the reception area, business operations, and facilities. Essential Functions • Acts as a resource for employees regarding all HR-related inquiries, policies, and procedures including but not limited to, employee relations, performance management, talent acquisition, and operational processes, ensuring timely and accurate responses. Consults with other university offices as needed to resolve more complex questions. • Provides ongoing monitoring and tracking of department budget. • Maintains executive's schedule by planning and scheduling meetings, conferences, teleconferences, and/or making travel arrangements as well as manage incoming calls for executive phone line. • Coordinates all office functions including but not limited to administering staff changes, departmental continuity plan, training, supplies, equipment maintenance, repairs and renovations. • Resolves office problems independently and facilitates solutions; confers with supervisor to resolve more complex situations. Job Duties Department budget & purchasing- tracking of expenses, approvals, payment of invoices, purchase card reconciliations, expense submission, scheduling/coordinating travel plans/expenses, reporting for director Manage calendar, scheduling, rescheduling meetings, booking rooms Coordinator of HR office to include logistical & operational needs regularly. This includes but is not limited to equipment requests, organizing of schedules, orders, & additional projects. Triage all incoming traffic to the HR dept, through phone, email, & in person. Initial point of contact for issues/questions to be resolved for multiple areas of HR. Customer service is a priority as the first point of contact for the office. Utilize multiple university systems for processing of needs &/or requests. Process unemployment claims & documentation retrieval. Process employment verifications, DoD verifications & other similar requests. Acts as a member or support to other HR teams during peak seasons to mitigate influx of needs from the university during those times. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college coursework business administration or social science. Three (3) years of experience in human resources or related field. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Provide professional, responsive customer service, both in verbal and written format. Priority focus given to customer experience in interactions with HR. Collaborative nature to connect all HR areas, as questions or issues often cross over. Ability to manage walk-in traffic, phone calls, email and assigned responsibilities. Ability to handle constant interruptions & multi-tasking while still able to meet deadlines & completion of work with accuracy. Gather knowledge of all areas within HR to provide first-line answers to questions and HR processes. Take initiative using professional judgement to create solutions that meet compliance and process standards. Capable to quickly learn various systems which are independent from each other to accomplish daily operations. Preferred Qualifications: Prefer previous work experience with providing high volume customer service over the phone and via email. Prefer experience with budgeting for a department/organization. Prefer experience with unemployment, verification of employment, i-9s and reverifications. Experience within HR & knowledge of multiple HR realms. Additional Information: Working conditions for this position is on-site at WSU's main campus Physical Requirements: Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Frequent 60-90% Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Frequent 60-90% Ability to remain in a stationary position. Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) c40dda4d Last Name (required) ae48d609 Email (required) 627143e3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d431e626 Last Name (required) ce544555 Email (required) 84f64854 Job Alert fee4dab9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Culture and HR Culture and HR Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 7dfcc523 Last Name (required) 8d44e19a Email (required) e616df31 Send This Job To: 6cf45f82 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our 