    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/deloitte-smart-factory-support-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Deloitte Smart Factory Support Student Assistant",
      "description": "Deloitte Smart Factory Support Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Deloitte Smart Factory Support Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Deloitte Smart Factory Support Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student Deloitte Smart Factory Support Student Assistant 496368 Student Department Ennovar Tech Services and Solutions Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 - $18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Ennovar is looking for an outstanding student to work at Deloitte's The Smart Factory on Innovation Campus to help with smart factory technologies. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Assist with planning and logistics for client tours of The Smart Factory @ Wichita, ensuring a curated experience tailored to client goals. • Support the development and implementation of Smart Factory use cases in collaboration with Deloitte’s Innovation Campus operations. • Assist with testing, integration, and maintenance of line components, systems, and quality control processes. • Contribute to the creation of work instructions and quality inspection protocols for various manufacturing cells on the production line. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements • Currently pursuing a degree in Computer Science; strong interest in Data Science preferred. Must be enrolled at Wichita State University for the duration of employment. • Strong interest in supply chain, operations, and Industry 4.0 technologies. • Ability to grasp and explain supply chain concepts and smart manufacturing strategies. • Demonstrated analytical and critical thinking skills. • Professional demeanor with strong character and executive presence. • Effective communicator, including in virtual or remote environments. • Ability to troubleshoot and resolve issues related to systems, processes, and development tools. • Familiarity with process improvement methods (e.g., Lean, Six Sigma). • Business acumen (basic understanding of accounting, finance, etc.). • Proficient in problem-solving with a process-oriented mindset. • Basic coding knowledge is a plus, but not required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment, including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 9a409a08 Last Name (required) 2739b6b1 Email (required) 2e7e7a29 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 1a9d8fea Last Name (required) 34aa5024 Email (required) be45409b Job Alert cabda79b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & da