    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-cad-cam-engineering-design-checker-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR CAD/CAM Engineering Design Checker",
      "description": "NIAR CAD/CAM Engineering Design Checker - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR CAD/CAM Engineering Design Checker - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CAD/CAM Engineering Design Checker NIAR Institute | Temporary NIAR CAD/CAM Engineering Design Checker 495586 Temporary Department NIAR CAD/CAM Lab Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $50 per hour Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Details Independently compares and verifies that 3D models are complete and accurate representations of 2D data packages. Develops and recommends solutions to design problems. Job Duties • Examines engineering drawings and related documents. • Compares 3D models and annotations to the provided 2D documents to ensure quality, accuracy, and completeness. • Provide feedback to the modelers and annotators on any errors or omissions. • Interfaces with modelers and annotators and helps mentor development. Additional Requirements • Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings and specifications • Proficient in reading 2D drawings • Ability to listen effectively, take direction, and possess initiative to accomplish assigned tasks Preferred Qualifications • Bachelor’s Degree in Engineering or related field • 2 years of related experience • Work is completed in-person and onsite in Wichita, KS Physical Requirements Ability to lift and carry up to 25 lbs Apply Now First Name (required) 127ebe8c Last Name (required) 671ac33f Email (required) 2b0ff6e3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 34640cdc Last Name (required) 2d218e52 Email (required) 6689ff70 Send This Job To: a0925ad7 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordin