    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/idp-compliance-services-coordinator-wichita-kansas-united-states-bcfc1653-c1ae-4e84-a5c8-1e223f26c40b": {
      "title": "IDP Compliance Services Coordinator",
      "description": "IDP Compliance Services Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States IDP Compliance Services Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode IDP Compliance Services Coordinator Office Ind & Defense Administration | Staff IDP Compliance Services Coordinator 499804 Staff Department: Industry & Defense Compliance Office Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Typically, Monday - Friday 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Details The Compliance Services Coordinator supports the university’s research compliance operations by managing administrative, operational, and data workflows that ensure alignment with federal, state, and institutional requirements. This position coordinates compliance board activities, maintains regulatory records, assists with COI/COC and misconduct processes, and serves as a key resource for researchers navigating protocol and compliance needs. Strong organization, communication, and data management skills are essential. Job Summary Provides support in the oversight of research compliance components the university. Manages the operational, administrative, and data workflows required to maintain institutional alignment with local, state and/or federal research requirements. Essential Functions Manages the operational, administrative, and data workflows required to maintain institutional alignment with local, state and/or federal research requirements. Manages operations for institutional research compliance boards including, but not limited to, preparing agendas, documenting minutes, and tracking protocol approval periods. Maintains accurate database records, audit logs, and internal tracking systems ensuring data integrity for regulatory reporting requirements and audit readiness. Serves as a resource and the primary point of contact for research personnel regarding compliance requirements, protocol submissions, and issue resolution. Assists with Conflict of Interest/Conflict of Commitment (COI/COC) reviews and management of Research Misconduct cases. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Six (6) years of experience working within research administration, quality assurance, or regulatory compliance settings; every 30 hours of related college coursework may be substituted for one (1) year of experience up to four (4) years. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of Federal research compliance frameworks (OHRP, FDA, HIPAA) and grant processes. Knowledge of research administration, protocol review cycles, COI/COC, and misconduct procedures. Strong organization, data management, and attention to detail. Clear written and verbal communication with diverse stakeholders. Proficiency in Microsoft 365 and Windows-based systems. Manage multiple compliance workflows and regulatory projects. Maintain confidentiality and sound judgment. Coordinate board operations, track approvals, and maintain audit‑ready records. Interpret and apply regulatory requirements consistently. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Apply Now First Name (required) c8e9f56c Last Name (required) 1539b65b Email (required) 93c656ee Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 3d3306ee Last Name (required) de982442 Email (required) fe3f38de Job Alert f01f4acc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Office Ind & Defense Administration Office Ind & Defense Administration Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 75063bb4 Last Name (required) abb3be04 Email (required) f5629800 Send This Job To: a2b353e8 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 9ac2a7c2 Last Name (required) 69428350 Email (required) 7ef958f8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/parking-enforcement-specialist-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Parking Enforcement Specialist",
      "description": "Parking Enforcement Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States Parking Enforcement Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Parking Enforcement Specialist WSU Police Department | Staff Parking Enforcement Specialist 499715 Staff Department: Parking & Transportation Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $15.34/hour and is commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 7 AM - 3 PM; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The University's Parking & Transportation Services has an opening for a 1st shift Parking Enforcement Specialist. This position also comes with a robust benefits package (effective on your first day) and generous paid time off. Job Summary Performs parking compliance work, safeguarding property owned or leased by the University by monitoring and patrolling parking areas for violations and escorting or transporting individuals to specific locations. Essential Functions • Conducts daily monitoring of parking lots for parking violations and issuing parking citations. • Assists in set up and tear down of parking lot reservations and special event needs. Set up and move cones, barricades, parking signs, and VMS (Variable Message Sign) trailers, as needed. • Patrol assigned areas, respond to motorist assistance situations, and observe and report special hazards. • Perform simple vehicle maintenance procedures and report mechanical problems to leadership. Job Duties Provides mobility assistance rides for students, faculty and staff on campus as needed. Assists UPD in performing traffic control duties. Calls upon University police officers to assist with police-related tasks/functions, as necessary. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent None Required License/Certifications/Training: Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) and National Crime Information Center (NCIC) certification within six (6) months of hire date. Valid drivers license Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to efficiently operate the T2 Flex system. Ability to operate a two-way radio. Ability to remain calm under stressful situations. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to give and follow instructions verbally and in writing. Ability to recall and record information concisely and accurately. Ability to read and understand written department guidelines, university policies, laws, rules, and regulations. Ability to build and sustain effective professional and courteous interpersonal relationships with a diverse constituency of faculty, staff, students, and public. Additional Information: During the application process your background will be closely examined. Please review the following background “disqualifiers.” If you think that any of these apply to you and you have questions, please call Parking Services at (316) 978- 5526 for clarification, or for more information. Must not have been convicted of, plead guilty or no contest to, or been diverted on a serious traffic violation within the past three years of date of application. Serious traffic violations to include, but not limited to vehicular homicide, DUI, reckless driving, hit and run, and eluding a police officer. Must not have received three moving violations during the last twelve months or been involved in two accidents for which they were at fault during the past twelve months. Must not be currently charged with, under indictment, or on probation for any criminal activity other than minor traffic violations. Physical Requirements: Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Frequent 60-90% Ability to remain in a stationary position. Occasional 30-60% Ability to inspect and/or surveil materials, equipment, reports, and/or incidents and identify any errors, needs and/or determining factors. Occasional 30-60% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Occasional 30-60% Ability to drive state vehicle. Occasional 30-60% Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Occasional 30-60% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Rare 0-30% Ability to position self to perform safety and security actions determined by police methods and procedures. Rare 0-30% Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Rare 0-30% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) fa435e72 Last Name (required) 35751567 Email (required) f135061e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 827107b3 Last Name (required) 292904e4 Email (required) 71eb1e5f Job Alert 5220ce94 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) WSU Police Department WSU Police Department Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) c1d5bee3 Last Name (required) 49bede72 Email (required) fef5ff8f Send This Job To: adddc897 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like workin