    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/recruitment-and-scholarship-coordinator-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator",
      "description": "Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator Barton School of Business | Academic/Student Support, Staff Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator 499570 Academic/Student Support Staff Department: Barton School Student Success Center Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range $39,700/yr, adjusted based on qualifications Work Schedule: General business hours; Evenings regularly during recruitment season & a couple of wknds in the year; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Be the person who builds the relationship, answers questions, coordinates visits, maintains communication, and guide prospective students through the enrollment process. Just like that Wichita State has a new student on campus! You made that happen! The position serves as a primary point of contact for prospective undergraduate students and families, manages recruitment territories, represents W. Frank Barton School of Business at events, and helps convert interest into applications and enrollment. We are looking for someone who can meet students where they are, communicate clearly, build trust quickly, and keep the recruitment pipeline growing. You're not afraid to chat with others about higher education & get excited by being able to tell people about WSU & all it has to offer! Represent Barton in the Market Build Relationships Recruit Freshmen and Transfer Students Convert Interest into Applications Support & Invigorate Campus Visits and Events Use CRM to Track Data Identify Recruitment Opportunities The Kind of Person Who Thrives Here: Someone who gets recharged by talking with others, variety in what they do, and measurable results with ownership over those. You may come from admissions, recruitment, student services, sales, outreach, or another role where relationships and follow-through matter. Organization is the other side of the coin that you must prosses to be successful though. You can speak with students and families, work with counselors and partners, manage events, use data, and stay organized across many conversations at once. You don't wait for students to find Barton, you go where they are, build the connection, make it feel real to the student & families, follow up at the right time, and help Barton be seen as their next step. Job Summary Collaborates with faculty and staff in a specific college, department, program or specific focal area to coordinate and expand student recruitment efforts. Serves as the coordinator for schools and organizations that align with the recruitment strategy. Aligns scholarship resources with recruitment goals. Coordinates scholarship competitions and promoted scholarship opportunities to qualified students. Essential Functions Represents specific University colleges, departments or programs at specified schools, college and community fairs, public presentations, and/or seminars. Participates in on and off campus recruitment programs, including group presentations; greets walk-in and scheduled visitors; maintains knowledge of all facets of the University. May develop, coordinate and execute all aspects of event planning for recruitment and scholarships to facilitate effective presentation of programs or events. Coordinates with related departments to facilitate recruitment, outreach, and/or marketing of related programs and services. May lead staff in the design and implementation of communications and educational content. Monitors scholarship compliance with program rules and regulations, provides status updates, and monitors student academic progress as required. Identifies, promotes and targets scholarships to eligible students. Collaborates with University staff and students to foster academic success. Job Duties Event planning & full execution - AGH scholarship Plan, organize & inform all team members of the event yearly. This includes participants, catering, venue & other aspects needed for a successful event to occur. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college course work in education or business Four (4) years of experience in recruiting, retention, admissions, or related fields. An additional 60 hours of college coursework beyond the minimum can be substituted for two (2) years of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: Valid Kansas drivers license Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to build strong relationships and rapport quickly. public speaking abilities. Knowledge of event planning aspects Familiar with higher ed admissions process and key university personnel Excellent communication skills and the ability to engage effectively with students, families, and institutional partners Proficiency in using CRM systems and other relevant tools Ability to travel regionally and work occasional evenings and weekends as needed Organized and able to accomplish deadline needs Capable of maintain confidentiality Comfortable engaging with diverse populations Preferred Qualifications: Event planning and execution Additional Information: N/A Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) a944101e Last Name (required) ad3c63b5 Email (required) e98292a2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 45259c05 Last Name (required) 1bfad994 Email (required) c2aff412 Job Alert 51e194b0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Staff Academic/Student Support Staff Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) cf6767a4 Last Name (required) 3d57edd3 Email (required) 38d13ac8 Send This Job To: d5d69a8c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 8de80c67 Last Name (required) 0d180f4b Email (required) 1c3fe8f6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
