    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/machinist-innovation-hub-coe-u4-nbe-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Machinist Innovation Hub CoE U4 NBE",
      "description": "Machinist Innovation Hub CoE U4 NBE - Wichita, Kansas, United States Machinist Innovation Hub CoE U4 NBE - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Machinist Innovation Hub CoE U4 NBE College of Engineering | Temporary Machinist Innovation Hub CoE U4 NBE 499682 Temporary Department Innovation Hub CoE Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 7000/semester Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. TBD with supervisor Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Shape the next generation of manufacturing professionals. We are seeking an experienced and engaging Lecturer in Machining Technology to teach, mentor, and prepare students for careers in modern manufacturing. This position offers the opportunity to combine industry expertise with hands-on instruction in machining, CNC operations, quality control, and manufacturing best practices within a dynamic academic environment. Job Duties The Lecturer in Machining Technology delivers classroom, laboratory, and project-based instruction in machining and manufacturing processes. The successful candidate will teach conventional and Computer Numerical Control (CNC) machining, blueprint reading, metrology, quality systems, safety practices, and manufacturing process improvement concepts. The lecturer will support student success through hands-on training, curriculum development, industry engagement, and academic advising. 1. Teach undergraduate and/or technical courses in machining, manufacturing, and related engineering technology subjects. 2. Deliver classroom, laboratory, and project-based instruction in: o Manual machining o CNC machining o CNC programming (G-code and M-code) o Blueprint reading and GD&T o Metrology and inspection methods o Manufacturing materials and processes 3. Develop and maintain course materials, assignments, laboratory exercises, and assessments. 4. Evaluate student performance and provide timely feedback. Laboratory Management 1. Operate, demonstrate, and supervise the use of machine shop equipment, including CNC mills, CNC lathes, manual mills, engine lathes, grinders, and related equipment. 2. Ensure safe operation of laboratory facilities and enforce compliance with all safety requirements and Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) standards. 3. Coordinate equipment maintenance, calibration, and inventory of tools and consumables. Student Engagement 1. Advise and mentor students regarding academic progress, career planning, internships, and industry certifications. 2. Support student projects, competitions, applied learning activities, and capstone projects. 3. Maintain regular office hours and provide academic support to students. Curriculum and Program Support 1. Participate in curriculum review and continuous improvement activities. 2. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and industry partners to ensure program relevance and workforce alignment. 3. Assist with accreditation, assessment, and program evaluation efforts. Industry and Continuous Improvement 1. Maintain knowledge of current machining technologies, manufacturing trends, automation, and Industry 4.0 practices. 2. Identify opportunities to improve laboratory operations, instructional effectiveness, and student learning outcomes using continuous improvement methodologies. Required Education This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Additional Requirements 1. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds with or without reasonable accommodation. 2. Ability to stand, walk, bend, and work in laboratory environments for extended periods. 3. Strong mathematical skills, including fractions, decimals, geometry, trigonometry, and machining calculations. 4. Ability to operate machine tools safely and effectively. 5. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and student success. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications 1. Bachelor's or Master's degree in Manufacturing Engineering, Engineering Technology, Industrial Technology, Mechanical Engineering, or a related discipline. 2. Previous teaching, corporate training, apprenticeship instruction, or workforce development experience. 3. Experience editing and troubleshooting G-code and CNC programs directly at machine controls. 4. Industry-recognized certifications such as: o NIMS Certifications o SME Certifications o FANUC Certifications o OSHA Safety Training 5. Experience machining diverse materials, including: o Aluminum o Stainless steel o Tool steels o Plastics o Composites 6. Knowledge of CAD/CAM software and computer-aided manufacturing systems. 7. Experience with Lean Manufacturing, Six Sigma, Kaizen, 5S, and continuous improvement methodologies. 8. Familiarity with quality management systems and manufacturing standards. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 058f3fc9 Last Name (required) 52373bd8 Email (required) 5f845acf Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b82eff16 Last Name (required) b2b82d9a Email (required) 45102e5c Job Alert 010fafde Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 17df9669 Last Name (required) e6f80911 Email (required) 94bd5706 Send This Job To: bc76b1e0 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 3234887b Last Name (required) 285e6146 Email (required) bec60d0e Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
