    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-hardware-security-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Hardware Security",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Hardware Security - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Hardware Security - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Hardware Security College of Engineering | Faculty Assistant Professor of Hardware Security 499424 On Site Faculty Department: Electrical and Computer Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range beginning $95,000/yr, commensurate with qualifications Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering in the College of Engineering invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Hardware Security . We seek an innovative scholar and educator who will contribute to the department’s teaching mission, research profile, and applied learning initiatives. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop and sustain a productive and externally visible research program, mentor students, and provide service to the department, college, university, profession, and community. We are seeking applicants whose technical interests in hardware security complement and augment the Department’s existing strengths and who are well positioned to develop collaborations as part of multidisciplinary research teams. Applicants with expertise in all areas of hardware security are encouraged to apply. Our hiring priorities include secure computer architecture, hardware Trojans and supply chain security, secure chip design, PCB security, secure FPGA/ASIC design and verification, embedded and IoT hardware security, fault injection, reverse engineering, hardware side-channel attacks, edge security, embedded AI, and physical attack resistance. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering hosts three undergraduate programs (BS in Computer Engineering, BS in Cybersecurity, and BS in Electrical Engineering), one master's program (MS in Electrical and Computer Engineering), and a Ph.D. program in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science. In addition, the department houses eight graduate certificate programs. The department serves over 500 undergraduate students and 100 graduate students. WSU has been designated as a Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense (CAE-CD) by the National Security Agency. This designation recognizes that WSU cybersecurity programs meet rigorous academic standards and prepare cybersecurity professionals to that will reduce vulnerabilities in our national infrastructure. The department is highly integrated with industry partners across the country and is home to the Hub for Cybersecurity Education and Awareness, the Center for Energy Studies, CommSys Lab, CAPPLab, and the Energy Systems Lab. In addition to these companies, the campus is home to Airbus, NETApp, the National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR), the Deloitte Smart Factory @ Wichita, the Crash Dynamics Lab, the Hub for Advanced Manufacturing and Research (HAMR), and the National Institute for Health Solutions and Innovation (NIHSI). Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching : Develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in hardware security and related areas of computer engineering. Potential teaching areas include processor and system security, secure system-on-chip (SoC) design, trusted computing, hardware Trojans, side-channel attacks, embedded and edge AI systems, FPGA- and ASIC-based system design, Internet of Things (IoT) systems, computer architecture, and other closely related topics. Responsibilities include curriculum development, effective instruction across appropriate delivery modalities, assessment of student learning, academic advising and mentoring, and supervision of undergraduate and graduate student research projects, theses, and dissertations, as appropriate. Research : Establish and maintain a high-quality research program in hardware security or a closely related area. This includes publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating research results through recognized academic venues. The faculty member is expected to pursue external funding through grants and industry collaborations to support research activities and, where appropriate, engage in interdisciplinary projects and industry partnerships. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated through a record of research accomplishments or clear potential for high-quality research productivity. Service : Contribute to service activities within the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, the College of Engineering, Wichita State University, and the broader profession. Service activities may include committee work, curriculum and program development, accreditation and assessment activities, student recruitment and outreach, professional society engagement, peer review, and community or industry outreach related to hardware security. Other Duties : Fulfill other duties as assigned, consistent with the faculty member’s expertise and departmental needs. Faculty members are expected to uphold the highest professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements An earned doctorate in cybersecurity, computer science, computer engineering, electrical engineering, or a closely related field with an emphasis on hardware security. Candidates must have completed all requirements for the Ph.D. by May 2027. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed by the end of June 2027. Demonstrated potential for effective teaching in hardware security and closely related areas. Demonstrated potential for productive research and scholarly activity in hardware security, as evidenced by a record of peer-reviewed publications and a strong potential for future research productivity. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Potential to obtain external research funding, or evidence of previous success in securing grants, contracts, or industry-supported research funding. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners in an academic environment. Ability to develop collaborations as part of a multidisciplinary research teams. Excellent written and oral communication skills, and the ability to work effectively with colleagues and students. The candidate should be able to collaborate in a collegial academic environment and adapt to the interdisciplinary and applied learning focus of Wichita State. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching or assisting with undergraduate or graduate courses in hardware security or closely related areas. Experience mentoring students, supervising research projects, or supporting student applied-learning experiences. Experience collaborating across disciplines or with industry, government, community, or critical infrastructure partners. Additional Information: Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. 1. Cover Letter: Describing qualifications and alignment with the position. 2. Teaching Statement (maximum 2 pages): Describing teaching interests, experience, and potential cybersecurity or computing courses the candidate could teach or develop. 3. Research Statement (maximum 2 pages): Describing current research accomplishments, future research plans, potential funding directions, and opportunities for student involvement. Priority deadline for applications is December 1, 2026. The appointment date for the position is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 58db4f0a Last Name (required) 7d590d0d Email (required) 006153de Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 5f611cad Last Name (required) 3fa173e9 Email (required) 12a3e33c Job Alert a9a3035a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 6412d625 Last Name (required) 9a741a1e Email (required) 7d50b420 Send This Job To: 7737203e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 5b182cee Last Name (required) ee7e28eb Email (required) 3c64d6d5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/international-student-advisor-wichita-kansas-united-states-ecb82c01-3a45-4389-ac57-efebdb9a0f2c": {
      "title": "International Student Advisor",
      "description": "International Student Advisor - Wichita, Kansas, United States International Student Advisor - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode International Student Advisor Strategic Enrollment Mgmt | Academic/Student Support, Staff International Student Advisor 499602 Academic/Student Support Staff Department: Office of International Education Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary set $19.06/hr Work Schedule: Monday through Friday 8am to 5pm;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story Wanting to spread your wings not only with what you know but also who you know? Let me offer up this opportunity to perform both all rolled into one. Supporting our international students new to the country or even those who’ve been here staying up to date with laws, regulations & all requirements for them to continue. You need to be eager to learn much of the position through your love of the written word. Being able to understand regulations & laws that are not in plain language will give you a leg up also. Understanding the confines to provide clarity and direction where solutions may be unclear, understanding the grey areas within while knowing how to navigate. Being culturally aware & keeping that at the forefront of your meetings will help you be successful. You can meet people from a far land with this position in more ways than one, so apply to start that cultural and educational trip! Job Summary Provides advising and information to international students and the community regarding F-1 immigration regulations and University policies and resources. Serves as the Designated School Official (DSO) in the updating of the Student and Exchange Visitor Information System (SEVIS) database in compliance with Department of Homeland Security (DHS) regulations. Essential Functions Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) and ensures compliance with Department of Homeland Security (DHS) rules and regulations. Advises students on federal, state and local requirements to maintain their status in the United States. Works with SEVIS and internal database to issue I-20s, process registrations, address updates, and student requests for employment. Monitors SEVIS alerts and communicates with students as needed. Coordinate with academic advisors to ensure international student enrollment and academic progress is in compliance with immigration regulations. Serve as a representative, advocate, and/or spokesperson for international students in dealing with other campus departments and community members. Job Duties This role provides a mixture of student advising, paperwork including follow-up as well as compliance checkpoints. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in student services or related field Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: - Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills - Ability to explain complex policies, procedures, and academic requirements in clear, student-friendly language - Ability to work effectively with students from diverse backgrounds and experiences. - Ability to adapt to changing institutional and governmental priorities, policies, procedures, and technology - Ability to work independently with minimal supervision, take initiative, exercise sound judgment, and effectively prioritize and manage responsibilities - Ability to make sound, independent decisions when policies or guidance do not clearly address a situation -Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive -Demonstrates cross-cultural sensitivity. -Requires a U.S. citizen or permanent resident as require by law for this position. Additional Information: Applicants must meet the requirement of being a \"U. S. Citizen\" or a Lawful Permanent Residence because the position requires access to the Student and Exchange Visitor Information System (SEVIS), a federal government database. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 1720f704 Last Name (required) 35a3a10e Email (required) 4c9b0af2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9f02aac9 Last Name (required) 5f266ca2 Email (required) acedb213 Job Alert 2d6f14b0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Staff Academic/Student Support Staff Department(s) Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This J