    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-industrial-engineering-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Industrial Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Industrial Engineering - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor - Industrial Engineering - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Industrial Engineering College of Engineering | Faculty Assistant Professor - Industrial Engineering 499421 On Site Faculty Department: Industrial, Systems, and Manufacturing Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range $95,000 to $110,000/yr, commensurate with qualifications Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Industrial, Systems, and Manufacturing Engineering in the College of Engineering at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Industrial Engineering. We seek an innovative scholar and educator who will contribute to our academic programs and research profile. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a productive research program, and provide service to the university and profession. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. Since 1928, Wichita State's College of Engineering has built a reputation for equipping engineering and computing students with the most complete education possible. From hands-on research using the latest technologies to our location in Kansas' center of industry — with virtually unlimited jobs, applied learning and professional connections — Shocker engineering students have everything they need to make their dream careers a reality. The Department of Industrial, Systems, and Manufacturing Engineering comprises 11 faculty, five degree programs (two bachelor’s, two master’s, and one PhD program), and six graduate certificate programs. The department is commi