    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/senior-educator-in-economics-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Educator in Economics",
      "description": "Senior Educator in Economics - Wichita, Kansas, United States Senior Educator in Economics - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Senior Educator in Economics Barton School of Business | Faculty Senior Educator in Economics 499588 On Site Faculty WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Department: Barton School of Business Department of Marketing & Economics & Marketing Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary is set at $80,940/yr Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and service commitments;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Economics in the W. Frank Barton School of Business invites applications for a Senior Educator position in Economics to begin in the fall of 2027. Candidates will teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional delivery formats, including traditional face-to-face, hybrid, blended, and fully online instruction. The position will foster applied learning in course design and engage with industry and the local business community through applied projects. The successful candidate will also advance knowledge through scholarly activities, including active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiatives, and outreach activities. We are looking for an instructor who can teach undergraduate- and graduate-level courses such as Behavioral Economics. They will establish clear learning objectives, develop curriculum and instructional materials that accomplish those objectives, and provide students with the support needed to succeed. Wichita State University places applied learning at the center of student experience. Every degree program at Wichita State includes a guaranteed applied learning or research experience, providing students with opportunities to develop relevant professional skills and meaningful experience before graduation. The successful candidate will have opportunities to integrate these experiences into economics education through applied projects with industry and engagement with local businesses and the larger community. The department provides undergraduate and graduate economics education and creates opportunities for teaching, applied learning, interdisciplinary collaboration, and engagement with industry and the broader community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties The successful candidate will be expected to: 1. Teaching: Teach four courses in the fall semester and four courses in the spring semester. Each course is three credit hours, with 2.5 hours of class time per week. Classes will be taught at the undergraduate and graduate levels using face-to-face and other instructional modalities, including online and blended formats. 2. Course Design and Student Support: Establish key objectives for classes; create curriculum that accomplishes the established objectives; develop syllabi that outline the topics to be explored and list due dates for assignments and examinations; give lectures and organize activities to present material and deepen understanding of coursework; and answer students’ questions and provide support to help them succeed. 3. Applied Learning and Community Engagement: Engage with local businesses and the larger community to provide applied-learning opportunities for students through industry- and community-based projects. 4. Service and Scholarly Activities: Engage in service activities at the department, Barton School of Business, university, profession, and local community levels. Scholarly activities may include active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiatives, and outreach activities. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree or Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements A graduate-level degree or higher in Economics or closely related field, at the time of application. For degrees in a related field, direct experience within the field of economics. Teaching experience at any level. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Evidence of technical and soft skills Knowledge of Behavioral Economics, statistics, and principles of microeconomics and macroeconomics. Ability to build professional relationships within the community and across the university at all levels. Ability to provide instruction of curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments. Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. REQUIRED MATERIALS 1. Cover Letter/Letter of application addressing how the candidate’s qualifications and experience align with the position. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach/philosophy and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) cf484d83 Last Name (required) 1977d01c Email (required) 3f7b676f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 440797eb Last Name (required) 71cf1010 Email (required) 744ebd86 Job Alert b1ac70aa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) d4ba342f Last Name (required) 165e2a3f Email (required) a04bdb29 Send This Job To: 26af1cf2 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 37c728ef Last Name (required) 153da69b Email (required) df81e2a2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
