    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-economics-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Economics - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Economics - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Economics Barton School of Business | Faculty Assistant Professor of Economics 499585 On Site Faculty Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. Department: Barton School of Business - Department of Marketing & Economics Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary set at $109,535/yr Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Candidates will have an exciting opportunity to contribute to the future of economics education and research at Wichita State University. The position will play an important role in strengthening undergraduate and graduate economics education, producing academic research that advances knowledge, and contributing to innovative academic and applied-learning initiatives that connect economics with industry and the broader community. Wichita State University is classified as a high research activity institution and provides faculty with opportunities and institutional support for research, interdisciplinary collaboration, external funding, and industry-engaged scholarship. The Department of Economics in the W. Frank Barton School of Business at Wichita State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Economics, beginning Fall 2027. You will teach undergraduate and graduate courses, establish clear learning objectives, develop curriculum and instructional materials that accomplish those objectives, and provide students with the support needed to succeed. We welcome candidates who can contribute expertise in economics and statistics and build productive professional relationships within the community and across the university. Wichita State University places applied learning at the center of student experience. Every degree program at Wichita State includes a guaranteed applied learning or research experience, providing students with opportunities to develop relevant professional skills and meaningful experience before graduation. The successful candidate will have opportunities to integrate these experiences into economics education through applied projects with industry, case studies, research, and engagement with local businesses and the larger community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties The successful candidate will be expected to: 1. Teaching: Teach two courses per semester (four courses per academic year) at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with courses offered in face-to-face, hybrid, blended, and fully online formats. Each course is three credit hours. Teaching assignments may include, depending on the candidate's expertise and program needs, Principles of Microeconomics, Labor Economics, Business Statistics, and related courses with the opportunity to develop courses in the candidate's area of expertise. The successful candidate will establish key objectives for classes, develop curriculum and syllabi, present course material through lectures and learning activities, and answer students' questions and provide support to help them succeed. 2. Applied Learning and Community Engagement: Foster applied learning in course design by developing meaningful opportunities for students to engage with industry, local businesses, and the larger community through applied projects, case studies, professional engagement, and other experiential learning activities. 3. Research: Develop and maintain an active and sustainable program of academic research consistent with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) expectations and the requirements for tenure and promotion at the Barton School of Business. The successful candidate will be expected to publish high-quality scholarly research in respected and leading economics or related academic journals and advance knowledge through sustained scholarly activity. 4. Service and Engagement: Contribute meaningful service to the department, Barton School of Business, university, profession, and local community. Service may include active involvement in committees, student mentorship, student recruitment and retention initiatives, professional organizations, outreach activities, and other activities that advance the mission of the department and school. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements A Ph.D. in Economics from an accredited institution. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies (ABD) will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed prior to the June 2027. Evidence of an established record of scholarly research or a strong research pipeline with demonstrated ability or potential to publish in high-quality economics or related academic journals. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, effective teaching in economics at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Evidence may include teaching evaluations, curriculum or course development, applied-learning activities, experience with face-to-face, hybrid, blended, or fully online instruction, or other indicators of teaching effectiveness. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of economics and statistics. Ability to build professional relationships within the community and across the university at all levels. Ability to provide instruction of curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments. Preferred Qualifications: Research and/or teaching interests in labor economics and/or environmental economics. Use of empirical methods, econometric techniques, or data-intensive approaches to address applied economic questions. Additional Information: Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. REQUIRED MATERIALS 1. Cover Letter/Letter of application addressing how the candidate’s qualifications and experience align with the position. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach/philosophy and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). 3. Research Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing research approach/philosophy and experience. A priority deadline for application review is October 31, 2026. The appointment for the position is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) d220ba3c Last Name (required) 502f09d4 Email (required) 0e614edc Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9c6cb0c9 Last Name (required) 54e19049 Email (required) 5e76298c Job Alert 7b922d27 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 91ba6981 Last Name (required) 3bc44428 Email (required) b571b0ef Send This Job To: 23725adb Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) b683d356 Last Name (required) 0aa4b98c Email (required) 5282c101 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
