    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-criminal-justice-corrections-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections 499464 On Site Faculty Department: School of Criminal Justice Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $65,000 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, may vary depending on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The School of Criminal Justice (SCJ) at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position starting on August 2, 2027 in Criminal Justice with the ability to teach and conduct research in the area of Corrections. We seek a dynamic and innovative scholar committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The successful candidate will contribute to our undergraduate and graduate programs, engage in impactful research, and participate in departmental, college, and university committees. The salary for this 9-month position will be $65,000. As one of the oldest criminal justice programs in the United States, our school offers bachelor's and master's degrees in Criminal Justice, a fully online bachelor's degree in Homeland Security, a bachelor's degree in Forensic Science, and master’s degrees in Forensic Biology and Forensic Firearms. Due to the school's strong partnership with local and state agencies, faculty have abundant research opportunities. The SCJ is housed in the Law Enforcement Training Center on WSU’s Innovation Campus – a partnership building shared with the Wichita Police Department and the Sedgwick County Sheriff’s Office. The SCJ has close partnerships with the Midwest Criminal Justice Institute and with the US Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms, and Explosives (ATF), which has two buildings on the Innovation Campus housing the Crime Gun Intelligence Center of Excellence, the NIBIN National Correlation and Training Center II, and the ATF Wichita Field Office. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in criminal justice, including corrections. The standard teaching load for research-active faculty is three classes per semester. Develop and maintain an active research agenda that leads to refereed publications. Seek external funding for research projects, individually or collaboratively, with faculty or local/state agencies. Mentor and advise students. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities. Engage with the community and contribute to public scholarship. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD or other terminal degree in criminal justice, sociology, criminology, or other related field completed prior to August 2027. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching in multiple modalities (e.g., online, hybrid, in-person) Demonstrated potential for publishing in peer-reviewed journals. Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and students from diverse backgrounds. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1) A cover letter 2) Current CV which clearly outlines practical experience in corrections 3) A statement of teaching philosophy For full consideration, completed applications should be submitted by November 2, 2026. For additional information, please contact david.eichhorn@wichita.edu. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 83374da0 Last Name (required) 3a3513ff Email (required) 3a8069c7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4116e3b1 Last Name (required) 00afc203 Email (required) aff6f3f8 Job Alert aba2f680 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 6be14268 Last Name (required) 9be1de7e Email (required) 252a97f3 Send This Job To: 3bfc99ec Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) e2e8c101 Last Name (required) 3e6be4a8 Email (required) d0cc92ea Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency