    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/financial-specialist-senior-wichita-kansas-united-states-7e8b7329-b728-4757-b2ae-cff9ac747bb2": {
      "title": "Financial Specialist, Senior",
      "description": "Financial Specialist, Senior - Wichita, Kansas, United States Financial Specialist, Senior - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Financial Specialist, Senior College of Health Professions | Staff Financial Specialist, Senior 499639 Staff Department: CHP Dean's Office Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $19.10 per hour and can be adjusted based on experience Work Schedule: M-F 8-5 Occasional weekends to attend university functions;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The College of Health Profession is looking for a team player to join our finance team. As a Financial Specialist, Senior, you will play a key role in supporting and tracking departmental finances, analyze and manage financial data, as well as identifying financial discrepancies. You will work closely with college leadership as you navigate budget and scholarship processes. Job Summary Completes complex financial transactions, which includes, but is not limited to, accounts receivable and/or payable, procurement card and transactional reconciliation, travel authorizations and reimbursements, endowment accounts, state appropriations and earned income, and grant funding using established processes, procedures and systems. Essential Functions Reviews, processes and audits complex transactions, compiles financial reports and reconciles accounts. Maintains accurate records, ensuring that invoices are paid and payments are received in a timely manner, as appropriate. Generates financial reports and audits and resolves financial discrepancies. Responds to inquiries related to account status, charges and discrepancies. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Four (4) years of experience in accounting, finance or related field. Every 30 hours of college coursework can be substituted for two (2) years of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to extract, analyze, and transmit complex information from varied sources Ability to compute, verify and compare figures and detect discrepancies in information or records High level of experience in Microsoft Office Ability to work within a fast-paced work environment Ability to work under broad guidelines with limited instructions, determine and organize steps required to accomplish tasks with the ability to reorganize tasks as necessary to meet deadlines Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Sedentary: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involves remaining stationary most of the time. Apply Now First Name (required) f027432c Last Name (required) c854cd28 Email (required) 78102bec Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 8b65e063 Last Name (required) d2081828 Email (required) 6c94e4da Job Alert 16cf4544 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staf