      "title": "Student Assistant GEEK's Front Desk - Work Study 0350W",
      "description": "Student Assistant GEEK's Front Desk - Work Study 0350W - Wichita, Kansas, United States Student Assistant GEEK's Front Desk - Work Study 0350W - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Student Assistant GEEK's Front Desk - Work Study 0350W College of Engineering | Student Student Assistant GEEK's Front Desk - Work Study 0350W 499752 Student Department College of Eng. ESSC Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 12/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. TBD with supervisor. Dependent upon course schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Serve as the first point of contact for the GEEKs Tutoring Center by providing outstanding customer service to students, faculty, and visitors while supporting the daily operations of the center. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Welcome students and visitors to the tutoring center. • Check students in and out for tutoring appointments. • Answer questions regarding tutoring services and center operations. • Maintain accurate records and assist with daily administrative tasks. • Monitor the tutoring space and communicate operational concerns to professional staff. • Assist with opening and closing procedures as assigned. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements MUST BE WORK-STUDY ELIGIBLE. • Must be enrolled as a Wichita State University student. • Excellent customer service and communication skills. • Strong attention to detail. • Ability to maintain confidentiality. • Dependable with consistent attendance. • Ability to work independently after training. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications • Currently a College of Engineering student. • Previous customer service or office experience. • Experience using Microsoft Office and basic computer applications. • Strong organizational and multitasking skills. • Familiarity with Wichita State resources is preferred. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 9d5f24ba Last Name (required) 404d93be Email (required) 9f11b1f8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) e0def598 Last Name (required) fb3e1e22 Email (required) a91ade96 Job Alert c3be7ed6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Shar