    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/student-assistant-geek-s-tutor-work-study-0350w-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Assistant GEEK's Tutor - Work Study 0350W",
      "description": "Student Assistant GEEK's Tutor - Work Study 0350W - Wichita, Kansas, United States Student Assistant GEEK's Tutor - Work Study 0350W - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Student Assistant GEEK's Tutor - Work Study 0350W College of Engineering | Student Student Assistant GEEK's Tutor - Work Study 0350W 499751 Student Department College of Eng. ESSC Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 15/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. TBD with supervisor. Dependent upon course schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Join the GEEKs Tutoring Center as a peer tutor and help College of Engineering students achieve academic success. Tutors provide course-specific academic support while creating a welcoming and collaborative learning environment that promotes student persistence, confidence, and engagement. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Provide one-on-one and small-group tutoring for College of Engineering courses. • Assist students in developing effective study strategies and problem-solving skills. • Maintain accurate tutoring records and complete required documentation. • Foster a welcoming, inclusive, and professional learning environment. • Collaborate with GEEKs staff and participate in required training and meetings. • Refer students to additional campus resources when appropriate. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements MUST BE WORK-STUDY ELIGIBLE. • Must be enrolled as a Wichita State University and College of Engineering student. • Must have successfully completed the courses they will tutor with strong academic performance. • Maintain good academic standing. • Demonstrate strong communication and interpersonal skills. • Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism. • Ability to work scheduled shifts throughout the semester. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications • Previous tutoring, mentoring, teaching assistant, or peer leadership experience. • Strong organizational and time management skills. • Demonstrated commitment to helping fellow students succeed. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 10e051ff Last Name (required) baf82ef9 Email (required) dfbd22bb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 8623cadf Last Name (required) 14696712 Email (required) 3675e109 Job Alert 4f214c42 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State Un