    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-educator-assistant-teaching-professor-of-physics-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics",
      "description": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics 499451 On Site Faculty Department: Physics Division of Mathematics, Statistics and Physics Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $55,000 to a maximum of $60,000 Work Schedule: M-F hours depend on class schedule;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story ​The Physics division in the Fairmount College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS) of Wichita State University (WSU) invites applications for a full-time 9-month non-tenure-track assistant educator/assistant teaching professor of physics starting on August 2, 2027. The successful candidate will employ a variety of strategies to foster student learning including encouraging active learning, promoting an inclusive classroom environment, maintaining proper course-related records, and promptly providing students with feedback as to their progress toward meeting the course objectives. Teaching responsibilities will primarily include face-to-face instruction during the day or evening. A full-time teaching load consists of 12 credit hours per term, which typically corresponds to 3 courses or lecture sections. The Physics division at Wichita State University (WSU) is an exciting, collaborative place to work where opportunities exist with department colleagues and other colleagues from across campus. The department offers B.A. & B.S. degrees in Physics and a growing graduate program, including both M.S. and Ph.D. degrees. Recognizing the value of hands-on training opportunities, the department also supports undergraduate research projects where students gain valuable experience. While non-tenure-track, this position offers a clear path to a long-term career through WSU’s established faculty promotion system, providing opportunities for rank advancement within the track. The department currently has nine tenured or tenure-track faculty, two teaching faculty, one postdoctoral research associate, 25 graduate students, and ~50 undergraduate physics majors. The faculty-led research focuses on two main themes: condensed matter physics and the physics of the universe, including high energy physics and astrophysics. Wichita State University (WSU) is a public research university in Wichita, Kansas, United States. It is one of the fastest-growing research universities in the country, with $411 million in research grants and contracts. Wichita State University is the major urban research and innovation university in Kansas with an enrollment of 17,548 students. The university offers more than 60 undergraduate degree programs in more than 200 areas of study in nine colleges. The university's graduate school offers more than 50 master's degrees in more than 100 areas, a specialist in education degree, and 13 doctoral degrees. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate level, including introductory algebra- and calculus-based physics classes. This responsibility includes designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, hybrid & online), and assessing student learning. While the focus is on teaching the large lecture-based introductory physics courses, opportunities may occur to teach upper division physics courses such as modern physics, thermal physics, E&M, etc. Service: A part of the workload is dedicated to service tasks to the Department, College, or University. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department. The faculty member may also engage in service to the academic community (such as reviewing paper manuscripts or grant proposals). Research/scholarly activities: Research activities are not required as part of the workload expectations for this position; however, continued scholarly activity and professional development, including pursuing research involving undergraduate students, are encouraged. Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member's talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree and Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Master's degree in Physics or closely related area for Assistant Educator or Doctorate degree in Physics or closely related area for Assistant Teaching Professor. Experience teaching physics at the college level Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to effectively teach undergraduate physics courses, including lecture and laboratory courses Ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, engaging, and dynamic environment comprised of individuals with a range of backgrounds, skills, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate degree in Physics or closely related area. At least two years of college-level physics teaching experience. Preferred License/Certifications/Training: No licensure required. Professional development or training in college teaching, instructional technology, laboratory safety, or evidence-based teaching practices is preferred. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter: A letter of application addressing how the candidate's qualifications and experience align with the position, including a summary of teaching philosophy and relevant scholarly interests. 2. Complete Curriculum vitae 3. Teaching statement: Statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) describing their conceptualizations of teaching and learning, teaching and assessment methods, and how their teaching practices will engage students from a range of backgrounds and experiences. Timeline Review of applications will begin on 15-Nov-2026 and continue until the position is filled. For best consideration, please submit all materials by 1-Nov-2026. The start date for this appointment is August 2, 2027. For any inquiries about the position, please contact Dr. Foudil Latioui at foudil.latioui@wichita.edu WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: No additional physical requirements Apply Now First Name (required) 5c73e7af Last Name (required) 43f40a8a Email (required) 5cd90661 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9725a63b Last Name (required) dbfeedb5 Email (required) bd3b0c04 Job Alert 458e609c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) b4a3b007 Last Name (required) 2a26a899 Email (required) 6aad6130 Send This Job To: 0210312a Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) c9628a78 Last Name (required) e2cbf229 Email (required) 066e5ed2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
