    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-integrated-marketing-communication-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication 499428 On Site Faculty Department: Elliott School of Communication Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000 - $75,000 Work Schedule: Schedule may vary depending on course offerings; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Elliott School of Communication at Wichita State University seeks a full-time, 9-month, tenure-eligible assistant professor in the Integrated Marketing Communications area, the largest concentration in the school. We are looking for collegial candidates with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and service for an appointment beginning August 2, 2027, with a salary range of $70,000 to $75,000 (maximum). Specifically, we seek scholars who bring special expertise in Integrated Marketing Communications (Public Relations and Advertising). The successful candidate will have opportunities to teach in both the graduate and undergraduate program depending on needs of the school, including courses in a new professionally oriented graduate degree in communication that complements our traditional MA academic track. IMC courses may include media analytics, strategy, social media, account management, measurement and evaluation techniques, and skills classes. Graduate courses may include quantitative research methods, communication theory, and IMC graduate seminars. Candidates will be expected to develop a productive research program and provide service to the university and the profession. Wichita State University is located in the heart of the largest media market in the state. We are committed to applied learning, which is supported by the broad network of alumni and other supporters working in the metro area. The Elliott School of Communication includes 10 full-time faculty, 12 GTAs, and two administrative staff. We are an integrated communication program, offering a common core of classes before students choose from three emphasis areas: integrated marketing communication, journalism and media production, and comm studies. Additionally, the ESC includes The Research Partnership, a full-service marketing research agency that contracts for a wide range of services including focus groups, phone, mail and online surveys, one-on-one interviews, and mystery shops for local and national government agencies, nonprofits, and large and small businesses. ESC faculty are encouraged to take advantage of our research facilities and participate, as desired, in our ongoing projects. Tenure track faculty members typically teach 6 courses per academic year. Tenure track faculty are expected to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online) and to incorporate applied learning into the course design, whenever possible. The successful candidate will establish and maintain a sustainable research program in the communication disciple that results in peer-reviewed scholarly publications. Tenure track faculty are expected to contribute service to the department, college, university, and the profession. The workload for this position is 60% teaching, 30% research, and 10% service. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiatives, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching : Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in IMC. This includes designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, online, or hybrid), and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising research projects or theses as appropriate, and incorporate applied learning opportunities (e.g. projects with industry or community partners) into the coursework whenever possible. Research/Scholarly Activity : Establish and maintain an active research program in communication. This includes publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated by a record of research accomplishments that follow the departmental tenure and promotion guidelines. Service : Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession (e.g. reviewing for journals, involvement in academic societies). Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD in Communication must completed prior to August 2027. Teaching experience at the collegiate level. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated potential to establish an independent and productive research program. Demonstrated ability or potential to work collaboratively and collegially with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: A record of scholarly productivity appropriate to career stage. Experience teaching qualitative methods and/or media analytics. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter of interest 2. Curriculum Vitae Review of candidates will begin on November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. If you have questions, please contact search chair and ESC director Dr. Lisa Parcell at lisa.parcell@wichita.edu. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) f8d037ae Last Name (required) 5a7061eb Email (required) 8ab02c61 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 0895f23b Last Name (required) 3a5df8fa Email (required) 6b0d15c5 Job Alert 87c638e4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 1dbd1fb7 Last Name (required) 62b50cfb Email (required) 4089160b Send This Job To: eb8e7687 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Ta