    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-educator-assistant-clinical-professor-and-director-of-transition-to-teaching-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching",
      "description": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching College of Education | Faculty Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching 499442 On Site Faculty Department: School of Teaching and Learning Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $80,000 Work Schedule: 8am to 5pm, Monday – Friday, with some flexibility for evenings and weekends as needed. Course offerings include Saturdays. Work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The School of Teaching and Learning in the College of Education at Wichita State University invites applications for a 12-month full-time assistant clinical professor of education and director of the Transition to Teaching program. We seek an expert in areas related to, but not limited to, alternative teacher education, preparing individuals who are changing careers to become teachers, and middle and high school teacher education. We are looking for a collaborative colleague to lead our alternative certification program in the School of Teaching and Learning and join an engaged and collaborative faculty at Kansas’s only urban public research university. The academic appointment for this position will be effective June 7, 2027. As a faculty member in the School of Teaching and Learning, the successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate level classes in the fall, spring, and summer as part of our alternative teacher preparation program. The new faculty member will also work with various populations of students, colleagues, and community, engage in grant seeking activities, and provide service to the program, department, college, university, and profession. About the University and the School of Teaching and Learning Wichita State University is located in the heart of the Midwest in the largest city in Kansas. Our beautiful 330-acre campus recently experienced rapid expansion, with renovation projects and new housing and campus life initiatives. Our enrollment of roughly 17,000 ranges from traditional undergraduate and graduate students to professionals adding new skills or changing fields. We have online programs and thriving campus life/residential students. The School of Teaching and Learning at Wichita State provides high-quality teacher training in early childhood, elementary, and middle/secondary fields. Over 90% of our students receive teaching contracts upon graduation and we are the major source of teachers in the Wichita metropolitan area. Within T2T, students complete their applied learning experiences in the classroom while maintaining employment as teachers of record while throughout their time in the program. Our faculty publish at the regional, national, and international level, present at major conferences in our respective fields, and serve on accreditation boards and professional committees. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties This position will lead the Transition to Teaching program in the School of Teaching and Learning. Faculty members share responsibility for programmatic and instructional decisions within and across program options. The position is a 12-month appointment and carries a 4:4 load for fall/spring semesters, with an additional 6 credit hours of teaching in the summer semester. The director receives a 1-credit release each semester as part of administrative duties for leading the program. The Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor position include 80% teaching of undergraduate and graduate level courses as assigned, with a focus on content specific pedagogy, research, capstone, and internship or field experience courses. This also includes mentoring and supervising T2T teachers in both years of the program and coordinating school placements. The faculty member will provide service to departmental, college, university, professional and community constituting 20% of this role. Primarily the service role will include the Director of the Transition to Teaching program: developing and maintaining relationships with local school districts and agencies; attend relevant meetings, maintaining student data, leading the program annual report, contributing to accreditation and university reports, and directing recruitment and retention for T2T program. The faculty member may collaborate with colleagues to seek grants related to alternative certification programs. This position requires regular on-campus presence at Wichita State University. The selected candidate must reside in Kansas within a reasonable commuting distance of the WSU main campus. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree or Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements A Masters or Ed.D or Ph.D. in Education, in teacher preparation or related field, completed prior to start date. Experience in K-12 teaching Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Evidence of potential for excellence in teaching. Willingness to employ various strategies in instructional delivery and learning activities, flexible teaching methods, and applied learning approaches. Evidence of communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with diverse students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and professionals. Ability to work supportively with returning adult college students/career professionals. Ability to develop relationships with community partners to enhance supervision and coordination of school placements. Preferred Qualifications: Earned Ed.D or Ph.D. in Teacher Preparation-Secondary Education or related field. Three years’ professional-level 6-12 teaching experience. Previous university level teaching experience, including online teaching Evidence of working with adult college students. Experience mentoring pre-service or in-service teachers. Experience in university level course development and implementation. Evidence of leadership in education. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter including teaching statement 2. Curriculum Vitae Review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 61b7c64e Last Name (required) 5aa796da Email (required) 0f830eed Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6c8984a3 Last Name (required) 182ce57d Email (required) 746b890f Job Alert 6e35241d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Education College of Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) e89ef6cf Last Name (required) a01d518e Email (required) 654c0e43 Send This Job To: f4602c09 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 2189fcd6 Last Name (required) 46dccec9 Email (required) e174b68e Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-biomedical-sciences-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences 499491 On Site Faculty Department: Department of Biological Sciences Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000 Work Schedule: M-F 8-5; Variable dependent on schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Position Overview: The Department of Biological Sciences in the Fairmount College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Biomedical Sciences. We seek applicants with teaching and research expertise in the fields of Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a productive research program, and provide service to the university and profession. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of August 2, 2027. Department Description: The Department of Biological Sciences offers majors in Biology with either an Ecological/Environmental/Organismal or a Biomedical emphasis. There are approximately 340 undergraduate majors and the department’s Master of Science in Biology program currently includes 19 graduate students. There are 11 faculty members and seven full-time departmental support staff/administrators. The department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and student success. The department is an affiliate of the Kansas Idea Network of Biomedical Research Excellence (K-INBRE). It houses modern laboratory space that includes analytical/molecular and cell culture equipment, microscopy and protein chemistry core facilities, an accredited animal facility, and access to the Kansas State University and Wichita State University High Performance Computing clusters. Core Responsibilities Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in the candidate’s area of expertise. This includes designing curriculum, delivering high-quality instruction, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising undergraduate and M.S. research projects. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active, externally funded research program in Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology involving undergraduate students and M.S. graduate students. This includes publishing peer reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession. Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member’s talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in the candidate’s area of expertise. This includes designing curriculum, delivering high-quality instruction, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising undergraduate and M.S. research projects. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active, externally funded research program in Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology involving undergraduate students and M.S. graduate students. This includes publishing peer reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD in Biology or related field and must be completed prior to August 2027. Teaching experience is broadly defined i.e. teaching assistantships, mentoring, participation in course lectures, etc. Please clarify in your teaching statement. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate classes in area of expertise. Effective written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated potential to establish an independent and productive research program. Demonstrated ability or potential to work effectively in collaborative environments and engage constructively with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral research experience is preferred, but strong candidates lacking postdoctoral experience will be considered. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1) Letter of application 2) Current curriculum vita 3) Statement of teaching philosophy and goals 4) Statement of research interests and goals 5) Copies of unofficial academic transcripts Applicants must apply by October 19, 2026 for full consideration. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) f25d2e17 Last Name (required) 04104d76 Email (required) 75da5081 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 58674121 Last Name (required) fdebfb1c Email (required) d55419e5 Job Alert c349629e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 646acd49 Last Name (required) b5181c75 Email (required) 2dc0643d Send This Job To: 257b2e86 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) bbb656a9 Last Name (required) c16ed256 Email (required) b70bda7a Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submit