    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-in-teacher-apprentice-program-ee-ecu-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU College of Education | Faculty Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU 499440 On Site Faculty Department: Teacher Apprenticeship Pathways, Literacy, & Special Education Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $65,000 Work Schedule: Typically, 8am-5pm, with some flexibility for evenings as needed ; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The College of Education at Wichita State University seeks a dynamic and experienced colleague to enhance our Teacher Apprentice Program (TAP) Team. Housed in the Department of Teacher Apprentice Pathways, Literacy and Special Education, the Assistant Professor in TAP is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track faculty position with a focus on teaching a variety of undergraduate courses related to specific content areas and foundational teacher preparation courses, mentoring TAP students and providing leadership to faculty and adjunct instructors, research, and service. Applicants must be committed to fostering an inviting environment and promoting the success of our students. The academic appointment for this position will be effective August 2, 2027. Serving over 700 students, TAP prepares students to complete their Bachelor of Arts in Early Childhood Unified/Elementary Education without leaving their current Para Educator job, earning field experience for work as a Para Educator. Courses are 100% online with some in-person options for general education course requirements. An inverted curriculum provides students opportunities to take education courses in their first semester in the program, increasing their skills as a para while working towards licensure as a Kansas teacher. Dedicated mentors provide guidance and support to students throughout their time in the program. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties The Assistant Professor in TAP EE/ECU will design and lead multi-disciplinary teaching initiatives including the redesign and continuous updating of content specific pedagogy courses as well as foundational education courses within TAP, to align with state and national accreditation, as well as program and student needs. Teaching will be informed by research and service in the field of alternative certification as well as content area and content specific pedagogical strategies. The Assistant Professor role will include 40% teaching in TAP EE/ECU will teach 9 credit hours in each fall and 9 credit hours in each spring semester, with a focus on core content specific pedagogy courses, exceptionality courses, core content concepts courses, foundational education courses, and/or internship or field experience courses. This also includes mentoring TAP students in their applied learning experiences throughout the program. Research and scholarship activities for the Assistant Professor in TAP EE/ECU will include 40% of the role, encompassing original research and program evaluation support. Specific research interest areas of candidates should include content specific pedagogies, alternative certification teacher pathways, student centeredness, and innovative teacher preparation programming. The faculty member would be expected to seek external funding grant opportunities for research and/or student supports and assist with current ongoing funded initiatives. The Assistant Professor in TAP EE/ECU will be expected to represent WSU by producing original works, both publications and presentations. Service ranging from program to national/international representation will be expected for 20% of the role of the Assistant Professor in TAP EE/ECU. Service to the program, department, college and university in the form of serving on and chairing committees of interest will be expected. Service to the program will include serving on the TAP Leadership Team, collaborating with faculty, supporting mentors and adjuncts instructors, and guiding program initiatives. Service to the field and profession, in the form of community, state-level, and national/international-level organization membership and engagement will be expected. This position requires regular on-campus presence at Wichita State University. The selected candidate must reside in Kansas within a reasonable commuting distance of the WSU main campus. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Early Childhood, Elementary, Special Education, or related field, completed prior to August 2027. Experience in K-12 teaching Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Willingness to accommodate a variety of learning styles and strategies in instructional delivery and learning activities, including online and blended learning, flexible teaching methods, and applied learning approaches. Ability to use various forms of technology to communicate with students, faculty, and other stakeholders in and outside of the university in 1:1, small group, and large group settings for varied purposes. Knowledge of and ability to describe practical implications of current trends, research, and education within the teacher preparation field. Familiarity with national and state standards and their implications to classroom instruction, teacher preparation, and curriculum design. Ability to design learning experiences and assessments that model best practices in education and are inclusive of special education students. Ability to make data-driven decisions that demonstrate continuous improvement in several settings (i.e. online instruction, K-12 curriculum design, teacher preparation program). Ability to learn program parameters and apply them to individual student programs of study and accreditation standards. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with all students and colleagues. Commitment to fostering an environment in which all students, faculty, staff, and community partners feel welcome, valued, supported, and engaged. Preferred Qualifications: Experience mentoring pre-service or in-service teachers Experience in online course development and implementation Elementary Teaching Experience Demonstrated experience and capability in conducting and disseminating scholarly research Preferred License/Certifications/Training: Elementary (PK-6) Teaching License Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Teaching Statement 4. Research Statement Review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 4aba480d Last Name (required) 49a058ab Email (required) 5821486f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 812acadd Last Name (required) 55e7959f Email (required) 142f0086 Job Alert b2a829e3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Education College of Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 29776a87 Last Name (required) 3f9836e7 Email (required) 711bdecc Send This Job To: 10693f66 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) f4049d54 Last Name (required) c24e5090 Email (required) c64f2319 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these