    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-cad-cam-hamr-operations-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant 499744 Student Department NIAR CAD/CAM Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 18 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Flexible with class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story NIAR’s Hub for Advanced Manufacturing and Research (HAMR) is seeking a student with strong communication, organization, and customer service skills to support facility operations. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties This role focuses on ensuring a smooth day-to-day experience for building occupants and visitors by checking and stocking amenities (e.g., coffee and soda supplies), assisting with events and tour scheduling and preparation, and supporting package/mail tracking and occupant notifications. Depending on building needs, the student may assist other staff, help coordinate activities for visitors and partners, and provide support throughout the HAMR facility. The position may also assist with general coordination tasks across HAMR and provide support for special events as needed. This position is ideal for students interested in gaining hands-on operations and customer service experience in a dynamic research environment. Under supervision, students will: • Support daily facility operations, including opening/closing procedures, cleanliness checks, and readiness of common areas. • Check, stock, and track amenities (coffee, soda, snacks, paper goods), monitor inventory levels, and coordinate reorders with staff. • Assist with scheduling and preparing for events and tours, including room reservations, A/V checks, signage, seating layouts, and setup/teardown. • Assist visitors and tour groups, manage check-ins, and provide wayfinding support. • Track incoming packages/mail and promptly notify building occupants; maintain logs and coordinate internal deliveries as directed. • Maintain shared calendars and documentation, including event schedules, inventory records, and standard operating procedures. • Support special events at HAMR with onsite logistics and customer service. • Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements • Strong communication and customer service skills. • Excellent organization, attention to detail, and reliability. • Experience with event setup or facilities support (preferred but not required). • Comfort with inventory management and basic tracking tools (e.g., Excel, SharePoint). • Basic knowledge of A/V equipment setup. • Ability to work collaboratively, take initiative, and meet deadlines. Additional Information Ability to lift and carry up to 25 lbs. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Students must have their own transportation, as some local travel between facilities may be required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) cd83a8e1 Last Name (required) f978e531 Email (required) d16492b9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) c1828898 Last Name (required) 03d38d91 Email (required) e758d3da Job Alert 9c51adb8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 912daaf4 Last Name (required) ea69c169 Email (required) 5ba2233f Send This Job To: d8659169 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 7b79c8ce Last Name (required) 4710d3b7 Email (required) 29d7b3ec Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
