    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-9-month-counseling-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling",
      "description": "Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling College of Education | Faculty Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling 499410 On Site Faculty Department: Counseling, Educational Leadership, Educational and School Psychology (CLES) Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $65,000 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday - afternoon and evening classes; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Counseling, Educational Leadership, Educational and School Psychology (CLES) Department in the College of Education at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Counseling beginning August 2, 2027. We seek a counselor educator who is committed to excellence in graduate teaching, clinical supervision, scholarship, student mentorship, and service. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth of the Counseling Program through high-quality instruction, supervision of counseling students, an active program of research, and engagement with professional and community partners. The successful candidate will teach graduate courses in counseling in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. Teaching responsibilities may include counseling core courses, clinical skills courses, practicum, internship, supervision, research methods, statistics, program evaluation, assessment, dissertation preparation, or other courses aligned with the candidate’s expertise and departmental needs. Candidates with expertise in research methodology, quantitative methods, qualitative methods, mixed methods, statistics, program evaluation, counselor education research, or related areas that support graduate and doctoral education are especially encouraged to apply. This position also includes supervising graduate students in clinical training experiences, advising master’s and doctoral students, maintaining a productive scholarly agenda, contributing to accreditation and assessment activities, and providing service to the department, college, university, profession, and community. The Counseling, Educational Leadership, Educational and School Psychology (CLES) Department prepares highly skilled, scholarly, and socially responsible professionals who serve individuals, families, schools, organizations, and communities through counseling, leadership, education, research, and service. The department offers a range of graduate programs, including the Master of Education in Counseling, Master of Education in Educational Leadership, Doctor of Education in Educational Leadership, Master of Education in Educational Psychology, Ph.D. in Education and Behavioral Studies with tracks in Educational Psychology and Clinical Mental Health Counselor Education and Supervision, and Educational Specialist in School Psychology. The Counseling Program includes CACREP-accredited master’s programs in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and School Counseling, as well as a doctoral track in Clinical Mental Health Counselor Education and Supervision. The program is also connected to the WISE Counseling Clinic, which provides supervised clinical training for graduate counseling students while offering accessible counseling services to the community. Faculty in the CLES Department work in a collaborative academic environment that values strong teaching, applied learning, clinical training, research productivity, student mentorship, interdisciplinary collaboration, and service to the profession and community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Core Responsibilities may include: Teaching - Teach graduate courses in the Counseling Program in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. - Teach courses across the counseling curriculum, which may include counseling theories, counseling techniques, group counseling, career counseling, diagnosis, assessment, practicum, internship, supervision, research methods, statistics, program evaluation, dissertation preparation, or other courses based on program needs and faculty expertise. - Contribute to doctoral-level instruction, including research-related coursework and dissertation preparation, as appropriate. - Develop and deliver effective instructional materials, learning activities, and assessments. - Support applied learning experiences that prepare students for professional counseling practice, supervision, leadership, and scholarship. - Advise and mentor graduate students in academic, professional, clinical, and scholarly development. Clinical Supervision and Professional Preparation - Supervise graduate students in practicum and internship experiences, including placements in the WISE Counseling Clinic and community settings. - Support students’ development of counseling skills, ethical decision-making, professional identity, and readiness for practice. - Develop, foster, and maintain relationships with community agencies, schools, clinical sites, and other professional partners to support student placements, referrals, and applied learning opportunities. - Contribute to the ongoing development and quality improvement of clinical training processes. Research and Scholarly Activity - Develop and maintain an active program of scholarly research consistent with expectations for tenure-track faculty. - Publish peer-reviewed scholarship and present research at professional conferences. - Pursue internal and external funding opportunities, as appropriate. - Mentor graduate students in research, scholarly writing, conference presentations, and dissertation development. - Contribute research expertise that strengthens the department’s master’s and doctoral programs. - Support departmental research capacity in areas such as counseling outcomes, counselor education, supervision, research methodology, statistics, program evaluation, assessment, or related areas. Service - Provide service to the Counseling Program, CLES Department, College, University, profession, and community. - Participate in program governance, curriculum development, recruitment, assessment, and accreditation-related activities. - Contribute to CACREP accreditation maintenance and continuous program improvement. - Engage with professional counseling organizations and related scholarly communities. - Support the department’s mission through collaboration, collegiality, and professional leadership. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Earned Doctorate or ABD from a CACREP-accredited university in counseling, and/or counselor education ( all requirements for the doctorate must be completed prior to August 2, 2027 ). Professional identity as a Counselor Educator as evidenced by affiliations with either/or the American Counseling Association (ACA), American School Counseling Association (ASCA), American Mental Health. Counselor Association (AMHCA), or the Association for Counselor Education & Supervision (ACES). LPC Licensure-eligible in the State of Kansas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Potential for establishing a record of publication and scholarship. Commitment to fostering an environment in which all students, faculty, staff, and community partners feel welcome, valued, supported, and engaged. Knowledge of CACREP standards. Willingness to accommodate a variety of learning styles and strategies in instructional delivery and learning activities, including online and blended learning, flexible teaching methods, and applied learning approaches. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with a broad pool students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and professionals Preferred Qualifications: Experience as a licensed professional counselor or clinical mental health counselor. Evidence of successful teaching experience in a CACREP-accredited program and experience in supervising counseling practicum and internship students. Expertise in one or more research areas such as quantitative, qualitative, mixed methods. Experience teaching research methods, statistics, program evaluation, assessment, dissertation preparation, or related graduate-level research courses. Additional Information: To apply, please complete the faculty profile which includes the names and contact information for three (3) professional references and be prepared to upload the following: 1. Cover Letter addressing how your qualifications and experience align with the position 2. Teaching Philosophy Statement 3. Research Philosophy Statement 4. Counseling Philosophy Statement Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position has been filled. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 017e8a37 Last Name (required) 4ef022e2 Email (required) 8339390c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) defb75d4 Last Name (required) 77c5db5c Email (required) 72ed9697 Job Alert d0ee493e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Education College of Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 68e25ea1 Last Name (required) 47b64ae4 Email (required) d5f94ce2 Send This Job To: c47d7c73 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. 