    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-accounting-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Accounting - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Accounting - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Accounting Barton School of Business | Faculty Assistant Professor of Accounting 499619 On Site Faculty Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. Department: School of Accountancy Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary set at $170,000/yr Work Schedule: Dependent on class and research schedule;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The candidate will have an exciting opportunity to help shape the future of accounting education and research at Wichita State University. The position will play an important role in advancing the School of Accountancy, strengthening partnerships with the accounting profession and broader business community, and contributing to the development of innovative academic and applied-learning initiatives that respond to the evolving needs of the accounting profession. The Barton School of Business is accredited through AACSB International in both business and accounting. Fewer than 1% of business schools worldwide hold this double accreditation. The School of Accountancy in the W. Frank Barton School of Business at Wichita State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Accounting, beginning August 8, 2027. Candidates will contribute to our growing undergraduate and Master of Accountancy (MAcc) programs that prepare students for successful careers in public accounting, industry, government, and nonprofit organizations. The candidate will join a collaborative academic environment committed to excellence in teaching, impactful scholarship, student success, and meaningful engagement with employers and the accounting profession. The School of Accountancy has strong relationships in the community, creating dynamic relationships for research, students and so much more. Barton School of Business at Wichita State University places applied learning at the center of student experience. Every degree program at Wichita State includes a guaranteed applied learning or research experience, providing students with opportunities to develop relevant professional skills and meaningful experience before graduation. The successful candidate will have opportunities to integrate these experiences into accounting education through industry-engaged projects, experiential learning, research, internships, and partnerships with the regional business and accounting community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties A candidate is expected to: 1. Teaching : Teach two courses per semester (four courses per academic year) in the School of Accountancy at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with courses offered in in-person, hybrid, and online formats. Teaching assignments will be based on the candidate's expertise and program needs and may include courses across a broad range of accounting disciplines. The successful candidate will also contribute to curriculum development, assessment, continuous improvement, and the advising and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students. 2. Research : Develop and maintain an active and sustainable research program consistent with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) expectations and the requirements for tenure and promotion at the Barton School of Business. The successful candidate will be expected to produce high-quality scholarly research with the potential for publication in respected and leading journals in accounting or closely related fields and to disseminate research through appropriate academic and professional venues. Collaborate with faculty colleagues, students, and external partners on scholarly initiatives when appropriate. 3. Applied Learning and Professional Engagement : Incorporate applied and experiential learning into course design and develop meaningful opportunities for students to engage with the accounting profession and broader business community through applied projects, case studies, employer engagement, internships, professional organizations, and other experiential learning activities. 4. Service and Engagement : Contribute meaningful service to the School of Accountancy, Barton School of Business, university, profession, and broader community. Service may include participation in committees, accreditation and curriculum assessment, student mentoring, student recruitment and retention initiatives, professional organizations, employer partnerships, advisory activities, community outreach, and other activities that advance the mission of the School and Barton School. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Earned a doctorate (Ph.D., D.B.A., or equivalent terminal degree) in Accounting or a closely related field. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies (ABD) will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed prior to August 2027. Evidence of an established record of scholarly research or a strong research pipeline with demonstrated potential for sustained publication in high-quality accounting or related academic journals consistent with the expectations of an AACSB-accredited institution. Evidence of effective teaching in accounting or related areas at the university level. Evidence may include teaching evaluations, course development, applied-learning activities, instructional technologies or software, experience with multiple instructional delivery formats, or other indicators of teaching effectiveness. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments, with students, faculty and community patners. Demonstrated ability to mentor students and contribute to student success. Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to student success and inclusive excellence in the field. Preferred Qualifications: Professional certification, such as a CPA, and/or significant professional accounting experience. Doctoral degree completed or in progress at an AACSB-accredited institution. Experience incorporating emerging technologies, analytics, artificial intelligence, or related innovations into accounting education or research. Pursue externally funded or industry-supported research. Experience with applied learning, interdisciplinary collaboration, or meaningful engagement with the accounting profession. Additional Information: W ork Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. REQUIRED MATERIALS 1. Cover Letter/Letter of application addressing how the candidate’s qualifications and experience align with the position. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach/philosophy and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). 3. Research Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing research approach/philosophy and experience. A priority deadline for application review is October 31, 2026. The appointment for the position is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 492f960c Last Name (required) 132c477c Email (required) 53a97e16 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6cf0bc34 Last Name (required) 9d5216dd Email (required) 2f4b2ee3 Job Alert 4ab3b922 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 2d9a8b5a Last Name (required) 9226527a Email (required) 3bc36e22 Send This Job To: 9b034907 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 574a8211 Last Name (required) c82dd8b4 Email (required) 02bea637 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/manager-student-legal-services-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Manager, Student Legal Services",
      "description": "Manager, Student Legal Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States Manager, Student Legal Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Manager, Student Legal Services Student Affairs (College) | Staff Manager, Student Legal Services 499559 Staff Department: Student Legal Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range beginning at $108,200/yr, adjusted based on qualifications Work Schedule: Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm. Some weekends and evenings will be required to support events.;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Are you a legal professional seeking a meaningful leadership role that supports a healthy work-life balance? Would you be interested in a position that allows you to have a direct impact on student success? If so, Wichita State University is seeking a dynamic and experienced legal professional to serve as the inaugural Manager of Student Legal Services! This leadership role provides direct legal services to students and support of the strategic oversight of the newly established program. This position is ideal for a licensed attorney with courtroom experience, a strong public service orientation, and the ability to lead a small team in a dynamic, student-centered environment. The successful candidate will have strong communication, leadership, and program development skills. Job Summary Manage, coordinate, and administer the day-to-day activities of student legal services programs and services. Oversee the implementation and evaluation of student legal services, ensuring alignment with University goals and initiatives and compliance with applicable rules and regulations. Essential Functions • Provide legal consultations, advocacy, and full legal representation to eligible students on a variety of criminal and civil matters; including performing conflict of interest checks related to representation. • Design and conduct student education, training and outreach initiatives in alignment with programming goals and objectives. • Establish sustainable processes, key performance metrics, management tools and reporting capabilities. Utilize data to develop new or revise current programs and services. Communicate quality and progress metrics to department, staff, and/or stakeholders. • Cultivate new and expand existing strategic partnerships and lead initiatives to support program success. Consult with stakeholders to assess needs and ensure effective support. • Oversee program budget according to needs. Monitor and adjust plans as resource requirements change. • Supervise assigned staff; including performance management, work allocation, training, promotion and enforcement of internal procedures and controls, and problem resolution. Evaluate performance and make recommendations for staff actions. Required Education and Experience: Juris Doctorate degree from an American Bar Association (ABA) accredited institution and admission to the Kansas State Bar Four (4) years of experience as a practicing attorney, with one (1) year in a leadership role. Required License/Certifications/Training: Licensed to practice law in the state of Kansas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Public speaking Legal writing and research Strong Interpersonal skills Document management Presentation Skills Regulatory compliance Report writing Risk Management Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Frequent 60-90% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Sedentary: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involves remaining stationary most of the time. Apply Now First Name (required) 87da2607 Last Name (required) 29401f69 Email (required) 488601c8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) be31dee4 Last Name (required) 73395f69 Email (required) 6a7feefc Job Alert d050dd7a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Student Affairs (College) Student Affairs (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 748a9ab1 Last Name (required) 2f5e440f Email (required) ab024e3a Send This Job To: d096ae64 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at an