    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-real-estate-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Real Estate",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Real Estate - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Real Estate - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Real Estate Barton School of Business | Faculty Assistant Professor of Real Estate 499587 On Site Faculty Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. Department: Barton School of Business Department of Finance, Real Estate, and Decision Sciences Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary is set at $140,000/yr Work Schedule: Based on course demands; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Candidates will have an exciting opportunity to help shape the future of real estate education and research at Wichita State University. The position will play an important role in advancing the Real Estate program, strengthening partnerships with the real estate industry, and contributing to the development of innovative academic and applied-learning initiatives that respond to the evolving needs of the commercial and residential real estate sectors. The Department of Finance, Real Estate, and Decision Sciences in the W. Frank Barton School of Business invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Real Estate, beginning August of 2027. Successful candidates will also play an important role in the academic leadership and continued development of the Real Estate program, with the opportunity to assume formal program leadership responsibilities accompanied by an additional stipend. The candidate will be actively engaged with the Center for Real Estate and its research, educational, and industry partnership activities. As the candidate develops in the role, and depending on qualifications and mutual interest, there may also be an opportunity to serve as Director of the Center for Real Estate. Wichita State University places applied learning at the center of student experience. Every degree program at Wichita State includes a guaranteed applied learning or research experience, providing students with opportunities to develop relevant professional skills and meaningful experience before graduation. The successful candidate will have opportunities to integrate these experiences into real estate education through industry-engaged projects, experiential learning, research, and partnerships with the regional business and real estate community. The Barton School is housed in Wayne and Kay Woolsey Hall, a state-of-the-art, 125,000-square-foot facility located on Wichita State University's Innovation Campus. The Innovation Campus creates a distinctive environment where students, faculty, and industry interact in close proximity. Major organizations with a presence on or adjacent to the Innovation Campus include Airbus, Deloitte's Smart Factory, NetApp, Spirit AeroSystems, Textron Aviation, and other industry partners. Wichita State University is classified as a high research activity institution and provides faculty with opportunities and institutional support for research, interdisciplinary collaboration, external funding, and industry-engaged scholarship. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties The successful candidate will be expected to: 1. Teaching : Teach two courses per semester (four courses per academic year) in the Real Estate program at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with courses offered in both in-person and online formats. Teaching assignments may include, depending on the candidate's expertise and program needs, Principles of Real Estate, Real Estate Finance, Real Estate Valuation and Appraisal, Real Estate Law, Property Management, Real Estate Investment Analysis, Urban Land Development, and other related courses. 2. Applied Learning and Industry Engagement : Incorporate applied and experiential learning into course design and develop meaningful opportunities for students to engage with the real estate industry and broader business community through applied projects, case studies, professional engagement, and other experiential learning activities. 3. Research : Develop and maintain an active and sustainable research program consistent with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) expectations and the requirements for tenure and promotion at the Barton School of Business. The successful candidate will be expected to produce high-quality scholarly research with the potential for publication in respected and leading journals in real estate, finance, economics, or closely related fields. 4. Service and Engagement : Contribute meaningful service to the department, Barton School of Business, university, profession, and broader community. Service may include participation in committees, student mentoring, student recruitment and retention initiatives, professional organizations, industry engagement, outreach activities, and other activities that advance the mission of the department and school. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements A Ph.D. in Real Estate Finance, Economics or a closely related field from an accredited institution, with demonstrated teaching and/or research expertise in real estate. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies (ABD) will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed by the end of May 2027. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Potential to pursue externally funded or industry-supported research. Ability and interest in developing productive partnerships with the real estate and broader business community. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments. Strong written, interpersonal, and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree completed or in progress at an AACSB-accredited institution. Relevant professional or industry experience in real estate or a closely related field. Experience incorporating applied or experiential learning into teaching. Research expertise directly related to real estate and its application to industry, communities, or public policy. Evidence of an established record of scholarly research or a strong research pipeline with demonstrated potential for publication in high-quality real estate, finance, economics, or related academic journals. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, effective teaching in real estate or related areas. Evidence may include teaching evaluations, course development, applied-learning activities, instructional technologies or software, experience with multiple instructional delivery formats, or other indicators of teaching effectiveness. Additional Information: Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. REQUIRED MATERIALS 1. Cover Letter/Letter of application addressing how the candidate’s qualifications and experience align with the position. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach/philosophy and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). 3. Research Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing research approach/philosophy and experience. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 106b518a Last Name (required) 72465144 Email (required) bb091222 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 34e55ff3 Last Name (required) 23a2df31 Email (required) 128e0759 Job Alert 10b982a5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) aef9f63a Last Name (required) 19cfc495 Email (required) f8cf2c12 Send This Job To: 5d7cc791 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 39727f2f Last Name (required) d03f0442 Email (required) 170f3786 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
