    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/nbe-student-assistant-work-study-0350w-wichita-kansas-united-states-09875358-ded2-45fe-a303-43e34870356e": {
      "title": "NBE Student Assistant - Work Study 0350W",
      "description": "NBE Student Assistant - Work Study 0350W - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Student Assistant - Work Study 0350W - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Student Assistant - Work Study 0350W Strategic Enrollment Mgmt | Student NBE Student Assistant - Work Study 0350W 499735 Student Department Rhatigan Student Center Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 12/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Up to 20 hours per week Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Looking for a fun, fast-paced campus job? Join the team at Shocker Sports Grill & Lanes in the Rhatigan Student Center! As a Guest Server, you'll help create a welcoming and enjoyable experience for WSU students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Looking for a fast-paced job where no two days are the same? Shocker Sports Grill & Lanes is looking for energetic, customer-focused team members to help create a great experience for our guests. As a Guest Server, you'll be one of the first faces guests see when they visit. You'll help provide outstanding service, maintain a welcoming atmosphere, and support daily operations in a fun and active entertainment environment. The position involves direct interaction with guests, cashiering, stocking supplies, maintaining cleanliness, and helping ensure every guest has an enjoyable experience. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Must be able to provide friendly, professional customer service while interacting with a diverse group of guests. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and remain calm under pressure. Must be dependable, punctual, and able to work scheduled shifts. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and special events as needed. Must be able to stand and walk for extended periods of time. Ability to lift, carry, and stock supplies weighing up to 25 pounds. Ability to follow established cash handling, food safety, and operational procedures. Must work well both independently and as part of a team. Strong communication, problem-solving, and decision-making skills are required. Commitment to maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for guests. Based on the position description, the role requires excellent verbal communication, teamwork, independent work, sound judgment, and a strong customer service focus. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Previous customer service, hospitality, restaurant, retail, or recreation experience. Experience handling cash transactions and operating a point-of-sale (POS) system. Ability to provide exceptional guest service in a fast-paced environment. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Experience working as part of a team while maintaining individual responsibilities. Demonstrated ability to anticipate guest needs and resolve concerns professionally. Ability to multitask and prioritize responsibilities in a busy setting. Flexible availability, including evenings, weekends, and special events. Interest in hospitality, customer service, food service, recreation, or event operations. Additional Information Shocker Sports Grill & Lanes is committed to creating a fun, welcoming, and customer-focused environment for both guests and employees. This position offers an opportunity to gain valuable experience in hospitality, customer service, cash handling, and team collaboration while working in one of Wichita State University's premier entertainment venues. Successful candidates will be enthusiastic, dependable, and committed to providing exceptional service to every guest. The position requires direct interaction with guests and supporting daily operations in a fast-paced environment. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 9d96e08d Last Name (required) 1a7f66bc Email (required) 84161d7f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 23d72fe2 Last Name (required) bd1e8d4c Email (required) 044e3702 Job Alert 287f4e41 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ecd480c5 Last Name (required) 1e5b63ee Email (required) 9bbd92e0 Send This Job To: 353ccffa Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) cb995330 Last Name (required) d3de148d Email (required) 6c9cda42 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is 