    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/temp-mentor-gear-up-heights-southeast-wichita-kansas-united-states-ca667165-f0ee-486f-a4f7-e8c0a487cb80": {
      "title": "Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast",
      "description": "Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast - Wichita, Kansas, United States Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast Strategic Engagement & Planning | Temporary Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast 499721 Temporary Department College Access Mentor/Tutor GEAR UP Heights & Southeast Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $20/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Mon-Fri, hours vary between 8:00am-5:00pm (regular evenings & weekends based on scheduled events but flexible) Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Wichita GEAR UP Heights and Southeast program serving students in grades 6-12 and first year in college. This is NOT a remote position - check the job location before applying! Job Summary Job Duties Works with students at Curtis, Coleman and Stucky Middle Schools and feeding into Heights and Southeast High School to provide college going services. Monitors and tracks student academic progress, graduation, enrollment in college and FAFSA completion. Provides grant related activities such as workshops and college campus visits, academic advising, career exploration and job search, mentoring, tutoring resources, and summer programs. Required Education This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Additional Requirements Associate's degree in Education, Counseling, Social Services or related field (minimum 60 credit hours completed). 6 months experience working with students in grades 6-12. Valid Driver's license required. Must be able to escort students on campus visits - which may include lots of walking. May be asked to make community and school presentations. Overnight travel to training and conferences may be required. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Education, Counseling, Social Services or related field Additional Information 10 hours per week (20 per pay period). Candidate will set office hours with supervisor. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) a99bbec4 Last Name (required) 1e53d63f Email (required) 86111ea9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6efafddb Last Name (required) 2548e3e7 Email (required) 273d7366 Job Alert 87591e7c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 344c3ef6 Last Name (required) 4393ebac Email (required) f29aa310 Send This Job To: ba3