      "title": "College Access Mentor Data Entry - Pittsburg",
      "description": "College Access Mentor Data Entry - Pittsburg - Wichita, Kansas, United States College Access Mentor Data Entry - Pittsburg - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode College Access Mentor Data Entry - Pittsburg Strategic Engagement & Planning | Temporary College Access Mentor Data Entry - Pittsburg 499699 Temporary Department Kansas Kids @ GEAR UP Campus Location Pittsburg, KS Hire Type Part Time Pay $20/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Mon-Fri, 8:00am-5:00pm (some evenings or weekends as necessary) Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Kansas Kids @ GEAR UP is a state-wide program serving students in foster care, grades 7-12 and first year in college. This is NOT a remote position - Pittsburg is the job location, if you live in or around the Pittsburg area apply now! Job Duties Enters transcripts, program activities and any documentation to the Kansas Kids @ GEAR UP database. Monitors and tracks student academic progress, graduation, enrollment in college and FAFSA completion. Assists students with KKGU dual credit application, DCF tuition waiver application and credit recovery, if needed. This position may be asked to help with program activities. Required Education This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Additional Requirements Valid Driver's license needed. This position requires you to drive to different schools to pick up transcripts or grade cards. You may also be asked to help transport students. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications Completion of 60 credit hours of college coursework At least one year experience working in an office setting Additional Information 20 hours per week (40 per pay period). Candidate will set office hours with supervisor. Must be able to complete a State of Kansas Child Abuse and Neglect background check. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 55d497bd Last Name (required) 7285a21e Email (required) 9e8b7ae8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b8e271ff Last Name (required) 37b289c7 Email (required) 6f7dc75f Job Alert 981ba26f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) e4b6c9d0 Last Name (required) 882f31f5 Email (required) 5990f4e7 Send This Job To: 4f3c50f8 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) b98550bc Last Name (required) 853829dd Email (required) 44364769 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a c