    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-composites-fabrication-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR Composites Fabrication Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR Composites Fabrication Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Composites Fabrication Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Composites Fabrication Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR Composites Fabrication Student Assistant 499199 Student Department NIAR Composites & Structures Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $19 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person”. Job Story The Composites Lab at Wichita State University is looking for a Student assistant to join our Composite Fabrication team. This position provides hands-on experience in manufacturing advanced composite structures used in aerospace research and development. The ideal candidate enjoys working with their hands, following detailed processes, and contributing to a collaborative research environment. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Assist with composite material preparation, cutting, and layup. • Fabricate composite panels, coupons, molds, and research components following engineering specifications. • Perform precise hand layup while following instructions. • Perform vacuum bagging and prepare parts for autoclave and oven curing. • De-mold cured laminates without damaging them. • Follow laboratory procedures and accurately document manufacturing activities. • Maintain a clean, organized, and safe laboratory environment Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications • Operation of some basic shop hand tools. • Strong attention to detail and ability to follow written work instructions. • Comfortable working in a hands-on manufacturing or laboratory environment. • Excellent verbal and written communication skills. • Experience using MS Office suite. • Self-motivated, self-disciplined, organized, and driven individual. • Able to work with minimal supervision. • Interested in learning about aerospace materials and processes. Additional Information • Lift large tools and boxes in and out of the freezer. (75lbmax) Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) ce57c9d5 Last Name (required) 6088ba6a Email (required) 3c4e25d2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 06326b0d Last Name (required) 5ed77c3b Email (required) 0c2e82ec Job Alert 83180f60 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State Univ