    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/temp-mentor-gear-up-heights-southeast-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast",
      "description": "Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast - Wichita, Kansas, United States Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast Strategic Engagement & Planning | Temporary Temp Mentor Gear UP Heights/ Southeast 499534 Temporary Department College Access Mentor/Tutor GEAR UP Heights & Southeast Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $20/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Mon-Fri, hours vary between 8:00am-5:00pm (regular evenings & weekends based on scheduled events but flexible) Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Wichita GEAR UP Heights and Southeast program serving students in grades 6-12 and first year in college. This is NOT a remote position - check the job location before applying! Job Duties Works with students at Curtis, Coleman and Stucky Middle Schools and feeding into Heights and Southeast High School to provide college going services. Monitors and tracks student academic progress, graduation, enrollment in college and FAFSA completion. Provides grant related activities such as workshops and college campus visits, academic advising, career exploration and job search, mentoring, tutoring resources, and summer programs. Required Education This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Additional Requirements Associate's degree in Education, Counseling, Social Services or related field (minimum 60 credit hours completed). 6 months experience working with students in grades 6-12. Valid Driver's license required. Must be able to escort students on campus visits - which may include lots of walking. May be asked to make community and school presentations. Overnight travel to training and conferences may be required. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Education, Counseling, Social Services or related field Additional Information 10 hours per week (20 per pay period). Candidate will set office hours with supervisor. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 48a14ecf Last Name (required) 6f47f658 Email (required) 94989ac3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 98265848 Last Name (required) a0b66a24 Email (required) 77482af9 Job Alert 44af9089 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ccb4cd61 Last Name (required) f2c58349 Email (required) f6926d38 Send This Job To: 7e397ece Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 124e866e Last Name (required) 5ba9cdc0 Email (required) 375a78c0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookie