      "title": "NBE Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect 0305I",
      "description": "NBE Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect 0305I - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect 0305I - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect 0305I College of Engineering | Student NBE Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect 0305I 499596 Student Department Mechanical Engineering Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 5000./semester Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. TBD with supervisor Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The primary function of a graduate teaching assistant (GTA) is to assist with instruction. GTAs have the latitude to make independent decisions, use judgment and exercise discretion when dealing with student matters. The main purpose and responsibility of GTAs is to impart knowledge or training to students at Wichita State University. Job Summary The primary function of a graduate teaching assistant (GTA) is to assist with instruction. GTAs have the latitude to make independent decisions, use judgment and exercise discretion when dealing with student matters. The main purpose and responsibility of GTAs is to impart knowledge or training to students at Wichita State University. Required Education Bachelor's Degree Required Experience To be eligible for an assistantship, students must be admitted to a degree program in either full or conditional standing. Students admitted on probation or placed on academic probation following admission may be eligible for assistantship awards under certain circumstances. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) a74c4721 Last Name (required) b9e4d724 Email (required) 483