    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-5-axis-cnc-machinist-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR 5-Axis CNC Machinist",
      "description": "NIAR 5-Axis CNC Machinist - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR 5-Axis CNC Machinist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR 5-Axis CNC Machinist NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR 5-Axis CNC Machinist 499480 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR Advanced Material and Prototyping Campus Location: Park City, KS Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 2nd Shift Monday – Friday; occasional weekends may be required as needed. Work is performed onsite and in-person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Information The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) is a fast-growing area within WSU, known globally for our expertise in the most critical areas of aerospace research and development. The Advanced Machining and Prototyping Lab is looking for CNC Machinist with 5-Axis experience to join our team. This position is located at our Park City, KS location. Job Summary Responsibilities include set up and operation of various tools and equipment to create, modify, or repair precision parts. Monitors the machinery and conducts regular quality checks to ensure they are running properly and that the parts are being produced according to specifications. Essential Functions Machines and fabricates components by preparing and operating machines; works from complex drawings, prototype sketches, electronic files and/or verbal instructions. Responsible for production of high precision parts and performs complex setups required to produce parts Troubleshoots issues with equipment, new programs, and/or products; detects equipment malfunctions and maintains machinery to ensure functionality Provides training and oversight of new hires and students Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent by hire date Three (3) years of experience as a CNC Machinist; Every 30 hours of related college coursework and/or technical training can be substituted for one (1) year of experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Experience with 5-Axis machining Demonstrates strong verbal and written communication skills Demonstrates and maintains value-added time management skills Demonstrate good work ethics and lead by example. Attention to detail Ability to meet deadlines Ability to read and follow technical drawings and diagrammed instructions Ability to use precision tools to take accurate measurements Attention to detail and self-motivated Valid Driver’s License is required Physical Requirements: Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Apply Now First Name (required) 227f1fa7 Last Name (required) 7f5feab2 Email (required) ec9c3e9d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4f7b79eb Last Name (required) a894590e Email (required) 37f40687 Job Alert 1d645169 Finalize your job alert by 