    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-atlas-assistant-program-management-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR ATLAS Assistant Program Management",
      "description": "NIAR ATLAS Assistant Program Management - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR ATLAS Assistant Program Management - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR ATLAS Assistant Program Management NIAR Institute | Temporary NIAR ATLAS Assistant Program Management 499584 Temporary Department NIAR ATLAS Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $18 per hour Work Schedule Flexible; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The NIAR ATLAS lab is looking for an assistant for their Program Management position. Job Duties Assist the Program Manager in updating project schedules, tracking milestone completions, and monitoring action items. Organize, archive, and route engineering project data, customer deliverables, and compliance records. Coordinate meeting logistics, prepare agendas, and take highly accurate, technical meeting minutes for client and research review teams. Help compile internal project status metrics, charts, and presentation decks for leadership reviews. Serve as an internal point of contact to follow up with multidisciplinary engineering teams on overdue project inputs. Perform general operational and office administration tasks as assigned to streamline laboratory operations. Additional Requirements High school diploma or equivalent. Basic understanding of project management lifecycle phases or engineering design workflows. Excellent technical written and oral communication skills to interact professionally with cross-functional teams. Strong attention to detail, organization, and a demonstrated ability to execute assigned tasks independently. Ability to work collaboratively within a fast-paced, multidisciplinary research lab environment. Capable of performing standard duties involving standing, walking, and remaining in a stationary position operating office equipment. Preferred Qualifications Experience or familiarity with project tracking software (e.g., Microsoft Project, Jira, Trello, or 3DEXPERIENCE platform). Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Additional Information Work is done on site at the main NIAR building on campus or at Sector A. Physical Requirements Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information Apply Now First Name (required) 9665208e Last Name (required) c0619c83 Email (required) 6a5c8254 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4e8450d4 Last Name (required) d2618d14 Email (required) 12141d73 Job Alert a65f21d5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 4187a4ac Last Name (required) 5148c048 Email (required) 8d76d64d Send This Job To: 597545e4 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information a