      "description": "NIAR ATLAS Graduate Assistant Program Management - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR ATLAS Graduate Assistant Program Management - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR ATLAS Graduate Assistant Program Management NIAR Institute | Student NIAR ATLAS Graduate Assistant Program Management 499583 Student Department NIAR ATLAS Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The NIAR ATLAS lab is looking for a graduate assistant for their Program Management position. Job Summary The primary function of a graduate assistant (GA) is to assist in basic scientific research using laboratory facilities, computer programming or operation, data collection, correlation and preliminary interpretation of data, statistical analysis of data and writing preliminary reports, bibliographical work, or assisting musicians or artists in their creative endeavors. Job Duties Assist the Program Manager in updating project schedules, tracking milestone completions, and monitoring action items. Organize, archive, and route engineering project data, customer deliverables, and compliance records. Coordinate meeting logistics, prepare agendas, and take highly accurate, technical meeting minutes for client and research review teams. Help compile internal project status metrics, charts, and presentation decks for leadership reviews. Serve as an internal point of contact to follow up with multidisciplinary engineering teams on overdue project inputs. Perform general operational and office administration tasks as assigned to streamline laboratory operations. Required Education Bachelor's Degree Additional Requirements Must be currently enrolled in a graduate program at WSU in Industrial Engineering, Aerospace/Mechanical Engineering, Business Administration, Project Managemen