    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/ae-student-assistant-work-study-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "AE Student Assistant - Work Study",
      "description": "AE Student Assistant - Work Study - Wichita, Kansas, United States AE Student Assistant - Work Study - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode AE Student Assistant - Work Study College of Engineering | Student AE Student Assistant - Work Study 499543 Student Department Aerospace Engineering Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 15/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. TBD with supervisor Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The Aerospace Engineering Department is seeking a reliable and professional Work-Study Student Assistant to provide front office support and assist with daily administrative operations. This role serves as a key point of contact for visitors, students, faculty, and staff. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Answer and direct incoming phone calls in a courteous and professional manner • Warmly welcome and assist visitors; check in guests and notify appropriate staff of arrivals • Respond to general inquiries and provide basic information about the college • Sort and distribute incoming mail to faculty and staff • Monitor and restock office supplies as needed • Help maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming office environment • Provide administrative support and assist with special projects as assigned Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements * MUST be enrolled at Wichita state University* • Must be eligible for Federal Work-Study • Minimum GPA of 2.5 • Availability to work 10–30 hours per week between Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM • Strong communication and customer service skills • Dependable, detail-oriented, and able to work both independently and as part of a team • Self-motivated with a strong work ethic and initiative • Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively • Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite; willingness to learn new systems • Prior phone or office experience is helpful; training will be provided Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 25f2a480 Last Name (required) 42d1c239 Email (required) 1b62ba72 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4e03bf3a Last Name (required) 009ff031 Email (required) 023b2ed4 Job Alert bf79f72c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 7b1416ff Last Name (required) 158fe5ec Email (required) 3ce6a1d8 Send This Job To: 984a6949 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 78f89bee Last Name (required) 8b9b0d25 Email (required) c74ec13f Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
