      "title": "NIAR Composites and Structures Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR Composites and Structures Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Composites and Structures Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Composites and Structures Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR Composites and Structures Student Assistant 496720 Student Department NIAR Composites & Structures Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $12 - $16 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person”. Job Story The NIAR Composites & Structures Lab is looking for a student assistant to do a variety of different tasks within their lab. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Main Duties Include, but are not limited to: 1. Perform physical and chemical testing on cured composites, foam, core, film adhesive and metals. 2.Cured physical testing compromise of acid digestion methods, ignition loss methods, tests for core or laminate density and specific gravity which requires handling of acids and other solvents. 3. Operate digester units, program temperature/humidity chambers and furnaces. 4. Accept, scan and handle shipments and packages delivered to NIAR. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements Enrolled in Wichita State University STEM Program Major in Aerospace or Mechanical Engineering is preferred. Must be an undergraduate student with a GPA above 3.0 Strong attention to detail Strong organizational and communication skills Must be proficient in MS 