    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/community-program-coordinator-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Community Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Community Program Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States Community Program Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Community Program Coordinator Strategic Engagement & Planning | Office/Administrative Support, Staff Community Program Coordinator 499108 Office/Administrative Support Staff Department: Public Policy and Management Center Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Begins at $42,608 annually, commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Mon-Fri, 8:00am - 5:00pm; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Are you an organized multitasker who thrives on bringing people, projects, and ideas together? Do you enjoy researching solutions, analyzing information, engaging with community partners, and helping meaningful initiatives move from concept to completion? If so, we want to hear from you. As our newest Community Program Coordinator, you'll play an important role in supporting services and programs delivered to community, governmental, and partner organizations. Working alongside project team members and clients, you'll help coordinate activities, conduct research and analysis, provide technical assistance, and support strategic initiatives that strengthen communities and help organizations achieve their goals. In this role, you'll be the connector who keeps projects moving forward by gathering and analyzing information, developing surveys, supporting financial and operational reviews, coordinating community engagement efforts, and helping prepare work plans, budgets, reports, and meeting materials. You'll work closely with stakeholders to organize project details, communicate progress, and ensure deliverables are completed accurately and on schedule. The Community Program Coordinator plays a vital role in translating information into action. Whether you're conducting program, regulatory, financial, or social media research, supporting strategic planning efforts, or preparing reports and presentations, your work will help clients make informed decisions and create meaningful outcomes for the communities they serve. You'll have opportunities to build relationships with community leaders, organizational partners, and project teams while contributing to projects that make a real impact. From coordinating special projects and analyzing data to supporting facilitation sessions and representing the organization at meetings, your contributions will help ensure successful project delivery and exceptional client service. If you're excited about combining organization, analysis, communication, and community engagement to help great ideas become reality, we'd love to meet you. Apply today and help us make great things happen together. Job Summary Assists in service delivery to community, governmental and/or associated organizations which may include, but is not limited to, training, technical assistance, financial analysis, survey development, strategic planning, and regulatory review. Essential Functions Performs program research, financial analysis, survey development and analysis, regulatory analysis, social media analysis, and other data collection and analysis. Develops and provides training, technical assistance and community engagement to organizations. Prepares, processes and edits financial or operational information, data and documents, including budgets, materials for meetings, special projects and reports. Assists with preparation of work plans, budgets, and reports. May represent organization and present at regional meetings and/or conferences. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree in public administration, finance, environmental or related field One (1) year of experience in research, data collection, analysis and reporting or related field Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent professional communication skills Clear, professional written communication (reports, summaries, etc.) Strong presentation and community outreach skills Project management skills (work planning, tracking deliverables, meeting deadlines) Coordinate multi-stakeholder initiatives, community meetings, workshops, etc. Manage relationships with people (clients, funders, partners, etc.) Navigate complex political and organizational dynamic Adjust quickly to changing project priorities Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) ebc4cacf Last Name (required) 36986f2e Email (required) b6fe234b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ae9a6c41 Last Name (required) 6440364d Email (required) dcdef2bb Job Alert a34ec6fa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Office/Administrative Support Staff Office/Administrative Support Staff Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by repl