    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/nbe-student-assistant-wsu-0350r-wichita-kansas-united-states-3f697328-9a30-4120-aa0f-00875d756814": {
      "title": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R",
      "description": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R College of Engineering | Student NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R 499538 Student Department Industrial, Systems and Manufacturing Engineering Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 Per Hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Office is open 8-5 Monday-Friday. Schedule will depend on student’s class schedule. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Industrial, Systems, and Manufacturing Engineering (ISME) department is seeking reliable and professional Student Assistants to provide front office support and assist with daily administrative operations. This role serves as a key point of contact for visitors, students, faculty, and staff. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Answer and direct incoming phone calls in a courteous and professional manner • Warmly welcome and assist visitors; check-in guests and notify appropriate faculty/staff of arrivals • Respond to general inquiries and provide basic information about the department/programs • Sort and distribute incoming mail to faculty and staff • Monitor and restock office supplies as needed • Help maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming office environment • Monitor and update bulletin boards, digital displays, and informational materials physically available in the office • Provide administrative support and assist with special projects as assigned Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements • Minimum GPA of 2.5 • Availability to work 10-20 hours per week between Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM • Strong communication and customer service skills • Dependable, detail-oriented, and able to work both independently and as part of a team • Self-motivated with a strong work ethic and initiative • Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively • Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite; willingness to learn new systems • Prior phone or office experience is helpful Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Additional Information Selection will be based on schedule availability and the ability to follow instructions. Review of application begins on August 24 and the position is open until filled Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 424c44e0 Last Name (required) 7135f279 Email (required) 76925052 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) a15d8c14 Last Name (required) bf8c02f8 Email (required) 29cea6a2 Job Alert 7fa3c183 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineer