    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/advanced-materials-and-manufacturing-research-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Advanced Materials and Manufacturing Research Assistant",
      "description": "Advanced Materials and Manufacturing Research Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Advanced Materials and Manufacturing Research Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Advanced Materials and Manufacturing Research Assistant NIAR Institute | Temporary Advanced Materials and Manufacturing Research Assistant 496164 Temporary Department NIAR Composites & Structures Lab Campus Location Huntsville, AL Hire Type Part Time Pay $18 - $25 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR-controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Advanced Materials and Manufacturing group at the National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) is seeking an engineering or related‑field student for a year‑round internship located in our downtown Huntsville, Alabama office. This role is designed to support an applied learning atmosphere while the student continues working toward their undergraduate or graduate degree. We are looking for candidates with an interest in metallic and polymer additive manufacturing, high‑temperature composite materials, or software development and databasing. This position supports all aspects of applied research for a variety of government and industry customers. Project work will typically involve the characterization, qualification, and integration of newly emerging materials and manufacturing processes into both current and next‑generation systems. The types of evaluation will involve a wide range of systems such as ground vehicles, aircraft, and missile. Evaluations may also include thermo-structural modeling and studies related to material decomposition in high-temperature environments. This position will be based entirely in Huntsville, AL, and will see you work closely with engineers at NIAR to support our growing government and industry customer base. If you are detail-oriented, enjoy challenging and rewarding work, and like being part of a team, consider applying for this position. Job Duties A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Additional duties and responsibilities will be the investigation of novel materials and analysis techniques with an understanding of the thermo-physical/mechanical properties. Various findings will be documented and reported in a clear and concise manner. Additional Requirements Must be able to work a minimum of 15 hours a week during the school semesters that transition into full-time during the summers. Ability to work well in a team environment and effectively communicate ideas and solutions. Self-motivated and able to work effectively with minimal supervision. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Must be able to work on site in Huntsville, Alabama. Additional Information This position does not allow telework. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) f678622d Last Name (required) 1c1d3a9b Email (required) ed077326 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9dd2a44d Last Name (required) 980de68f Email (required) 6a11ea66 Job Alert 97165b13 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) f6544602 Last Name (required) 2f27fdfa Email (required) 80f5b3b5 Send This Job To: db087691 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 637964f7 Last Name (required) c7ee67ed Email (required) 5e072930 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
