    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/wsu-athletics-general-event-staff-wichita-kansas-united-states-d319d019-3687-4677-877a-65c46fbc1ef6": {
      "title": "WSU Athletics General Event Staff",
      "description": "WSU Athletics General Event Staff - Wichita, Kansas, United States WSU Athletics General Event Staff - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode WSU Athletics General Event Staff Women's Sports/Activities | Temporary WSU Athletics General Event Staff 498520 Temporary Department Wichita State Intercollegiate Athletic Association Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay Pay range $11-13 per hour Work Schedule Ability to work a non-traditional schedule involving many nights, weekends, &/or holidays. Subject to sport(s) home schedule. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Wichita State Intercollegiate Athletic Association, Inc, is searching for professional, service-focused individuals for Event Staff for Charles Koch Arena, Eck Stadium, Wilkins and Cessna Stadium. Event Staff is responsible for crowd management and executing Arena, Stadium and WSU-ICAA event policies and procedures. Positions include but aren't limited to ticket taker, security, and parking staff. We deliver memorable experiences that connect all to Shocker Nation Through a Shared Sense of Pride & Passion., Job Summary Job Duties Collects and verifies tickets from event attendees. Greets patrons and assists them in finding their seats. Assists guests with locating exits and amenities such as restrooms and concession areas. Assists guests with limited mobility or other special needs to and from their seats. Ensures that aisles, walkways, and designated seating areas are clear, clean, and safe. Calmly assists with disputes regarding tickets and seats. Notifies supervisor of any problems with facilities, supplies, and venue. Assists guests with complaints or concerns; escalates concerns to supervisor when necessary. Performs other related duties as assigned. Required Education Additional Requirements Requires prolonged standing, sitting, walking and stair climbing to access full range of facility. Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed. Required Experience Preferred Qualifications Previous experience preferred. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, both written and verbal. Able to work effectively both independently and on a team. Strong problem-solving skills and able to make decisions in a fast-paced environment. Exemplify a strong commitment and willingness to provide outstanding customer service. Additional Information Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position and/or traverse campus buildings, including stairs. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) dda9cb3b Last Name (required) bc71c9f2 Email (required) c8708ea0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 33148cdb Last Name (required) 9b94e33e Email (required) 102cfa2d Job Alert 7838e28a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) Women's Sports/Activities Women's Sports/Activities Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscri