    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/nbe-student-assistant-wsu-0350r-wichita-kansas-united-states-95875e3d-945b-46da-b3ac-d9e2232ea467": {
      "title": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R",
      "description": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R 499483 Student Department Community Engagement Institute Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Downtown Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15.00 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Varies with school schedule / 10 hours a week Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The ideal candidate is a creative and motivated student with an interest in branding, social media, graphic design, and strategic communication. They should have some experience creating engaging digital content and an interest in learning how to develop cohesive communication campaigns from idea to execution. We’re looking for a student who brings fresh ideas, stays curious about current communication and social media trends, and is excited to apply what they are learning in a real-world setting. Most importantly, the ideal candidate will bring curiosity, initiative, creativity, a willingness to learn, and a passion for using communication to make a meaningful impact. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Social Media Support: Assist in creating content to increase our presence on platforms such as Facebook, LinkedIn, and X (Twitter). • External Communications: Collaborate on messaging, design, and strategies that raise the visibility of our organization’s work through newsletters, blogs, media outreach, and digital storytelling. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements • Strong written and verbal communication skills • Experience or interest in social media management, digital marketing, or communications • Ability to work independently and collaborate across teams • Creativity and an eye for compelling, broad storytelling • Familiarity with platforms like Adobe and/or Canva, and social media scheduling tools Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Additional Information Benefits of the Internship • Real-world experience in nonprofit and community communications • Opportunities to network and collaborate across multiple teams • Mentorship and guidance from communication professionals • A chance to make a tangible impact on the visibility of community-centered work Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 107ebc03 Last Name (required) 10793df2 Email (required) 59442744 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 81797f8e Last Name (required) 7a2234be Email (required) 97abfd6c Job Alert eb34e638 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Engage