    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/applied-learning-college-access-coach-wichita-kansas-united-states-df8af578-f74f-4e5a-8f15-b1de43c4ab84": {
      "title": "Applied Learning College Access Coach",
      "description": "Applied Learning College Access Coach - Wichita, Kansas, United States Applied Learning College Access Coach - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Applied Learning College Access Coach Strategic Enrollment | Student Applied Learning College Access Coach 499302 Student Department Undergraduate Admissions Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15.00/Hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Varied dependent upon student's class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story This position will work with various college and career centers at local high schools to assist students with the college search process. The goal of the coach position is to help high school students feel informed about their future decisions, wherever that next step might be. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Carry out administrative and technical tasks related to college readiness. Conduct office hours at local high schools to assist students on their college search. Gain knowledge related to college readiness, topics such as applications, scholarships, FAFSA, and additional opportunities available in higher education. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Student must be a domestic undergrad studying at least one of the following eligible programs: Psychology, Social Work, Organizational Leadership, Communication (various emphases considered), or Education (various emphases considered). Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifica