    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/emergent-leadership-student-assistant-applied-learning-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Emergent Leadership Student Assistant - Applied Learning",
      "description": "Emergent Leadership Student Assistant - Applied Learning - Wichita, Kansas, United States Emergent Leadership Student Assistant - Applied Learning - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Emergent Leadership Student Assistant - Applied Learning Academic Affairs Departments | Student Emergent Leadership Student Assistant - Applied Learning 499274 Student Department WSU at McConnell Campus Campus Location Wichita, KS-WSU McConnell Hire Type Part Time Pay Set pay is $12/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Mon & Wed or Tue & Thur, dependent on class schedule. Time will consist of 10 hours per week, split as needed between days. One-time after hours or Saturday event will be worked into schedule as possible. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Looking to strengthen your leadership expertise while in college? We are seeking a Shocker who is interested in developing their skills to emerge as a confident and committed leader through a paid applied learning student position. This opportunity is to help you gain hands-on experience in a challenging, diverse career environment while working in an educational service setting at McConnell Air Force Base. You will assist the Military Education Specialist in connecting, engaging, supporting, and helping military-connected members while further developing and utilizing your leadership skills at the WSU at McConnell Campus. Exemplify leadership through informed, professional, and courteous engagement. Dr. Mark Vermillion, Chair of the Sport & Leadership Studies Department, will ensure that this position provides meaningful, real-world experiences that directly align with your academic preparation and professional goals. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties The Emergent Leadership Student Assistant - Applied Learning position provides practice in developing leadership skills through: • event planning and execution • cross-organizational teamwork • analysis of situations to provide insight • fostering engagement among a diverse population Assistance may include helping with events or projects as required (i.e., identifying, listing, and preparing materials for events, event set-up/tear-down, creating documents/spreadsheets/signage, reviewing books/research/theory/data that could be applied in support of a specific population, etc.) and other duties as assigned. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements U.S. Citizenship and Real ID, no exceptions. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications Working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications is preferred. Additional Information Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 35c24bcc Last Name (required) 9ea76980 Email (required) 60010b13 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6d85bb3f Last Name (required) a4345969 Email (required) 88f34d09 Job Alert 5bd9d78b Finalize your jo