      "title": "Graphic Design Intern for OAL Applied Learning WSU 0350R",
      "description": "Graphic Design Intern for OAL Applied Learning WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States Graphic Design Intern for OAL Applied Learning WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Graphic Design Intern for OAL Applied Learning WSU 0350R Academic Affairs Departments | Student Graphic Design Intern for OAL Applied Learning WSU 0350R 499182 Student Department Online and Adult Learning Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $10.00 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Flexible around class schedule, Mon-Fri. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The applied learning experience will include brand-aligned design, visual storytelling, digital asset creation, and print-ready production. These responsibilities serve as a proving ground where the student applies foundational design principles—layout, typography, color theory, accessibility, and visual hierarchy—while learning to work with real constraints, timelines, and stakeholders. This experience also supports interdisciplinary application by connecting design practice to communication strategy, student engagement, and retention-focused initiatives. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties The internship will provide meaningful, real-world experiences aligned with the student’s academic preparation and professional goals. The intern will contribute to projects that elevate the visibility of student success initiatives at WSU while developing essential skills in visual communication, branding, accessibility-conscious design, and professional collaboration. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements No additional requirements Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications General knowledge of graphic design software Advanced communication skills Additional Information Student must be enrolled in the College of Fine Arts Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 937b8129 Last Name (required) 7ac99159 Email (required) f366eb0d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 675d124b Last Name (required) 42b091ed Email (required) 75a67a2c Job Alert 605177c7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Academic Affairs Departments Academic Affairs Departments Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Some