    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-composites-and-structures-non-destructive-inspection-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR Composites and Structures Non-Destructive Inspection Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR Composites and Structures Non-Destructive Inspection Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Composites and Structures Non-Destructive Inspection Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Composites and Structures Non-Destructive Inspection Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR Composites and Structures Non-Destructive Inspection Student Assistant 499449 Student Department NIAR Composites & Structures Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $16 - 18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The NIAR Composites & Structures lab is looking for a Non Destructive Inspection Student Assistant. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Assist with Non-Destructive Inspection (NDI) laboratory operations. • Prepare, organize, and label test specimens and equipment. • Support ultrasonic and other NDI testing activities under supervision. • Maintain laboratory cleanliness and organization. • Clean and maintain the ultrasonic water tank and surrounding work area. • Assist with equipment setup, calibration, and routine maintenance. • Enter and organize test data, files, and documentation. • Help manage inventory, tools, and laboratory supplies. • Follow all laboratory safety procedures and standard operating instructions. • Perform other laboratory-related tasks as assigned. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements • Enrolled in Wichita State University Engineering Program • Major in Aerospace or Mechanical Engineering is preferred. • Must be an undergraduate student with a GPA above 3.0 Additional Information • Ability to lift and carry materials and equipment up to 50 lbs. • Frequent standing, walking, bending, kneeling, and reaching. • Ability to climb ladders or step stools when required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 449df45d Last Name (required) eb2eebc5 Email (required) 9cdf56f1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 381242e6 Last Name (required) 1149d67b Email (required) efe7ee50 Job Alert 2ec8ca3f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job Wi