    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/integra-technologies-software-engineer-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant",
      "description": "Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant 498164 Student Department Ennovar Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Ennovar is looking for a student assistant software engineer to work at Integra Technologies. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Provide enhancements and bug fixes for OMS and related database interfaces. Includes PL/SQL, Python, Perl, Java, and shell scripts. Support personal computers and related peripherals in a professional manner. Troubleshoot and support network infrastructure; perform upgrades and assist with monitoring for potential issues. Install upgrades and configure network printing, directory structures, rights, security, and software on file servers. Analyze user requirements, procedures, and problems to automate processes and improve existing computer systems. Provide IT support for all systems in production areas, including printers, networking, tablets, and Windows-based systems. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements Enrollment in a Computer Science or related degree program Student must have completed their Introduction to Programming course. Preferred Qualifications Prior hardware and software experience Knowledge/Skills Effectively and efficiently use Microsoft Office applications and other computer programs. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures, and governmental regulations. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret technical user/administration manuals for networks, personal computers, operating systems, or other materials related to job duties. Ability to effectively interface with other departments and management. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) ebee7de8 Last Name (required) 8e39150d Email (required) 9e351f86 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 807434bb Last Name (required) b76e8d92 Email (required) cfe40b5f Job Alert e961ce64 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 0f766554 Last Name (required) e8717f28 Email (required) 900762cf Send This Job To: ac08f99c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) f56af535 Last Name (required) 96b2d6b0 Email (required) d90c6b33 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information abou