    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/nbe-graduate-assistant-0310g-wichita-kansas-united-states-ce9798b8-032e-44e5-93e3-7e421db3b8ba": {
      "title": "NBE Graduate Assistant 0310G",
      "description": "NBE Graduate Assistant 0310G - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Graduate Assistant 0310G - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Graduate Assistant 0310G Information Technology | Student NBE Graduate Assistant 0310G 499400 Student Department Graduate Assistant for Technology Help Desk & Desktop Support – Shocker Success Center Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay Up to $3,840.00 per semester Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. 20 hours a week Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Join Our WSU Technology Help Desk Team! Are you a Graduate Student passionate about technology and helping others? The Tech Help Desk is seeking a dedicated individual to provide top-notch technical support to our community. As a member of our Technology Help Desk team, you will: • Assist with system access, wireless networks, email, University websites, and more. • Support students with personal devices, ensuring they stay connected and productive in a student-centered center. • Offer comprehensive services for WSU client computers via phone, email, and online ticketing. Key Responsibilities: • Assist with password resets and troubleshoot general access issues. • Create and manage tickets for servicing University-licensed software and hardware. • Collaborate closely with other teams, including Desktop Support, Windows Server Group, Network Support, and Telecom. Why Join Us? • Customer satisfaction is our top priority. You'll play a crucial role in meeting our community's tech needs. • Team-oriented environment. Work alongside skilled professionals and gain valuable experience. • Benefits. You will receive in-state tuition while in this position and be paid 20 hours a week. If you're ready to make a difference and help our WSU Technology Help Desk thrive, apply today! Job Summary A Graduate Staff Assistant (GSA) assistants university service and academic units in either non-teaching or non-research activities. Specific duties of the GSA vary widely, depending on the administrative or academic unit to which they are assigned, but should be at a level to make use of their education and abilities. Job Duties Provides technical support to customers of the University services, including system access, wireless networks, email, University websites, ticketing requests, and other services. Offers a full range of services necessary for operating the University client computers and peripherals. This position will focus on helping students with personal devices. In addition, Help Desk support is provided via phone, email, online ticketing, and walk-ins. Duties include but are not limited to assisting in password resets, troubleshooting general access issues, and creating tickets (work orders) for servicing university-licensed software and hardware. The Help Desk must work closely with other team members outside the Help Desk, including Desktop Support, Windows Server Group, Network Support, Telecom, and others. Customer satisfaction is paramount. This position reports to the Lead and Manager of the Technology Help Desk. The employee will receive assignments, general directions, and priorities from the Lead or Manager of the Technology Help Desk, Director of Client Services, and Chief Information Officer. Required Education Bachelor's degree Additional Requirements Essential Functions • Assists users with authentication to University networks, applications, and websites. • Responds to and diagnoses problems through user discussions, including problem recognition, research, isolation, and resolution. Solves less complex equipment and application issues. • Refers to problems that require a higher level of expertise and in-person service to desktop support staff. Alerts appropriate staff to issues that have the potential to disrupt network functions. • Diagnoses, may repair, and maintains various computer devices, operating systems, network connections, and hardware and software. • Contact clients regularly to discuss specific symptoms of equipment failure, the nature of repairs required, and possible solutions to equipment problems. Update the ticketing system as needed. Required Experience To be eligible for an assistantship, students must be admitted to a degree program in either full or conditional standing. Students admitted on probation or placed on academic probation following admission may be eligible for assistantship awards under certain circumstances. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, skills, and abilities: • Must possess a strong customer-centered philosophy. • Must be able to offer assistance adapted to clients' computer abilities. • Working knowledge of Windows Operating System, Mac OS, and Android. • Professional personal presentation. • Excellent listening skills • Strong verbal communication skills • Written communication skills • Ability to work with minimum supervision. Additional Information Join Our WSU Technology Help Desk Team! Are you a Graduate Student passionate about technology and helping others? The Tech Help Desk is seeking a dedicated individual to provide top-notch technical support to our community. As a member of our Technology Help Desk team, you will: • Assist with system access, wireless networks, email, University websites, and more. • Support students with personal devices, ensuring they stay connected and productive in a student-centered center. • Offer comprehensive services for WSU client computers via phone, email, and online ticketing. Key Responsibilities: • Assist with password resets and troubleshoot general access issues. • Create and manage tickets for servicing University-licensed software and hardware. • Collaborate closely with other teams, including Desktop Support, Windows Server Group, Network Support, and Telecom. Why Join Us? • Customer satisfaction is our top priority. You'll play a crucial role in meeting our community's tech needs. • Team-oriented environment. Work alongside skilled professionals and gain valuable experience. • Benefits. You will receive in-state tuition while in this position and be paid 20 hours a week. If you're ready to make a difference and help our WSU Technology Help Desk thrive, apply today! Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) e6feba5c Last Name (required) dd5680b9 Email (required) d0499de1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) f7d171ef Last Name (required) 4915041c Email (required) 0932bfda Job Alert efe767f7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Information Technology Information Technology Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) b45378f2 Last Name (required) 952c3225 Email (required) eb8c42aa 