    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-program-manager-atlas-wichita-kansas-united-states-220eb453-cade-4c55-91c7-a1b512c88deb": {
      "title": "NIAR Program Manager - ATLAS",
      "description": "NIAR Program Manager - ATLAS - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Program Manager - ATLAS - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Program Manager - ATLAS NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR Program Manager - ATLAS 499441 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR ATLAS Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Details ATLAS is looking for a Program Manager with a good understanding of material and process specifications, manufacturing techniques, and certification and qualification testing for advanced composites materials. Job Summary Performs program management in the laboratory to ensure satisfactory completion of research projects and programs. Manages laboratory research and testing and directs laboratory activities in matters of significance. Manages program requirements, production, scope, and budget. Coordinates with internal and external resources and/or stakeholders including engineering, contracts, finance, and other research laboratories. Essential Functions Manages laboratory activities related to the program, including research, testing; manages program requirements including production, scope, and budget Provides oversight of the work of the program to ensure that the work is completed on time and in accordance with established standards or specifications Evaluates program effectiveness by collecting and analyzing data in support of key performance metrics Ensures that activities are in compliance with policies and regulations Coordinates with and provides reports and updates to internal and external resources and stakeholders Required Education and Experience High school diploma or equivalent Five (5) years of related program management experience; Every 30 hours of related college coursework can be substituted for one (1) year of experience (maximum of four (4) years). Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Serves as primary point of contact for an entire statement of work and responsible for on-time delivery, costs, and overall performance. Provides risk management and mitigation strategies for on-time deliveries. Should have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must be proficient in the following computer skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, MS Project, MS VISIO. Demonstrated ability providing technical and management assistance and support to customers. Demonstrated ability to understand and interpret program requirements. Demonstrated ability leading collaboration of research activities. Demonstrated technical aptitude. High degree of energy, enthusiasm, and motivation for customer satisfaction. Demonstrated ability providing support in defining current and future technology advances that enhance and ensure laboratory prominence. Demonstrated ability in assisting with the preparation of long and short term business plans for a program. Experience working with cross-functional teams to ensure successful completion of program activities. Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Excellent time-management and critical thinking skills. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in engineering Physical Requirements Ability to inspect and/or surveil materials, equipment, reports, and/or incidents and identify any errors, needs and/or determining factors. Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Apply Now First Name (required) 70ed0344 Last Name (required) fe337f14 Email (required) 3de7aacb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d143dde4 Last Name (required) 9d3e766d Email (required) c71c095a Job Alert 63616520 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Staff Aviation Staff Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 1e0e51e4 Last Name (required) 5203d05a Email (required) d792aa0a Send This Job To: aaf311b4 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We