    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/idp-information-security-analyst-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "IDP Information Security Analyst",
      "description": "IDP Information Security Analyst - Wichita, Kansas, United States IDP Information Security Analyst - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode IDP Information Security Analyst Office Ind & Defense Administration | Information Technology, Staff IDP Information Security Analyst 499416 Information Technology Staff Department: IDP Information Technology Center Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 8am-5pm, Monday-Friday; additional hours may be requested as needed;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Information WSU IDP is currently searching for a Cybersecurity Analyst to assist with NIAR’s Security Helpdesk and Operations Center (SHOC). The SHOC is responsible for monitoring and safeguarding the organization’s systems and data, as well as enforcing cybersecurity industry best practices and compliance with NIST 800-171. The SHOC also plays a support and collaborative role with other WSU InfoSec teams. As a Cybersecurity Analyst, you will play a crucial role in supporting our cybersecurity efforts. This job offers a unique opportunity to apply and expand your knowledge in a real-world cybersecurity environment. You will work alongside with our Cybersecurity Teams, gaining hands-on experience in a Security Operations Center (SOC) environment and other cybersecurity domains. This position offers substantial exposure to the ever-evolving cybersecurity sector, and an opportunity to work with different tools, to be creative, and to be part of solutions to safeguard our systems, network, data and infrastructure. Job Summary Performs all procedures necessary to ensure the safety of information systems assets and to protect systems from intentional or inadvertent access or destruction. Essential Functions Interfaces with user community to understand their security needs and implements procedures to provide accommodations. Ensures that user community understands and adheres to necessary procedures to maintain security. Conducts accurate evaluation of the level of security required. Provides management with status reports and security metrics. Functions as part of the incident response team Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Six (6) years of experience in information security. Every 30 hours of college coursework can be substituted for one (1) year of experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Foundational cybersecurity knowledge, understanding of cybersecurity concepts, protocols, and best practices. Willing to listen and eager to learn. Detail oriented and excellent analytical skills. Self-motivated, proactive, and willing to take on investigations and research. Effective communication skills Comfortable asking “who, what, when, where, why, and how” Problem-solving skills Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree in Cybersecurity, Information Security, Computer Science, or related field. 1-2 years of experience in cybersecurity, preferrable in a SOC or as cybersecurity analyst. Relevant coursework or certifications in cybersecurity (e.g., CompTIA Security+, Network+, etc.) Knowledge and understanding of security concepts such as Phishing, Incident Response, Threat Analysis, and Cybersecurity Awareness Experience with Microsoft SharePoint, Project, Excel, PowerPoint and Visio Adept at writing technical documents Presentation skills Physical Requirements: Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Apply Now First Name (required) 7701f58a Last Name (required) 7db41c54 Email (required) bc99be84 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 95b8eae7 Last Name (required) 20002c99 Email (required) 21410ea4 Job Alert 91980bea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Technology Staff Information Technology Staff Department(s) Office Ind & Defense Administration Office Ind & Defense Administration Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) bccc843e Last Name (required) 8171dd2d Email (required) 5791169e Send This Job To: aa8a16cf Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, departme