      "title": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R",
      "description": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Student NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R 499383 Student Department Anthropology Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $13 / hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. TBD as class schedule allows & department needs Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The Anthropology Student Assistant provides administrative, academic, and operational support to faculty, staff, and students within the Department of Anthropology. This position offers students an opportunity to gain professional experience in higher education while contributing to the daily functions of the department. Duties may include research or clerical duties to include data collection, management, laboratory or office operations, event assistance, data entry, and support for departmental projects and activities. Students assistants will be directly supervised by a faculty member in the Department of Anthropology. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Student assistant may preform duties such as: Assist with research activities from an anthropological lens, including background research, data collection, laboratory management, file organization, and collections management. Assist with filing, scanning, copying, and organizing departmental records and materials. Perform data entry and maintain accurate departmental databases and spreadsheets. Prepare and distribute departmental correspondence, flyers, and promotional materials. Help organize and maintain office, laboratory, and storage spaces. Assist with student recruitment, outreach activities, and departmental events. Complete special projects and other duties as assigned. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Preference for Anthropology Majors Additional Information Please list major field of study Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 745a87d4 Last Name (required) e3c8e393 Email (required) 382a06d2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6c67e617 Last Name (required) 0f9677c0 Email (required) f6b00eb4 Job Alert 1d6bfd1e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may a