      "title": "NBE Lecturer WSU 0237L",
      "description": "NBE Lecturer WSU 0237L - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Lecturer WSU 0237L - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Lecturer WSU 0237L College of Fine Arts | Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer NBE Lecturer WSU 0237L 499382 Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Department School of Digital Arts Campus Location Wichita, KS-WSU Shocker Studios (Harry Street) Hire Type Part Time Pay Pay amount for the Fall 2026 semester is $2500 Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. varies by course schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Lecturers in the School of Digital Arts are expected to teach media arts courses as assigned following the prescribed curriculum as set forth in the course syllabus. The lecturer’s responsibilities include developing course materials, inspiring meaningful discussions, grading assignments, and providing feedback on student work. Lecturers are also expected to complete any requisite training as assigned by Wichita State University and the College of Fine Arts. If for some reason a lecturer is unable to make a class meeting, they must work with the program coordinator of their area to find appropriate coverage of materials. Job Summary The lecturer's responsibilities include developing course material and curricula, inspiring meaningful discussions, attending conferences, consulting with other academics and professionals, supervising graduate students, grading assignments, and being an active member of the university. Job Duties Lecturers in the School of Digital Arts are expected to teach media arts courses as assigned following the prescribed curriculum as set forth in the course syllabus. The lecturer’s responsibilities include developing course materials, inspiring meaningful discussions, grading assignments, and providing feedback on student work. Lecturers are also expected to complete any requisite training as assigned by Wichita State University and the College of Fine Arts. If for some reason a lecturer is unable to make a class meeting, they must work with the program coordinator of their area to find appropriate coverage of materials. Required Education Dependent upon department requirements. Additional Requirements Bachelor's degree or relevant professional experience Required Experience Dependent upon department requirements. Preferred Qualifications Master's Degree Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Frequent 60-90% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) ca68a5e4 Last Name (required) a12b41db Email (required) 3d5260f2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 382ef985 Last Name (required) de95795d Email (required) 6e26d143 Job Alert d4c5c225 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Department(s) College of Fine Arts College of Fine Arts Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replyin