    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/senior-contracts-and-grants-specialist-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist",
      "description": "Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist Office of Research (College) | Staff Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist 499112 Staff Department: Office of Research Campus Location: Remote - Candidate must reside outside of the immediate Wichita metro area to be eligible for remote work. Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Position range begins at $61,169/year and is commensurate with experience. Work Schedule: Typically, 8:00AM – 5:00PM, Monday – Friday. Overtime as needed to meet deadlines. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story In this senior-level role, you will provide comprehensive pre-award support for primarily grant and contract applications submitted on behalf of Wichita State University. Are you a problem solver? Enjoy the challenge of multiple projects and meeting their deadlines? This position will be responsible for the development, implementation and oversight of pre-award grant and contract functions, including ensuring all applications comply with sponsor and University guidelines, and State and Federal rules and regulations. In this role, you will be part of a team that makes it possible for Wichita State and our industry partners to conduct research and projects that will improve and change the community of Wichita, health, education, and technology for Kansas, the US and possibly the world! Job Summary Writes, reviews, and negotiates complex contracts pertaining to grants, sponsored research, service activities and other initiatives. Facilitates complex grant proposal development and fund sourcing as well as campus training efforts. Researches and interprets regulations, guidelines, and standards and oversees the processing of complex contracts and/or grants. Essential Functions Writes, reviews, and negotiates complex contracts, grants, and other sponsored awards. Reviews, assembles, and submits complex proposals on behalf of the University. Delivers education and guidance to faculty, research staff, departments, and administrators in development of competitive proposals and award administration of projects as well as funding policies, rules, and regulations. Researches and facilitates compliance with University, state, and federal laws, policies, and regulations in the daily operations of the contract and/or grant lifecycle. Advises leadership regarding potential conflicts of interest and time and dispute resolutions. Assists with the production of reports, proposals, and analyses for the University and for federal, state, educational, and other funding and regulatory agencies. Collects and prepares required documentation for proposals and contracts. Develops and reviews budget pertaining to the sponsored awards. Required Education and Experience: Sixty (60) hours of college coursework in business administration Four (4) years of experience in supporting complex proposal submissions, or negotiating complex contracts and/or awards at a university, government, or complex organization. An additional 60 hours of college coursework can be substituted for two (2) years of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: Certified Research Administrator (CRA) or Certified Pre-Award Research Administrator (CPRA) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: *Proficiency in negotiation and contract negotiation techniques sufficient to deal with high-level business, industry, scientific and/or government officials or proficiency in proposal and budget development experience. *Computer proficiencies to include word processing, spreadsheet, database, internet, and other forms of electronic communication. *Ability to multi-task, work cooperatively as part of a team and maintain high output when working autonomously. *Ability to provide excellent customer service. *Ability to multi-task with a common-sense approach to prioritizing. *Advanced grammar and writing, excellent verbal, interpersonal, analytical and communication skills. Additional Information: Remote work opportunities may be available. Candidate must reside outside of the immediate Wichita area to be eligible for remote work. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) d1ebb707 Last Name (required) d89de5c4 Email (required) b6036da0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ba8f2b3f Last Name (required) 0bcb8821 Email (required) 4cdf9303 Job Alert f620f4f3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Office of Research (College) Office of Research (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 382e5cda Last Name (required) e0dea0bc Email (required) 74e66ef7 Send This Job To: 4105c159 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta D