      "title": "GTA- Indirect School of Art, Design and Creative Industries (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "GTA- Indirect School of Art, Design and Creative Industries (Fall 2026) - Wichita, Kansas, United States GTA- Indirect School of Art, Design and Creative Industries (Fall 2026) - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode GTA- Indirect School of Art, Design and Creative Industries (Fall 2026) College of Fine Arts | Student GTA- Indirect School of Art, Design and Creative Industries (Fall 2026) 499135 Student Department School of Art, Design and Creative Industries Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $3,600/semester Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Dependent on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story School of Art, Design and Creative Industries Indirect Teaching Assistantship (GTA-Indirect) Job Summary The primary function of a graduate teaching assistant (GTA) is to assist with instruction. GTAs have the latitude to make independent decisions, use judgment and exercise discretion when dealing with student matters. The main purpose and responsibility of GTAs is to impart knowledge or training to students at Wichita State University. Job Duties Duties vary per position to be defined by the School of Art, Design and Creative Industries per semester per engagement. Required Education Bachelor's Degree Additional Requirements To be eligible for an assistantship, students must be admitted to a degree program in either full or conditional standing. Students admitted on probation or placed on academic probation following admission may be eligible for assistantship awards under certain circumstances. Required Experience To be eligible for an assistantship, students must be admitted to a degree program in either full or conditional standing. Students admitted on probation or placed on academic probation following admission may be eligible for assistantship awards under certain circumstances. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree Physi