      "title": "NIAR CAMO Maintenance Support Technician",
      "description": "NIAR CAMO Maintenance Support Technician - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR CAMO Maintenance Support Technician - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CAMO Maintenance Support Technician NIAR Institute | Temporary NIAR CAMO Maintenance Support Technician 498925 Temporary Department NIAR Center for Aircraft Modification and Operations Location Wichita, KS-WSU McConnell Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person”. Job Story The Maintenance Support Technician ensures technicians have the tools, materials, and logistical support needed to perform efficiently. This position focuses on organization, transport, and readiness—helping keep the hangar running smoothly and safely. Job Duties Retrieve, transport, and deliver tools, parts, and equipment to maintenance personnel as requested. Maintain inventory of consumables, hardware, and commonly used materials. Keep work areas, tool rooms, and hangar floors clean, organized, and hazard-free. Support technicians during maintenance tasks by staging equipment or preparing work areas. Track tool usage and ensure all tools are returned, accounted for, and in serviceable condition. Assist with moving ground support equipment (GSE) and positioning maintenance stands, ladders, and platforms. Perform basic administrative tasks such as logging parts, updating records, and completing checklists. Follow all safety procedures, FAA regulations, and company policies. Respond quickly to requests from supervisors and technicians. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Ability to follow instructions and work in a fast-paced environment. Basic mechanical aptitude or interest in aircraft Reliability and responsiveness Team-oriented mindset Strong work ethic and initiative Safety awareness Time management and multitasking Preferred Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Previous experience in a warehouse, maintenance, or aircraft environment Familiarity with hand tools and basic shop equipment Forklift certification (or willingness to obtain) Additional Information This position requires a valid driver's license Must be at least 16 years old Environmental Factors Active aircraft hangar environment with exposure to noise, moving equipment, and varying temperatures. Requires use of personal protective equipment (PPE) such as safety glasses, gloves, and hearing protection. Physical Requirements Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. and stand/walk for extended periods. Apply Now First Name (required) d1da39cb Last Name (required) 6dc02318 Email (required) e7c157c3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) dcd8375e Last Name (required) d0ede6a9 Email (required) 45672fd5 Job Alert c5526473 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe 