      "title": "NBE WSU Temp",
      "description": "NBE WSU Temp - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE WSU Temp - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE WSU Temp Strategic Engagement & Planning | Temporary NBE WSU Temp 499149 Temporary Department Veteran Student Support Services Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $21/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Mon - Fri, 12-5 Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Veteran Student Support Services (VSSS), a federally funded TRIO program at Wichita State University, is seeking a highly organized, customer-focused Administrative Assistant to support the daily operations of the program. This position serves as the first point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and community partners while providing administrative, clerical, and light database support that contributes to the success of military-connected students. The ideal candidate is detail-oriented, dependable, and enjoys working in a collaborative, student-centered environment. This position plays an important role in maintaining accurate student records, supporting program events, and ensuring compliance with federal reporting requirements. Job Summary Job Duties Provide professional front-office reception and customer service to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Answer and direct phone calls, emails, and other communications. Schedule appointments and maintain staff calendars as needed. Prepare correspondence, reports, spreadsheets, and other program documents. Perform data entry and maintain accurate student records in program databases and university systems. Assist with tracking student participation, services, and outcomes to support federal grant reporting. Organize and maintain electronic and paper files in accordance with university and federal confidentiality requirements. Assist with planning and coordinating workshops, orientations, student events, and outreach activities. Order, organize, and maintain office supplies and program materials. Support the VSSS team with special projects and other administrative duties as assigned. Required Education This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Additional Requirements Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications Associate's degree or coursework in business, office administration, or a related field. Experience with database management, data entry, or student information systems. Experience working in higher education, TRIO programs, or student services. Familiarity with military culture and a commitment to serving veterans, service members, and military-connected students. Experience coordinating meetings, workshops, or special events. Additional Information Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) da41401a Last Name (required) 92987ffa Email (required) 38c01a26 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 0546e540 Last Name (required) 6b464292 Email (required) d6db9dbf Job Alert 417b948f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create 