    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-machine-technician-atlas-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR Machine Technician - ATLAS",
      "description": "NIAR Machine Technician - ATLAS - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Machine Technician - ATLAS - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Machine Technician - ATLAS NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR Machine Technician - ATLAS 499055 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR Advanced Technologies Lab for Aerospace Systems Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Monday - Friday; 1st Shift. Work is performed onsite and in person. Job Details Join the NIAR Advanced Technologies Lab for Aerospace Systems as a machine technician. In this role, you’ll operate advanced automated fiber placement and CNC machining equipment to produce high‑precision aerospace components. You’ll handle machine setup, program verification, composite layup, troubleshooting, and quality checks in a fast‑paced, research‑driven environment. Ideal candidates bring CNC machining experience, strong attention to detail, and the ability to work from complex technical instructions. This position requires U.S. Person status due to export compliance regulations. Job Summary Responsibilities include set up and operation of various tools and equipment to create, modify, or repair precision parts. Monitors the machinery and conducts regular quality checks to ensure they are running properly and that the parts are being produced according to specifications. Essential Functions Machines and fabricates components by preparing and operating machines; works from complex drawings, prototype sketches, electronic files and/or verbal instructions. Responsible for production of high precision parts and performs complex setups required to produce parts Troubleshoots issues with equipment, new programs, and/or products; detects equipment malfunctions and maintains machinery to ensure functionality Provides training and oversight of new hires and students Job Duties Set up, mount, and prep tools for Automated Fiber Placement (AFP) layup. Load, verify, and run N/C programs. Debugs N/C programs with assistance from programming team. Calibrate tow placement to ensure machine operates properly. Verify defect free composite fiber placement on a continuous basis. Understand and adhere to work instructions and sequences specified in blueprints, operations planning, engineering orders, program setup sheets, standard work planning, etc. In addition to AFP machine operations, operator tasks include hand layup of composite assemblies. Operator will perform all tasks and activities associated with the manufacture of AFP Test panels. Must be able to set-up and adjust various machine setting such as but not limited to, programs, shop aids and bond jig placement. Help troubleshoot machine issues. Comply with AS9100 requirements. Conduct supply inventory management Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent by hire date Three (3) years of experience as a CNC Machinist; Every 30 hours of related college coursework and/or technical training can be substituted for one (1) year of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: Ability to become certified to operate forklifts, respirator use, and crane operation. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Experience using a KUKA controls and Siemens controls Demonstrates strong verbal and written communication skills Demonstrates and maintains value-added time management skills. Demonstrate good work ethics and lead by example. Attention to detail Ability to meet deadlines Ability to read and follow technical drawings and diagrammed instructions Ability to use precision tools to take accurate measurements Attention to detail and self-motivated Physical Requirements: Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Apply Now First Name (required) 3099a022 Last Name (required) 5a0e98fe Email (required) 633e2164 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) a30ee8aa Last Name (required) 7e094feb Email (required) 80ac1802 Job Alert 9901a138 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Staff Aviation Staff Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) bdefb3e8 Last Name (required) 493d0d1a Email (required) 914eb849 Send This Job To: 233bb2b9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appoin