    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-consultant-senior-loads-engineer": {
      "title": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer -",
      "description": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer - NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer - social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer NIAR Institute | Aviation, Temporary NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer 499068 Aviation Temporary Department NIAR Design, Analysis, Requirements & Certification (DARC) Location Wichita, KS-WSU McConnell Job Summary: The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) at Wichita State University is a nationally known aviation research center, providing a wide range of services including research, design, testing, certification and training. This role provides senior-level leadership for an external loads engineering group, functioning as an independent contractor responsible for guiding the team through the development of aircraft-level load cases and documentation required for program milestones. This position emphasizes technical direction, coordination of team activities, and mentoring of engineers at varying experience levels. Some travel may be required. Job Responsibilities: • Lead a team of engineers responsible for aircraft-level flight and ground loads development • Establish team priorities, define technical approaches, organize work assignments, and ensure alignment with program schedule • Proficient with static and dynamic external loads development • Coordinate with Mass Properties, Flight Sciences, Stress, F&DT disciplines • Prepare and deliver high-quality technical reports and customer-facing material • Mentor junior and mid-level engineers, fostering skill development and communication • Provide proactive communication and status updates to leadership and customers • Work independently with minimal oversight while ensuring team performance • Domestic travel up to 10% may be required. Qualifications/Minimum Requirements: • Bachelor’s degree in Engineering • Ten (10) years of experience in External Loads • Leadership experience - leading an engineering team and acting as a technical focal • Familiarity with civil and/or military requirements • Demonstrated ability to meet schedule expectations • Excellent writing and communication skills • Experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) • Professional and diplomatic demeanor • Strong accountability and integrity • Experience mentoring of interns and junior engineers Preferred Qualifications (Desired Skills/Experience): • Software Proficiency – Matlab, Nastran, Femap, Python, and similar tools All services are pursuant to a Professional Services Agreement, which must be executed prior to being assigned work Apply Now First Name (required) 5730030e Last Name (required) 5e84334a Email (required) acbc32a3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 762ba68b Last Name (required) 107dc93f Email (required) 913d625c Job Alert ee12e692 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Temporary Aviation Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ff0b1412 Last