    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/lecturer-wsu-wichita-kansas-united-states-75abd21a-8169-405e-8858-9da56dac3c45": {
      "title": "Lecturer WSU",
      "description": "Lecturer WSU - Wichita, Kansas, United States Lecturer WSU - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Lecturer WSU College of Health Professions | Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Lecturer WSU 498960 Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Department School of Nursing Campus Location Manhattan, KS Hire Type Part Time Pay Salary, Based on experience Work Schedule Day, Evening, or weekend shifts as needed Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Lecturer for undergraduate nursing students, Manhattan campus Job Summary The lecturer's responsibilities include developing course material and curricula, inspiring meaningful discussions, attending conferences, consulting with other academics and professionals, supervising graduate students, grading assignments, and being an active member of the university. Job Duties A Nurse Clinical lecturer, also known as an adjunct clinical instructor, oversees nursing students in clinical environments like hospitals, clinics, or community health centers. Their duties include guiding students in translating classroom theory into practical patient care and ensuring safe, evidence-based practices. Clinical lecturers utilize assessment and evaluation methods, assign grades, and help develop course materials. This role is carried out in accordance with the rules and regulations set by the Kansas State Board of Nursing and relevant accrediting bodies. Required Education Dependent upon department requirements. Additional Requirements Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) Minimum of one (1) year of clinical experience as a Registered Nurse Hold an active, current, unencumbered license to practice in Kansas Required Experience Dependent upon department requirements. Preferred Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) Teaching in nursing education Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Frequent 60-90% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) eabc8d16 Last Name (required) 1973f1dc Email (required) a1e2cb90 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b27e40e1 Last Name (required) 941f7066 Email (required) 698760fa Job Alert 5200a629 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Department(s) College of Health Professions College of Health Professions Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 55557c4f Last Name (required) 19b02992 Email (required) 022a1629 Send This Job To: 3b996056 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying ST