    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/contracts-and-grants-specialist-office-of-research-wichita-kansas-united-states-3590fcc7-5e3c-45b8-a81b-c223f7dd0a24": {
      "title": "Contracts and Grants Specialist - Office of Research",
      "description": "Contracts and Grants Specialist - Office of Research - Wichita, Kansas, United States Contracts and Grants Specialist - Office of Research - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Contracts and Grants Specialist - Office of Research Office of Research (College) | Staff Contracts and Grants Specialist - Office of Research 498962 Staff Department: Office of Research Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Position range begins at $27.36 per hour and is commensurate with experience. Work Schedule: Typically, 8:00AM – 5:00PM, Monday – Friday. Work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story In this role, you will provide comprehensive pre-award support for primarily grant and contract applications submitted on behalf of Wichita State University. Are you a problem solver? Enjoy the challenge of multiple projects and meeting their deadlines? This position will be responsible for the development, implementation and oversight of pre-award grant and contract functions, including ensuring all applications comply with sponsor and University guidelines, and State and Federal rules and regulations. In this role, you will be part of a team that makes it possible for Wichita State and our industry partners to conduct research and projects that will improve and change the community of Wichita, health, education, and technology for Kansas, the US and possibly the world! Job Summary Writes, reviews, and negotiates contracts pertaining to grants, sponsored research, service activities and other initiatives. Facilitates grant proposal development and fund sourcing as well as campus training efforts. Researches and interprets regulations, guidelines, and standards and oversees the processing or contracts and/or grants. Essential Functions Writes, reviews, and negotiates contracts, grants, and other sponsored awards. Reviews, assembles, and submits proposals on behalf of the University. Delivers education and guidance to faculty, research staff, departments, and administrators in development of competitive proposals and award administration of projects as well as funding policies, rules, and regulations. Researches and facilitates compliance with University, state, and federal laws, policies, and regulations in the daily operations of the contract and/or grant lifecycle. Advises leadership regarding potential conflicts of interest and time and dispute resolutions. Assists with the production of reports, proposals, and analyses for the University and for federal, state, educational, and other funding and regulatory agencies. Collects and prepares required documentation for proposals and contracts. Develops and reviews budget pertaining to the sponsored awards. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Six (6) years of experience in proposal development, research compliance, contract drafting or related field; every 30 hours of college coursework in accounting, finance, or business can be substituted for one year of experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Proficiency in negotiation and contract negotiation techniques sufficient to deal with high-level business, industry, scientific and/or government officials or proficiency in proposal and budget development experience. Computer proficiencies to include word processing, spreadsheet, database, internet, and other forms of electronic communication. Ability to work cooperatively as part of a team and maintain high output when working autonomously. Ability to provide excellent customer service. Ability to multi-task with a common-sense approach to prioritizing. Advanced grammar and writing, excellent verbal, interpersonal, analytical and communication skills. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 30e13fdc Last Name (required) eb444b91 Email (required) 388920ae Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4cd00935 Last Name (required) 509c535d Email (required) b49c8e80 Job Alert 1051ebfe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Office of Research (College) Office of Research (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) c24ff73d Last Name (required) 668f3adc Email (required) b55944bf Send This Job To: d5b1b025 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory pro