    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-cnc-machinist-i-composites-wichita-kansas-united-states-790c9c84-1bb3-4122-a712-5d367bb9ff61": {
      "title": "NIAR CNC Machinist I - Composites",
      "description": "NIAR CNC Machinist I - Composites - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR CNC Machinist I - Composites - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CNC Machinist I - Composites NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR CNC Machinist I - Composites 498898 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR Composites Campus Location: Wichita, KS - Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Work Schedule: Typically, Monday - Friday, 4:00 pm - 12:00 am. Pay: Commensurate with experience Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person”. Job Details The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) is a fast-growing area within WSU, known globally for our expertise in the most critical areas of aerospace research and development. Composites is looking for a CNC Machinist to join our team. Job Summary Responsibilities include set up and operation of various tools and equipment to create, modify, or repair precision parts. Monitors the machinery and conducts regular quality checks to ensure they are running properly and that the parts are being produced according to specifications. Essential Functions Machines and fabricates components by preparing and operating machine. Works from complex drawings, prototype sketches, electronic files and/or verbal instructions. Responsible for production of high precision parts and performs the machine setups required to produce parts. Loads parts in machine, cycles machine, and detects malfunctions in machine operations such as worn or damaged cutting tools. May troubleshoot issues with equipment, new programs, and/or products. Required Education and Experience High school diploma or equivalent by hire date One (1) year of experience as a CNC machinist; Every 30 hours of related college coursework and/or technical training can be substituted for one (1) year of experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Demonstrates strong verbal and written communication skills Demonstrates and maintains value-added time management skills. Demonstrate good work ethics and lead by example. Attention to detail. Ability to meet deadlines. Ability to read and follow technical drawings and diagrammed instructions. Ability to use precision tools to take accurate measurements. Attention to detail and self-motivated. Valid Driver’s License is required. Physical Requirements Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to inspect and/or surveil materials, equipment, reports, and/or incidents and identify any errors, needs and/or determining factors. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Apply Now First Name (required) f093371f Last Name (required) 39e73663 Email (required) 2f4ec55f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 1995ed54 Last Name (required) 994254b7 Email (required) bf38ade1 Job Alert 2b6875b0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the 