    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-dimensional-metrologist-ii-cmm-programmer-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR Dimensional Metrologist II - CMM Programmer",
      "description": "NIAR Dimensional Metrologist II - CMM Programmer - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Dimensional Metrologist II - CMM Programmer - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Dimensional Metrologist II - CMM Programmer NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR Dimensional Metrologist II - CMM Programmer 498492 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR AMP Lab Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Typically 8am – 5pm Monday – Friday; occasional evenings and weekends may be required as needed. Work is performed at NIAR Facilities and on-site at Customer facilities. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Information The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) at Wichita State University is looking for an experienced CMM Programmer. This position is located at the Advanced Machining and Prototyping (AMP) lab in Park City, KS. Come join our fast-paced and fast-growing team! Job Summary Performs tasks related to metrology measurements and analysis, including research and data collection, to support production. Produces accurate and repeatable measurement of parts and tools. Responsible for the care and upkeep of metrology equipment. Essential Functions Performs tasks related to metrology measurements and analysis to support teams and production. Establishes technical requirements for metrology measurements, planning implementation of new metrology techniques and measurement methods, processes, software, and equipment. Produces accurate and repeatable measurements of production parts and tools. Prepares inspection plans and schedules inspection tasks. Maintains and tracks metrology equipment and/or automation. Writes and runs advanced programs for metrology equipment. Provides reports for inspected parts; assembles First Article Inspection (FAI) reports. Assist in the development and provides training courses to internal and external partners. Provides guidance, direction, and assistance to junior metrology engineers. Researches new technologies Job Duties Program and Operate CMM equipment. Analyze measurements with metrology software: PolyWorks, Metrolog, and PC-DMIS. Research new metrology equipment, techniques, measurement methods, processes, and software. Participate in automated metrology projects. Prepare inspection plans and schedules inspection tasks. Produces accurate and repeatable measurements. Provides inspection reports for inspected parts and tooling. Assist with the development of CMM training courses. Provide training courses for customers. Provides guidance, direction, and assistance to junior dimensional metrologist. Required Education and Experience High school diploma or equivalent by date of hire Five (5) years of related work experience; or an equivalent combination of related education and experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to learn additional functions of metrology, including portable, stationary, and automation. Demonstrated advanced understanding of metrology concepts and practices. Demonstrated knowledge of Geometrical Dimensioning and Tolerancing (GD&T). Demonstrated advanced knowledge of metrology software. Ability to work productively with a variety of customers to understand their needs and constraints. Ability to work independently or as a member of a team. Ability to pay close attention to detail, organize tasks, and to think critically. Proficient in using hand gauges such as micrometers, calipers, and bore gauges. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Preferred Qualifications Five (5) years CMM programing experience; or an equivalent combination of related education and experience. High proficiency with two or more CMM providers. High proficiency with two or more Metrology software programs. Additional Information This position will perform tasks related to CMM Programming and CMM Operation using advanced 5 axis probing, analyze those measurements in a variety of metrology software packages and provide detailed reports and analysis. Take part in research to expand the capabilities of CMM equipment including automation. Help develop and provide training for CMM programming and equipment operation. Physical Requirements Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Apply Now First Name (required) ad5a4f13 Last Name (required) 95f7ddf3 Email (required) 2f668a0e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 04656241 Last Name (required) eaf2acbc Email (required) 8d654947 Job Alert 72b5e4a6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Staff Aviation Staff Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at