    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/student-assistant-work-study-wichita-kansas-united-states-e8fc4988-fabc-47c7-bb5b-a1211c63bee0": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Work Study",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Work Study - Wichita, Kansas, United States Student Assistant - Work Study - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Student Assistant - Work Study Strategic Enrollment Mgmt | Student Student Assistant - Work Study 498741 Student Department Office of Financial Aid/Shocker Fin Wellness Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $12.00/hour Work Schedule flexibility with student work/class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The Wichita State Office of Financial Aid is opening applications for an exciting new student peer financial counselor position for Spring and Fall 2023! The Office of Financial Aid is looking for undergraduate sophomores, juniors, and 4th year students (non-graduating) of any major who are passionate about increasing financial literacy among students on campus. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties 1. Learn how to become a peer financial coach through training in financial literacy topics, student financial aid, and counseling/presentation soft skills. 2. Meet with members of the WSU community to share knowledge of financial wellness like financial aid and financial literacy. 3. Assist the financial aid office with front desk support and administrative tasks between peer financial coach meetings and workshops. 4. Support the financial wellness coordinator and peer advising lead with developing financial wellness initiatives at WSU. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications • Official certification in federal financial aid training and peer financial coaching • Professional experience in: o Direct practice through one-on-one counseling with individuals and leading workshop groups o Documentation, intake, and termination o Community health work o Financial aid support o Project development and research o Event planning Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) a1ce4d9b Last Name (required) 29b0fce2 Email (required) a02f1b9d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) bb8cf591 Last Name (required) 697a9be5 Email (required) 76c97192 Job Alert 97a6c2a0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Na