    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/idp-information-assurance-and-security-engineer-wichita-kansas-united-states-7fa3b1d0-9324-4a61-ae2e-06dfd6e9f3f9": {
      "title": "IDP Information Assurance and Security Engineer",
      "description": "IDP Information Assurance and Security Engineer - Wichita, Kansas, United States IDP Information Assurance and Security Engineer - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode IDP Information Assurance and Security Engineer Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Staff IDP Information Assurance and Security Engineer 498842 Staff Department: Ennovar Campus Location: Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Typically Monday – Friday, 8am – 5pm; additional hours, including after-hours support of firewalls, may be required to support business needs. Work is completed onsite and in-person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Information We are seeking a self-driven, highly motivated, hands-on IT Security Engineer to serve as a subject-matter expert (SME)/technical lead on our cybersecurity operations team. This individual contributor role focuses on operational excellence and maturity for different cyber operations processes, automation alignment, internal audit readiness (e.g., internal & external audits, including CMMC), and mentorship. The SME will work on-site at Textron, collaborating with junior staff, student contractors, and technical teams, while interfacing with non-IT stakeholders to support secure, scalable cybersecurity operations. Job Summary Implements secure networking solutions to meet internal and external compliance requirements. Works in a cross-functional role requiring coordination with internal partners to monitor and control company networks. Ensures least privilege is followed and networks are secured from unauthorized devices and excessive access. May require collaboration with external companies to understand technical and business requirements in order to deliver solutions. Essential Functions Sets up, maintains, and performs ongoing configuration of firewalls. Performs vulnerability management and is responsible for change controls. Creates and maintains network security architecture and strategy. Responsible for device discovery, identification, and inventory. Provides enforcement of least privilege network access. Manages network isolation projects. Delivers troubleshooting and user support efforts. Provides incident management support. Manages and trains students. Performs other duties as assigned. Required Education and Experience High school diploma or equivalent at time of hire Five (5) years of cybersecurity or network security field experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Hands-on experience ensuring and supporting DFARS, NIST SP 800-171, NIST SP 800-53, CMMC (Level 2), and FedRAMP compliance Ability to identify and automate manual tasks using approved automation frameworks Ability to support the Security Exceptions process with technical input and documentation Ability to collaborate with cross-functional teams to align cybersecurity practices with business needs Ability to lead internal audit preparation and ensure documentation meets standards Strong technical background in automation, audit readiness, and governance Experience mentoring junior staff or student teams Familiarity with ServiceNow and scripting (PowerShell, Python) Familiarity with infrastructure concepts Experience using AI tools (e.g., GitHub Copilot, AI-based analytics platforms) Excellent communication skills with ability to interface across technical and non-technical teams Willingness and ability to work on-site full-time Physical Requirements Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Apply Now First Name (required) cce5b431 Last Name (required) ce1ba57a Email (required) 2675642c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) e30e41a7 Last Name (required) c7f2e2e2 Email (required) d6e1008c Job Alert e545a303 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) a5007e8d Last Name (required) 237b1f2a Email (required) 1ac1b35a Send This Job To: 1fccedcf Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) c88a621d Last Name (required) 31f3869b Email (required) 1ded37b4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage o