    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/f45-instructor-wichita-kansas-united-states-c20e0b2a-b2ec-4956-a9fd-15a1759d525d": {
      "title": "F45 Instructor",
      "description": "F45 Instructor - Wichita, Kansas, United States F45 Instructor - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode F45 Instructor Student Affairs (College) | Student F45 Instructor 498728 Student Department Campus Recreation Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15.00/hr Work Schedule variable dependent upon class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The F45 Instructor is committed to creating a safe, engaging, and effective environment for group exercise classes at Wichita State University. This role involves delivering high-quality fitness experiences to students, Campus Recreation members, and non-members. The instructor should be passionate about fitness, dedicated to promoting health and wellness, and focused on fostering a supportive and fun community. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Attend in-service meetings and training sessions as required. • Arrive 15 minutes before class to ensure a prompt and organized start. • Maintain a professional demeanor and uphold the values of Wichita State University and Campus Recreation. • Serve as an ambassador for the Health & Fitness department, promoting its mission and services. • Ensure participant safety during all classes by monitoring and modifying exercises to accommodate varying fitness levels. • Educate participants on proper equipment usage and ensure all university equipment is used appropriately. • Provide a friendly, positive, and customer service-oriented environment. • Observe, educate, and enforce facility rules in a welcoming and helpful manner. • Engage in ongoing professional development and training to expand knowledge in the fitness field. • Report potential hazards or unsafe conditions to the direct supervisor promptly. • Respond to medical emergencies within your qualification level and ability. • Perform other duties as assigned to support program operations and success. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Required Qualifications Comprehensive understanding of the physical aspects of exercise and fitness. Exceptional public speaking and communication skills. Strong interpersonal and people skills to engage and motivate participants. Proven ability to demonstrate and explain proper exercise techniques and practices. Current CPR/First Aid certification or willingness to obtain it within two weeks of the start date. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Pursuing Bachelor's degree in Exercise Science, Health Sciences, or a related field. Current certifications in group fitness or personal training (e.g., ACE, NASM, AFAA, or similar). Previous experience teaching F45 or leading group exercise classes. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) c05a6b94 Last Name (required) 73296f65 Email (required) e4f8ec7c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d9bd4727 Last Name (requi