    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-consultant-design-engineer-structure-and-systems": {
      "title": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Design Engineer - Structure and Systems -",
      "description": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Design Engineer - Structure and Systems - NIAR CONSULTANT - Design Engineer - Structure and Systems - social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CONSULTANT - Design Engineer - Structure and Systems NIAR Institute | Aviation, Temporary NIAR CONSULTANT - Design Engineer - Structure and Systems 498547 Aviation Temporary Department: NIAR Engineering Design and Modification Team Campus Location: Wichita, KS-WSU McConnell Job Summary: Since its inception in 1985, National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) at Wichita State University has made a name for itself as the most capable university-based aviation research center in the United States, providing research, design, testing, certification and training to the aviation manufacturing industry, government agencies, educational entities and other clients that can benefit from our services. NIAR is looking for a talented Design Engineer to join our growing, innovative team. This position will be an independent contractor consulting as a Design Engineer with NIAR to support various diverse customer programs. This person will support design tasks across structural elements, systems installations, and engineering deliverables throughout the product lifecycle. They will execute changes to CAD models, drawings, and other documents in support of the product, participate in trade studies, create and maintain ICDs (interface control documents), and coordinate with customers. Some travel may be required. Responsibilities: Designs and substantiates structure, mechanical systems, and interior components on various company projects and programs across the entire lifecycle of design and development. Design activity includes primary structure, flight test and development structure, instrumentation, flight controls, ECS, secondary structures, interiors, control surfaces, special mission equipment, prototype development, etc. Prepare and maintain technical documentation such as design datasets, change requests, and engineering reports. Requirements: Ability to work on-site 80% of the time This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Bachelor or above degree in engineering technical discipline with two (2) years’ experience Self-motivated and driven to produce high quality designs on schedule Experience in 3D CAD tools (3DExperience, CATIA V5, Siemens NX, Solidworks) Familiarity with NASA and/or FAA structural design standards Experience with airframe structure, systems, or interior design using appropriate CAD workbenches Experience developing and modifying 3D models & drawings or MBD datasets Familiar with GD&T, design fundamentals, and ASME standards Y14.5, Y14.31, Y14.37, and Y14.41 Proficiency of GD&T tolerance application Experience with Microsoft Office (word, excel, PowerPoint). Excellent writing and communication skills Domestic travel up to 10 % may be required Desired Skills/Experience: Knowledge of applicable industry system specifications such as ARP 4754, AS 50881, DO-160 All services will be provided as an independent contractor, pursuant to a Professional Services Agreement, which must be executed prior to being assigned any work. Apply Now First Name (required) 96d081e6 Last Name (required) 181a58ab Email (required) 928389fb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) efd85096 Last Name (required) 89347c0a Email (required) d952e545 Job Alert 244c0700 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Temporary Aviation Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 96a07ee6 Last Name (required) d0777e48 Email (required) 45b4e64f Send This Job To: fdaec2a8 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) aa4ff91e Last Name (required) 75ab97d7 Email (required) 5f3c7954 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
