    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-atlas-injection-molding-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR ATLAS Injection Molding Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR ATLAS Injection Molding Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR ATLAS Injection Molding Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR ATLAS Injection Molding Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR ATLAS Injection Molding Student Assistant 498452 Student Department NIAR ATLAS Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties -Operate the press lab machinery and assist with ongoing operations within the lab. -Perform manual labor intensive tasks such as switching molds, operating power tools, operating injection molding machines and repair work. -Work on CAD design projects and MS Office applications. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements -Able to work for 20 hours during school semesters and 40 hours during summer -Easily able to understand and perform labor-intensive work on manufacturing/maintenance operations on the ENGEL and Krauss Maffei machines. -Be self-motivated to perform maintenance or organization/cleaning duties when necessary. -Able to easily grasp new and wide-ranging concepts such as robot programing, injection molding machine programming, chiller, plumbing, electrical troubleshooting etc... -Attention to detail with all tasks ensuring high quality results (TC wiring, tool prepping, mold polishing) in a timely manner. -Cleanliness and organization of lab space ensuring all tools and machinery are maintained in good working condition. -Ability to follow basic safety procedures to minimize accidents and harm to others within the work cell. -Become forklift certified and operate an overhead crane Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to stand or sit for extended periods Ability to lift and carry up to 50 lbs Apply Now First Name (required) 7b640c23 Last Name (required) 0087dfd1 Email (required) a6bdffd6 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 68e79a6d Last Name (required) c20955c5 Email (required) 73979bcc Job Alert 3fc6aab1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ef6bf1af Last Name