      "title": "NIAR Composites and Structures Machinist",
      "description": "NIAR Composites and Structures Machinist - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Composites and Structures Machinist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Composites and Structures Machinist NIAR Institute | Temporary NIAR Composites and Structures Machinist 497115 Temporary Department NIAR Composites & Structures Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Full Time Pay $18 - 21 per hour Work Schedule Monday - Friday 4 pm - 12 am Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person”. Job Story The NIAR Composites & Structures lab is looking for a machinist. Job Duties Responsible for setting up and operating CNC machines with minimal supervision. Read and interpret instructions to machine parts to specified dimensions while meeting tolerances. Additional Requirements Must be able to work Monday - Friday from 4 pm - 12 am. 40 hours per week. Machining experience preferred. Able to do simple addition and subtraction. Physical Requirements Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information Ability to remain in a stationary position for up to 8 hours. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs Ability to be in loud noise environments Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify errors, needs and/or determining factors Lifting steel fixtures and occasional heavy parts Apply Now First Name (required) 11207b6e Last Name (required) 9d07c4fa Email (required) aff0e6e8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or