    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-darc-electrical-design-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant 497770 Student Department Engineering Design and Mod Team Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 - 22 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Engineering Design and Mod Team is seeking a student assistant to assist with electrical design. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area in which the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties This position will support various diverse program efforts as an electrical design student assistant. Tasks include detailed 2d schematics of electrical systems, 3d routing and modeling of electrical systems, drawing creation, software tool automation, and modeling parts from existing diagrams, scans, and drawings. This role will utilize design handbooks, recommended practices, and industry standards to define engineering for electrical systems. The electrical design intern will primarily utilize Autocad, Siemens Capital, CATIA V5, and 3DX CAD software. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Working towards a degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or Computer Science. Sophomore or higher preferred. Experience and interest in electrical systems, circuit analysis, and software automation. Experience with MATLAB, AutoCAD, Visual Basic, and Python programming. Prefer interest in CAD. CATIA V5, 3DX, or Solidworks. Experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Excellent writing and communication skills. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment, including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) d55fab83 Last Name (required) 530e4c78 Email (required) acc7c645 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6d5c406d Last Name (required) b346f3be Email (required) 320ba6b7 Job Alert 2e033689 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 3825dd57 Last Name (required) cb6f6b3d Email (required) 6be68902 Send This Job To: faf8646b Share Now! Please wait... Done Not 