    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/custodial-lead-special-events-and-projects-2nd-shift-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Custodial Lead, Special Events and Projects (2nd shift)",
      "description": "Custodial Lead, Special Events and Projects (2nd shift) - Wichita, Kansas, United States Custodial Lead, Special Events and Projects (2nd shift) - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Custodial Lead, Special Events and Projects (2nd shift) Physical Plant | Facilities/Groundskeeping, Staff Custodial Lead, Special Events and Projects (2nd shift) 499732 Facilities/Groundskeeping Staff Department: Facilities Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starting at $17.73 and commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 3:00 pm - 11:30 pm Sunday - Tuesday & Friday - Saturday (days off are Wednesday & Thursday); work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Custodial Lead of Special Events and Projects plays a key role in keeping the WSU campus clean, disinfected, and safe while supporting the energetic flow of athletic, community, and special events that bring the university to life. This dynamic position adapts to shifting schedules, including weekends, evenings, and nontraditional hours, to ensure every event shines, from packed athletic games to campus wide celebrations. In addition to event support, this role also contributes to important campus projects such as floor refinishing, carpet extraction, deep restroom sanitization, and seasonal maintenance tasks that keep facilities in top condition. The position also champions environmentally conscious “green” cleaning practices, helping create healthier spaces for students, staff, and visitors. With a robust benefits package effective on day one, generous paid time off, and the opportunity to directly support WSU’s most memorable moments, this role offers both meaningful impact and rewarding flexibility. Job Summary Performs routine manual work in cleaning, servicing, and stocking supplies in University buildings as well as routine manual work including set-up and support for University and athletic facilities special events and projects, excluding housing facilities. Acts as a liaison between custodial staff and leadership to ensure service excellence. Essential Functions Assists University special events by providing support before, during and after events. Sweeps, mops, and buffs and sprays buff floors and vacuums rugs and carpets in assigned area as needed. Provides support for floor care, including restoring, maintaining, and refinishing floors of all types as well as other custodial special projects. Washes windows, walls, and other assigned areas. Picks up trash, empties garbage containers, and removes all trash to area for disposal. Cleans rest rooms, offices, and replenishes supplies. Performs regular inspections of all areas to determine need for services and/or quality of services performed. Communicates findings and recommendations to leadership. Maintains sufficient stock and supplies for the proper performance of assigned duties. Provides guidance and coaching to custodial staff as needed. Conducts service recovery efforts in response to questions and/or concerns from faculty, staff, students, and visitors according to the department's customer service protocols. Assists supervisor with payroll, scheduling, education of department staff, budget and other duties as assigned. Shovels and removes snow and ice from designated areas such as roofs, sidewalks and entryways as required. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in custodial work Required License/Certifications/Training: Valid Driver's License Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of the materials, methods and practices used in housekeeping operations and operation, use care of vacuum cleaners, scrubbing machines, floor machines and other janitorial equipment; and the use of safe principles and safe techniques for Supervision. Familiarity with the principles of inventory control: sanitation and all practices and procedures. Ability to work and supervise effectively with fellow workers and others Ability to keep and maintain records. Ability to maintain and organize filing and record keeping systems, confidential information. Ability to supervise multiple custodial work units and various projects, work orders, and personnel. Physical Requirements: Ability to position self to clean designated areas, equipment and items. This includes but is not limited to the ability to clean in confined, elevated, and loud noise spaces. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to drive state vehicle. Ability to remove snow and ice from designated areas. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Additional Physical Requirement: Heavy Work: Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 20 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) 70725a42 Last Name (required) bd0639a7 Email (required) 9ce83fcb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4dbf8c81 Last Name (required) 5b276e13 Email (required) db47ea8c Job Alert b744889d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Facilities/Groundskeeping Staff Facilities/Groundskeeping Staff Department(s) Physical Plant Physical Plant Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 726848c7 Last Name (required) 7ca1aba5 Email (required) 0502f5f8 Send This Job To: d4365017 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Custodian - 2nd Shift Join Our Team as a Custodian – Be the Hero of Clean Spaces! Are you ready to make a real difference every day? As a Custodian, you’ll be the champion of cleanliness and comfort, ensuring our spaces shine and sparkle for everyone who walks through the door. From keeping areas spotless to stocking essentials, you’ll play a key role in creating an environment people love. Custodian Specialist (2nd shift) When campus floors need expert care and cleaning equipment needs a skilled hand, our Custodian Specialist, Senior steps in to make it happen. You’re the kind of person who takes pride in a gleaming hallway, a freshly waxed floor, and a vacuum that hums like new. You know your way around scrubbers, buffers, and carpet extractors, and when something breaks, you don’t just report it, you help fix it. You research parts and coordinate repairs to keep our custodial equipment running like a dream. Assistant Director- TRIO Communication Upward Bound You can talk career goals with a school administrator, coordinate a program with university partners, and then turn around and connect with a room full of high school students. You know how to read the room, meet people where they are, and make connections that stick. Working with students, families, schools, and university partners, you’ll help create experiences that make college and future opportunities feel more accessible to the students you serve. You’ll build relationships throughout the school and community, collaborate with other TRIO programs and university departments, and help shape an academic-year curriculum that keeps students engaged, curious, and moving forward. Custodian Specialist (2nd Shift) IDP oin Our Team as a Custodian Specialist – Be the Hero of Clean Spaces! Due to ITAR regulations, the candidate must be a US Citizen to be considered for this role. Are you ready to make a real difference every day? As a Custodian Specialist, you’ll be the champion of cleanliness and comfort, ensuring our spaces shine and sparkle for everyone who walks through the door. From keeping areas spotless to stocking essentials, you’ll play a key role in creating an environment people love. You’ll also get hands-on with some cool equipment and embrace “Green” cleaning practices, because we care about healthier workplaces and a healthier planet. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 3cb1bfe0 Last Name (required) e5d910af Email (required) ef8076b9 Send Please wait... Done