    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-clinical-psychology-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology 499795 On Site Faculty Department: Department of Psychology Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000.00 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8am to 5pm; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Psychology Department at Wichita State University seeks to hire a 9-month tenure-track, Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology to begin August 2, 2027. We welcome applications from individuals with a cognitive-behavioral orientation as broadly-defined. We are open to all areas of research and clinical interests, but are especially interested in scholars who could contribute in one or more of the following areas: integrated behavioral healthcare in the primary care setting, family systems approaches, and third-wave behavioral therapies. Applicants should be PhD graduates of an APA- accredited program in clinical psychology, (completed prior to August of 2027), licensed (or licensed-eligible) as a psychologist in the state of Kansas, and have a strong record of peer-reviewed publications. The Clinical Psychology PhD Program at Wichita State is fully-accredited by the American Psychological Association and embraces a scientist–practitioner model, within a clinical–community framework. The department has three Ph.D. programs in clinical, community, and human factors psychology, as well as a large undergraduate student body. The department is research oriented and has an expectation for faculty to seek external funding. Wichita State also has an in-house clinical psychology training clinic that serves the greater Wichita area. Salary is $70,000.00. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, mentor Ph.D. students, conduct research, apply for grants, publish in peer reviewed journals. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD graduate of an APA- accredited program in clinical psychology. Degree should be completed prior to August of 2027. Experience publishing in peer-reviewed journals Required License/Certifications/Training: Licensed (or licensed-eligible) as a psychologist in the state of Kansas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Training in clinical psychology Ability to contribute to building an inclusive and welcoming environment for colleagues and students Ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, engaging, and dynamic environment comprised of individuals with a range of backgrounds, skills, and perspectives. Ability to attract external funding Commitment to teach both graduate and undergraduate courses Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research philosophy Description of how you work to create a cooperative and welcoming work place. (attach as Faculty Document 1) Review of applications will begin November 20, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact Samantha Slade at samantha.slade@wichita.edu WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) dddd27c7 Last Name (required) 53d0ca91 Email (required) 68cf949a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 2f55e63e Last Name (required) 61a43c84 Email (required) bafa2272 Job Alert 4887eeff Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ec7f166c Last Name (required) 652708a2 Email (required) 08f1526b Send This Job To: ffb3a206 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Custodian - 2nd Shift Join Our Team as a Custodian – Be the Hero of Clean Spaces! Are you ready to make a real difference every day? As a Custodian, you’ll be the champion of cleanliness and comfort, ensuring our spaces shine and sparkle for everyone who walks through the door. From keeping areas spotless to stocking essentials, you’ll play a key role in creating an environment people love. Custodial Lead, Special Events and Projects (2nd shift) The Custodial Lead of Special Events and Projects plays a key role in keeping the WSU campus clean, disinfected, and safe while supporting the energetic flow of athletic, community, and special events that bring the university to life. This dynamic position adapts to shifting schedules, including weekends, evenings, and nontraditional hours, to ensure every event shines, from packed athletic games to campus wide celebrations. In addition to event support, this role also contributes to important campus projects such as floor refinishing, carpet extraction, deep restroom sanitization, and seasonal maintenance tasks that keep facilities in top condition. The position also champions environmentally conscious “green” cleaning practices, helping create healthier spaces for students, staff, and visitors. With a robust benefits package effective on day one, generous paid time off, and the opportunity to directly support WSU’s most memorable moments, this role offers both meaningful impact and rewarding flexibility. Custodian Specialist (2nd shift) When campus floors need expert care and cleaning equipment needs a skilled hand, our Custodian Specialist, Senior steps in to make it happen. You’re the kind of person who takes pride in a gleaming hallway, a freshly waxed floor, and a vacuum that hums like new. You know your way around scrubbers, buffers, and carpet extractors, and when something breaks, you don’t just report it, you help fix it. You research parts and coordinate repairs to keep our custodial equipment running like a dream. Assistant Director- TRIO Communication Upward Bound You can talk career goals with a school administrator, coordinate a program with university partners, and then turn around and connect with a room full of high school students. You know how to read the room, meet people where they are, and make connections that stick. Working with students, families, schools, and university partners, you’ll help create experiences that make college and future opportunities feel more accessible to the students you serve. You’ll build relationships throughout the school and community, collaborate with other TRIO programs and university departments, and help shape an academic-year curriculum that keeps students engaged, curious, and moving forward. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) a3648ad6 Last Name (required) 3ea1ab99 Email (required) 5d036dfc Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors 