    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-research-associate-composites-wichita-kansas-united-states-f6494fa0-c9b7-4579-9eb0-15e3c71957c4": {
      "title": "NIAR Research Associate - Composites",
      "description": "NIAR Research Associate - Composites - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Research Associate - Composites - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Research Associate - Composites NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR Research Associate - Composites 499834 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR Composites & Structures Campus Location: 4004 N. Webb Rd Wichita, KS - NIAR / NCAT Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Typically Monday - Friday 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person”. Job Details We are seeking a motivated and detail‑oriented Research Associate to support laboratory research, process development, and materials testing within the Composites & Structures department. In this role, you will work alongside experienced researchers to execute hands-on laboratory activities, contribute to quality and process improvements, and support projects that drive industry-leading advancements. If you are a self‑starter with a passion for applied research, we invite you to apply. Job Summary Performs daily laboratory activities with the objective of achieving optimal quality control, process implementation and project performance. Reports outcomes throughout the process and at project conclusion. Essential Functions Designs and conducts specialized research as instructed by senior laboratory staff. Provide periodic status reports as requested and provide results report as project conclusion. Reviews research laboratory procedures, recommends updates to current procedures and implements new procedures as appropriate. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree in Engineering or a related STEM field Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to initiate work as a self-starter and to prioritize with time management skills Demonstrated ability with attention to detail and analytical aptitude Excellent verbal and written communication skills Ability to work independently and as team player; work in an environment that builds people, engages the community, and provides customer satisfaction Strong problem‑solving skills with the ability to think critically Physical Requirements: Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Ability to position self to place, construct, and/or maintain equipment and items in designated spaces. This includes but is not limited to the ability to work in confined and elevated spaces. Ability to inspect and/or surveil materials, equipment, reports, and/or incidents and identify any errors, needs and/or determining factors. Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Apply Now First Name (required) fc67e4ae Last Name (required) bada30c5 Email (required) 2710dd2d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 69a4e0ef Last Name (required) a75f532e Email (required) 71a88e08 Job Alert 06ccc4bb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Staff Aviation Staff Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 94b0fe73 Last Name (required) 9818afda Email (required) 8e80f618 Send This Job To: c61a2436 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Custodian - 2nd Shift Join Our Team as a Custodian – Be the Hero of Clean Spaces! Are you ready to make a real difference every day? As a Custodian, you’ll be the champion of cleanliness and comfort, ensuring our spaces shine and sparkle for everyone who walks through the door. From keeping areas spotless to stocking essentials, you’ll play a key role in creating an environment people love. Custodial Lead, Special Events and Projects (2nd shift) The Custodial Lead of Special Events and Projects plays a key role in keeping the WSU campus clean, disinfected, and safe while supporting the energetic flow of athletic, community, and special events that bring the university to life. This dynamic position adapts to shifting schedules, including weekends, evenings, and nontraditional hours, to ensure every event shines, from packed athletic games to campus wide celebrations. In addition to event support, this role also contributes to important campus projects such as floor refinishing, carpet extraction, deep restroom sanitization, and seasonal maintenance tasks that keep facilities in top condition. The position also champions environmentally conscious “green” cleaning practices, helping create healthier spaces for students, staff, and visitors. With a robust benefits package effective on day one, generous paid time off, and the opportunity to directly support WSU’s most memorable moments, this role offers both meaningful impact and rewarding flexibility. Custodian Specialist (2nd shift) When campus floors need expert care and cleaning equipment needs a skilled hand, our Custodian Specialist, Senior steps in to make it happen. You’re the kind of person who takes pride in a gleaming hallway, a freshly waxed floor, and a vacuum that hums like new. You know your way around scrubbers, buffers, and carpet extractors, and when something breaks, you don’t just report it, you help fix it. You research parts and coordinate repairs to keep our custodial equipment running like a dream. Assistant Director- TRIO Communication Upward Bound You can talk career goals with a school administrator, coordinate a program with university partners, and then turn around and connect with a room full of high school students. You know how to read the room, meet people where they are, and make connections that stick. Working with students, families, schools, and university partners, you’ll help create experiences that make college and future opportunities feel more accessible to the students you serve. You’ll build relationships throughout the school and community, collaborate with other TRIO programs and university departments, and help shape an academic-year curriculum that keeps students engaged, curious, and moving forward. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 2bec287d Last Name (required) d4dc4d0c Email (required) 6b27d02c Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
