    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/facilities-specialist-university-libraries-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Facilities Specialist, University Libraries",
      "description": "Facilities Specialist, University Libraries - Wichita, Kansas, United States Facilities Specialist, University Libraries - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Facilities Specialist, University Libraries Library | Staff Facilities Specialist, University Libraries 499784 Staff Department: University Libraries Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $17.73 per hour Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm, evenings and weekends as required.; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Do you thrive in a dynamic environment where your skills in meeting service standards and inventory management can shine? University Libraries is seeking a dedicated and innovative Facilities Specialist to join our team. This role is pivotal in ensuring physical spaces are accessible, organized, and compliant with the highest standards. Job Summary Performs a variety of professional and administrative duties that facilitate the operations of a function(s), program(s), and/or department(s). Essential Functions Supports the programs and services provided by the department(s) by performing varied or related processes which may include creating and maintaining databases and websites, monitoring, facilitating, and enforcing compliance with established criteria, guidelines and standards, etc. May coordinate, attend, prepare materials for and/or take minutes at meetings and special events. May prepare or assist in the preparation of budgets, grant applications, proposals, status reports and/or financial statements. May identify and pursue ways to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of administrative procedures used by students, faculty, visitors and staff. May order and maintain sufficient inventory of office supplies and equipment. May be assigned to lead, assist, coordinate or support special projects as needed. Job Duties Monitor, evaluate, and maintain unit's physical spaces Enter or modify data in databases and applications Enter and monitor ticketing system Coordinate activities with central facilities services units Search databases and the internet for bibliographic data or other data in support of library systems (ex. Catalog) or applications Interpret and apply policies, best practices and procedures Attend department and unit meetings, training sessions and special events Maintain data on unit activities and prepare routine reports Identify and report on recommendations for continuous improvement of the unit’s efficiency and effectiveness Monitor unit supplies Order office supplies as necessary Participate in unit and departmental projects May hire, train, supervise, and evaluate student workers. Other duties as assigned Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in general office, clerical, administrative support or related field Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to work in a highly physical production environment Strong customer service orientation Strong problem-solving, organizational and analytical skills Demonstrated ability to work in databases, including accurate data entry and searching Excellent attention to detail; ability to maintain high level of quality Ability to enter metadata using established standards and best practices Demonstrated excellent oral and written communication skills in English; strong interpersonal skills Ability to learn new skills, technology, and computer applications quickly Ability to adapt to new practice and theory Demonstrated ability to work well independently and in teams with varied user communities Ability to operate office equipment (including, but not limited to, computers, photocopiers, and scanners) Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) 1e9f2a47 Last Name (required) f25cb30a Email (required) 8ac29bd7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 2e93c9bc Last Name (required) 55a5c5e2 Email (required) 3da6e428 Job Alert aa0e8dc4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Library Library Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 455fb2f5 Last Name (required) 9953c89f Email (required) 2abaedb0 Send This Job To: 6bcae781 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working