    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/usd-259-tech-support-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "USD 259 Tech Support Student Assistant",
      "description": "USD 259 Tech Support Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States USD 259 Tech Support Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode USD 259 Tech Support Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student USD 259 Tech Support Student Assistant 495911 Student Department Ennovar Tech Services and Solutions Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story Ennovar is looking for a student to work tech support for Wichita public schools USD 259. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Works under the supervision of the Site Technology Specialist (STS). Displays a high skill level and technical expertise relating to computer technology, networking, and other functions of the assignment. Conducts in-service training activities for building personnel regarding the proper use and maintenance of computer equipment and software. Meets specified deadlines and confers with the STS to ensure the satisfactory execution and completion of a specific job. Works cooperatively with others in order to maintain a harmonious and efficient operation. Coordinates with STS and district support organizations on technology issues for the site. Determines priority with the STS. Tracks backlog of requests. Escalates problems as necessary. Performs workstation hardware/software setup and maintenance to include: * Hardware upgrades and installs * OS installs and updates * Software installs and updates * Repair of hardware components, working with the STS for the appropriate warranty replacement work Serves as a resource for troubleshooting technology systems issues (hardware, software, network). Demonstrates understanding of site network topology. Performs network administration. Assists the STS as necessary in managing student and staff user accounts and network shares. Installs and manages server-based applications, as necessary. Performs network troubleshooting of switches and network drops in classrooms/offices, escalating problems if necessary. Performs all other duties as required by the STS. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements - Must work a minimum of 25 hours, Monday-Friday, between the hours of 7:30 AM - 4:30 PM. - Must be self-sustaining - Must have basic IT knowledge - Preferred Major(s): MIS, Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Computer Engineering Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 65a37d20 Last Name (required) e2205a3e Email (required) 8d0d1a1a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) bb198a93 Last Name (required) 032915d3 Email (required) 01bec29e Job Alert 88d7b06a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering