    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/boeing-kitters-junior-lead-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Boeing Kitters Junior Lead",
      "description": "Boeing Kitters Junior Lead - Wichita, Kansas, United States Boeing Kitters Junior Lead - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Boeing Kitters Junior Lead Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Temporary Boeing Kitters Junior Lead 495295 Temporary Department Ennovar Tech Services and Solutions Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $18 - 20 per hour Work Schedule Dependent upon classes Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Junior Lead is responsible for leading a team of 10 to 12 student employees. Reporting to the Senior Lead, this role involves managing activities related to production, personnel, and workflow of kits. Job Duties • Lead a team of 10 to 12 student employees in the production of kits. • Oversee workflow by monitoring completion/verification of kits. • Ensure adherence to production schedules and quality standards. • Train and coach team members on job tasks, policies, and safety protocols • Assist in certifying Kitters for production and verification. • Monitor and manage inventory levels for kitting purposes. • Complete daily metrics as needed. • Collaborate with the Senior Lead to optimize production processes and efficiency. • Maintain cleanliness and safety standards in the work area. • Perform any other duties as assigned to support production operations. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements • Previous experience in a leadership or supervisory role (1yr. preferred). • Strong communication and interpersonal skills • Ability to effectively lead and motivate a team. • Detail-oriented with a focus on quality and accuracy • Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and handle multiple tasks simultaneously. • Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications (Excel, Word, Outlook) Preferred Qualifications • High school diploma or equivalent • Availability to work flexible hours, Monday through Friday between 5 am – 9 pm, including weekends if required. • Reliable transportation • Must be able to sit for long periods and walk long distances. • Experience in a manufacturing or production environment • Knowledge of production processes and workflow management • College degree in a related field but not necessary • People management skills Apply Now First Name (required) cff008d1 Last Name (required) a9bc26a8 Email (required) d4733057 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) c856d164 Last Name (required) 5bc32af3 Email (required) c4266023 Job Alert b017ccbe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 2fb4c126 Last Name (required) a8b8b841 Email (required) ced31c65 Sen