    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-educator-american-sign-language-program-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program",
      "description": "Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program 499617 On Site Faculty Department: American Sign Language Program Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $ 50,000-$55,000 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, times variable dependent on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Modern & Classical Languages & Literatures (MCLL) at Wichita State University seeks a passionate and student-centered educator to join its American Sign Language program as an Assistant Educator of American Sign Language with a focus on Interpreter Education. This is a 9-month, non-tenure track faculty appointment beginning August 2, 2027. This position offers the opportunity to foster a new generation of ASL interpreters while contributing to a growing and collaborative language department that values applied learning, community engagement, and service. The successful candidate will help strengthen connections between the university, the Deaf community, and professional interpreting environments while fostering student success through innovative teaching and mentorship. Success in this role means that students graduate with stronger ASL fluency, basic/foundational interpreting skills, and meaningful connections to the Deaf community. Through collaborative teaching, mentorship, and service, you will help advance interpreter education while contributing to a vibrant academic environment and the greater Wichita community. The Department of Modern & Classical Languages & Literatures offers majors in French, Spanish, and American Sign Language, along with minors in French, Spanish, American Sign Language, Japanese, and German. Faculty engage in diverse areas of scholarship and practice, and Wichita State is recognized for its commitment to applied learning and meaningful partnerships with industry and community organizations. This position provides the opportunity to make a lasting impact on students, contribute to the advancement of interpreter education, and engage in service both on campus and throughout the Wichita community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teach undergraduate American Sign Language and interpreter education courses through a variety of instructional modalities. Create engaging learning experiences that integrate applied learning, experiential projects, and industry-relevant practices. Collaborate with ASL faculty on curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives. Mentor and advise students as they pursue academic, professional, and career goals in interpreting and Deaf community engagement. Build and maintain relationships with local Deaf community organizations and stakeholders to support student learning and language access initiatives. Participate in outreach activities that enhance community engagement and promote the ASL program. Contribute service to the department, college, university, and the broader ASL and interpreting professions. Support Wichita State University's commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and community-connected learning. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree or Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements MA degree in American Sign Language, Interpreting, or related field by start date. Fluency in American Sign Language as demonstrated by test scores or credentials such as but not limited to: ASLPI score of 4 or higher, SLPI rating of Advanced Plus or higher, BEI Advanced Certification, RID certification (NIC or CDI). Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Effective written communication skills. Ability to develop and collaborate in a robust teaching program. Ability to collaborate with diverse academic and non-academic groups. Effective mentoring skills. Demonstrated teaching effectiveness Preferred Qualifications: ASL Interpreting degree Interdisciplinary/industry collaboration experience as demonstrated by professional credentials in the ASL Interpreting profession (either state or national level). Demonstrated instructional effectiveness in teaching interpreting and ASL related content at the college level. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Teaching Statement, including any (including examples of teaching experience i.e. workshops, courses taught, etc., and teaching evaluations if possible) Review of applications will start on December 15th and will continue until the position has been filled . Letters of recommendation will be requested to semifinalists. Feel free to contact Dr. Edward Bart Edward.bart@wichita.edu or Dr. Rocio del Aguila rocio.delaguila@wichita.edu for any questions. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 7c64c038 Last Name (required) d5577e4d Email (required) 570ab7fa Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 1ca187b7 Last Name (required) e4778fb1 Email (required) 719f3742 Job Alert bea62394 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 6011c2b9 Last Name (required) 1d01bb15 Email (required) a3f71810 Send This Job To: 00eb046a Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Paper Grader-Yuan Liu Are you a detail-oriented student with a strong background in mathematics and/or statistics, and the ability to work independently on assigned tasks? The Mathematics and Statistics department is seeking qualified student paper graders for the spring semester 2027. Paper Grader-Catherine Cannizzo Are you a detail-oriented student with a strong background in mathematics and/or statistics, and the ability to work independently on assigned tasks? The Mathematics and Statistics department is seeking qualified student paper graders for the spring semester 2027. Paper Grader-Tianshi Lu Are you a detail-oriented student with a strong background in mathematics and/or statistics, and the ability to work independently on assigned tasks? The Mathematics and Statistics department is seeking qualified student paper graders for the spring semester 2027. Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus The WSU - Ascension Via Christi School of Nursing is accepting applications for an Assistant Educator (MSN prepared)/Assistant Teaching Professor (DNP prepared) to provide instruction of didactic, clinical and/or technologies labs, and teaching/supervision in the undergraduate/graduate program as appropriate by educational preparation. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 0c2c6f2e Last Name (required) 6317bb02 Email (required) 3a74bac9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
