    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/university-police-chief-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "University Police Chief",
      "description": "University Police Chief - Wichita, Kansas, United States University Police Chief - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode University Police Chief WSU Police Department | Staff University Police Chief 499719 Staff Department: WSU Police Department Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range from $108,000-$140,000/yr, negotiated based on qualifications Work Schedule: 8-5 Monday-Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story Wichita State University invites applications for University Police Chief (Chief). The Chief serves as the chief law enforcement and public safety executive for the Wichita State University and provides strategic leadership, direction, and oversight for all police and public safety operations. The Chief is responsible for developing and implementing a comprehensive campus public safety program that supports the University's academic, research, residential, healthcare, and administrative missions while promoting a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, staff, visitors, and the broader university community. Job Summary Directs, plans and manages all functions and operations of the University police department in the enforcement of laws and University regulations, the prevention of crime, and protection of life and property. Essential Functions Directs and coordinates University security, safety and protection programs to include traffic control, patrolling of physical property; enforcement of statues and University regulations, crime prevention and investigation of accidents, injuries and criminal acts. Serves as the face and spokesperson of the University for all law enforcement related issues. Maintains a high degree of visibility, represents the department in the local community and serves a central role in establishing and maintaining strong collaborative relationships with University staff and local, regional, state and federal public safety agencies. Develops department budget and monitors and adjusts plan as resource requirements change. Provides timely and accurate reports in compliance with local, state, and federal regulations and higher education guidelines including monthly criminal and conduct statistics, crime reports, and the annual DOE Clery Act report. Develops and leads managers and officers in the efficient and effective administration of law enforcement initiatives and programs. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Ten (10) years of experience in general law enforcement or related field, including progressively responsible supervisory and managerial experience at the command staff level. Every 30 hours of college coursework in criminal justice, fire science, law enforcement or related field can be substituted for one (1) year of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: Meet minimum qualifications standards of the State of Kansas for certified police officer as outlined in K.S.A. 74-5605 Certified law enforcement officer or capability to become a Kansas certified law enforcement officer within one year of hire date, in accordance with Kansas law Completed basic law enforcement training program recognized by Kansas Law Enforcement Training Commission (KLETC) and obtained certification as a law enforcement officer from KLETC before given permanent status Complete and receive Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) and National Crime Information Center (NCIC) certification within one (1) year of hire date or will be terminated Valid Kansas driver's license Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to manage a full-service police department, budgets and daily operations. Ability to work effectively in collaborative environments and engage constructively with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Experience on a leadership team within a department High level of law enforcement experience. Experience in an educational environment Additional Information: Application Instructions: - Verification of Highest Level of Education (please provide a copy of your transcript or scanned copy of your diploma/equivalency as required by KSA 74-5605). Providing false or misleading statements within this application, whether intentional or not, will result in permanent removal from the application process. During the application process your background will be closely examined. Please review the following background “disqualifiers.” If you think that any of these apply to you and you have questions, please call the Wichita State University Police Department at (316) 978- 3450 for clarification, or for more information. Must satisfy all requirements as set forth in Kansas Statute 74 – 5605. Must satisfy all requirements as set forth by Wichita State University www.wichita.edu If military service has been rendered your DD214 must reflect a separation code and an Honorable Discharge or an Under Honorable Conditions (General). Uncharacterized discharges are reviewed on a case by case basis. Applicants may be eliminated from the process if they have not fully disclosed ALL information requested. Applicants WILL be eliminated from the process if they have falsified, intentionally misrepresented, or have not been completely truthful on a questionnaire, document, or application as part of the pre-employment process. Applicants will be permanently disqualified for the following if: Has been convicted, expunged, or received diversion on any state, municipality, or federal misdemeanor crime of domestic violence or its equivalent under the Uniform Code of Military Justice. As an adult or juvenile (17 years old or younger), has been involved, convicted, expunged, or on or after July 1, 1995, been placed on diversion by state or federal government for a crime which is a felony (includes sale of illegal or prescription drugs) or its equivalent under the Uniform Code of Military Justice. As an adult or juvenile (17 years old or younger) may not have been convicted of a crime involving an act of dishonesty, to include but not limited to; theft, insufficient funds (check), fraud, false police reports, etc. Applicants may be temporarily disqualified for the following: Must not have used or possessed any felony level drug or controlled substance, i.e. cocaine, heroin, opium, methamphetamine, etc. within the past 10 years of date of application. Convictions, diversions, expungements, or involvement in any misdemeanor crimes of violence, or use of physical force or threats within the past five years of date of application. Convictions, diversions, expungements or involvement in misdemeanor crimes within the past three years of date of application. Convictions, diversions, expungements or involvement in any misdemeanor crimes involving morals, or weapons charges within the past five years of date of application. Must not have used, bought, or possessed marijuana, LSD, hashish, mushrooms, K 2, peyote, ecstasy, etc., within the past three years of date of application. Must not have used, bought, or possessed illegal or non – prescriptive steroids within the past three years of date of application. Must not have been convicted of, plead guilty or no contest to, or been diverted on a serious traffic violation within the past three years of date of application. Serious traffic violations to include, but not limited to vehicular homicide, DUI, reckless driving, hit and run, and eluding a police officer. Must not have received three moving violations during the last twelve months or been involved in two accidents for which they were at fault during the past twelve months. Must not have been convicted, taken diversion, plead guilty or no contest to an MIP (minor in possession of alcohol) or MIC (minor in consumption) within the past twelve months of date of application. Must not be currently charged with, under indictment, or on probation for any criminal activity other than minor traffic violations. If previous law enforcement experience has been rendered, must not have a sustained violation of dishonesty to include but not limited to, lying, falsifying reports or documents, illegally obtaining narcotics, courtroom testimony/credibility For the purposes of this application process “conviction” includes rendering of judgement by a military court martial pursuant to the uniform code of military justice, by a court of the United States or by a court of competent jurisdiction in any state, whether or not expunged; and any diversion agreement entered into for a misdemeanor crime of domestic violence and any diversion agreement entered into on or after July 1, 1995, for a felony. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to inspect and/or surveil materials, equipment, reports, and/or incidents and identify any errors, needs and/or determining factors. Ability to drive state vehicle. Ability to position self to perform safety and security actions determined by police methods and procedures. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) a91cb3f1 Last Name (required) ae751192 Email (required) 317041bf Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4d6ad056 Last Name (required) dd8a390e Email (required) bcaa2d95 Job Alert f433cec9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) WSU Police Department WSU Police Department Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) addfe0f9 Last Name (required) 15d92d69 Email (required) 1d6d64ba Send This Job To: d4b6df33 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life The Pathfinders’ position is a vital member of the Residence Life staff. Pathfinders contribute to residents' education by serving as mentors, role models, and academic resources, and by connecting them with other key departments across campus. The Pathfinders will play a key role in fulfilling the academic mission of the Housing and Residence Life department. It is important that Pathfinders develop and maintain open lines of communication with faculty and staff involved in LLC and Housing and Residence Life. To achieve these goals, the Pathfinders must be actively engaged with students in their LLC and with various campus departments. This person will report directly to the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. In addition, the Pathfinders will work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Postdoctoral Researcher, Forensic Psychology The Forensic Psychology Postdoctoral Residency Program offers a comprehensive, clinically intensive structured training experience designed for clinical psychology doctoral graduates who are committed to specializing in the application of psychological science to legal questions. Grounded in scientist-practitioner principles, the residency integrates advanced forensic assessment, empirical research, professional mentorship, and engagement with the legal and justice communities. NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R Seeking motivated students currently enrolled at WSU who are interested in tutoring middle/high students during the academic year. Eligibility requirements include a 3.0 GPA or higher, valid driver's license and reliable transportation, good verbal and written communication skills, and ability to use Microsoft Word, Excel, and Access. HR Assistant - Shared Services Making an impact happens in this position in so many ways and with so many people! Our team focuses on providing detailed and accurate service to our university partners in all aspects related to hiring, onboarding & after hire updates. This makes this position dedicated to customer service and problem resolution to solution focused. Downstream effects of our work impact multiple systems and partners. We seek an individual who can identify errors others miss & ensure the team is being as accurate, effective & efficient as possible. Your day can change from standard daily tasks to switching gears into problem solving mode or address customer concerns in an instant & then end with an appointment with an employee. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) c62f51a5 Last Name (required) ba2da870 Email (required) 747ed9ee Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-main-campus-wichita-kansas-united-states-56acd5e4-d949-4aee-8d45-a9c063829bb1": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus College of Health Professions | Faculty Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus 499760 On Site Faculty Department: WSU-AVC School of Nursing Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starts at $67,000 Work Schedule: Typically M-F 8-5, occasional weekend or evening shift; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The WSU - Ascension Via Christi School of Nursing is accepting applications for a 9-month Assistant Teaching Professor (DNP prepared) to provide instruction of didactic, clinical and/or technologies labs, and teaching/supervision in the undergraduate/graduate program as appropriate by educational preparation. This position will also participate in curriculum development and evaluation and will be expected to maintain academic and professional expertise. Participation in Department, College, and University activities and committees is expected. The nursing program is very robust with a traditional RN program, an RN-BSN completion program, and Masters’ program with a focus on education, and a DNP program with foci in FNP, PMHNP, and AGPNP. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree Teaching experience Faculty Requirements DNP (Doctor of Nursing Practice) Valid Kansas State APRN License Valid Kansas State Nursing License Nurse Practitioner Certificate Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent interpersonal skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills Computer competency Knowledge of clinical practice Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) 8ab4f87e Last Name (required) 99508c6a Email (required) ae7eaf9b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4497a468 Last Name (required) 6d7d186a Email (required) 071dfd58 Job Alert 168cac67 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Health Professions College of Health Professions Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) a010a4d3 Last Name (required) c539a709 Email (required) 281f247b Send This Job To: 8485c827 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life The Pathfinders’ position is a vital member of the Residence Life staff. Pathfinders contribute to residents' education by serving as mentors, role models, and academic resources, and by connecting them with other key departments across campus. The Pathfinders will play a key role in fulfilling the academic mission of the Housing and Residence Life department. It is important that Pathfinders develop and maintain open lines of communication with faculty and staff involved in LLC and Housing and Residence Life. To achieve these goals, the Pathfinders must be actively engaged with students in their LLC and with various campus departments. This person will report directly to the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. In addition, the Pathfinders will work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Postdoctoral Researcher, Forensic Psychology The Forensic Psychology Postdoctoral Residency Program offers a comprehensive, clinically intensive structured training experience designed for clinical psychology doctoral graduates who are committed to specializing in the application of psychological science to legal questions. Grounded in scientist-practitioner principles, the residency integrates advanced forensic assessment, empirical research, professional mentorship, and engagement with the legal and justice communities. NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R Seeking motivated students currently enrolled at WSU who are interested in tutoring middle/high students during the academic year. Eligibility requirements include a 3.0 GPA or higher, valid driver's license and reliable transportation, good verbal and written communication skills, and ability to use Microsoft Word, Excel, and Access. HR Assistant - Shared Services Making an impact happens in this position in so many ways and with so many people! Our team focuses on providing detailed and accurate service to our university partners in all aspects related to hiring, onboarding & after hire updates. This makes this position dedicated to customer service and problem resolution to solution focused. Downstream effects of our work impact multiple systems and partners. We seek an individual who can identify errors others miss & ensure the team is being as accurate, effective & efficient as possible. Your day can change from standard daily tasks to switching gears into problem solving mode or address customer concerns in an instant & then end with an appointment with an employee. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 9cf220e6 Last Name (required) 13094285 Email (required) 2160cb35 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
