      "title": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus College of Health Professions | Faculty Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus 499756 On Site Faculty Department: AVC-WSU School of Nursing Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $65,000 Work Schedule: Typically M-F days; occasional weekend or evening; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The WSU - Ascension Via Christi School of Nursing is accepting applications for a 9-month Assistant Educator (MSN prepared)/Assistant Teaching Professor (DNP prepared) to provide instruction of didactic, clinical and/or technologies labs, and teaching/supervision in the undergraduate/graduate program as appropriate by educational preparation. This position will also participate in curriculum development and evaluation and will be expected to maintain academic and professional expertise. Participation in Department, College, and University activities and committees is expected. The nursing program is very robust with a traditional RN program, an RN-BSN completion program, and Masters’ program with a focus on education, and a DNP program with foci in FNP, PMHNP, and AGPNP. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Assistant Educator - MSN Assistant Teaching Professor - doctoral degree in nursing Valid Kansas Nursing license Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent interpersonal skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills Computer competency Knowledge of clinical practice Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) e807c450 Last Name (required) 4b6f9231 Email (required) 7bd301ed Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 19a7bbc7 Last Name (required) e16c3f64 Email (required) 165da88d Job Alert 8410864e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Health Professions College of Health Professions Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 49a97ebd Last Name (required) 408ebe9e Email (required) b724081c Send This Job To: 7b5f87ed Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life The Pathfinders’ position is a vital member of the Residence Life staff. Pathfinders contribute to residents' education by serving as mentors, role models, and academic resources, and by connecting them with other key departments across campus. The Pathfinders will play a key role in fulfilling the academic mission of the Housing and Residence Life department. It is important that Pathfinders develop and maintain open lines of communication with faculty and staff involved in LLC and Housing and Residence Life. To achieve these goals, the Pathfinders must be actively engaged with students in their LLC and with various campus departments. This person will report directly to the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. In addition, the Pathfinders will work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Postdoctoral Researcher, Forensic Psychology The Forensic Psychology Postdoctoral Residency Program offers a comprehensive, clinically intensive structured training experience designed for clinical psychology doctoral graduates who are committed to specializing in the application of psychological science to legal questions. Grounded in scientist-practitioner principles, the residency integrates advanced forensic assessment, empirical research, professional mentorship, and engagement with the legal and justice communities. NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R Seeking motivated students currently enrolled at WSU who are interested in tutoring middle/high students during the academic year. Eligibility requirements include a 3.0 GPA or higher, valid driver's license and reliable transportation, good verbal and written communication skills, and ability to use Microsoft Word, Excel, and Access. HR Assistant - Shared Services Making an impact happens in this position in so many ways and with so many people! Our team focuses on providing detailed and accurate service to our university partners in all aspects related to hiring, onboarding & after hire updates. This makes this position dedicated to customer service and problem resolution to solution focused. Downstream effects of our work impact multiple systems and partners. We seek an individual who can identify errors others miss & ensure the team is being as accurate, effective & efficient as possible. Your day can change from standard daily tasks to switching gears into problem solving mode or address customer concerns in an instant & then end with an appointment with an employee. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 0a1f9b13 Last Name (required) 01bc553d Email (required) cbe5fae0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
