r LLC and with various campus departments. This person will report directly to the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. In addition, the Pathfinders will work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Postdoctoral Researcher, Forensic Psychology The Forensic Psychology Postdoctoral Residency Program offers a comprehensive, clinically intensive structured training experience designed for clinical psychology doctoral graduates who are committed to specializing in the application of psychological science to legal questions. Grounded in scientist-practitioner principles, the residency integrates advanced forensic assessment, empirical research, professional mentorship, and engagement with the legal and justice communities. NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R Seeking motivated students currently enrolled at WSU who are interested in tutoring middle/high students during the academic year. Eligibility requirements include a 3.0 GPA or higher, valid driver's license and reliable transportation, good verbal and written communication skills, and ability to use Microsoft Word, Excel, and Access. HR Assistant - Shared Services Making an impact happens in this position in so many ways and with so many people! Our team focuses on providing detailed and accurate service to our university partners in all aspects related to hiring, onboarding & after hire updates. This makes this position dedicated to customer service and problem resolution to solution focused. Downstream effects of our work impact multiple systems and partners. We seek an individual who can identify errors others miss & ensure the team is being as accurate, effective & efficient as possible. Your day can change from standard daily tasks to switching gears into problem solving mode or address customer concerns in an instant & then end with an appointment with an employee. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive