g and Residence Life department. It is important that Pathfinders develop and maintain open lines of communication with faculty and staff involved in LLC and Housing and Residence Life. To achieve these goals, the Pathfinders must be actively engaged with students in their LLC and with various campus departments. This person will report directly to the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. In addition, the Pathfinders will work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Postdoctoral Researcher, Forensic Psychology The Forensic Psychology Postdoctoral Residency Program offers a comprehensive, clinically intensive structured training experience designed for clinical psychology doctoral graduates who are committed to specializing in the application of psychological science to legal questions. Grounded in scientist-practitioner principles, the residency integrates advanced forensic assessment, empirical research, professional mentorship, and engagement with the legal and justice communities. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) c7147061 Last Name (required) fc2980e1 Email (required) fff75bf0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a pass