    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/pathfinders-housing-and-residence-life-wichita-kansas-united-states-45c0e74c-03f1-4a08-aa5b-81db4aec1ae9": {
      "title": "Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life",
      "description": "Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life - Wichita, Kansas, United States Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life Student Affairs (College) | Academic/Student Support, Student Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life 499877 Academic/Student Support Student Department Housing and Residence Life Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $10/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Variable dependent upon class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The Pathfinders’ position is a vital member of the Residence Life staff. Pathfinders contribute to residents' education by serving as mentors, role models, and academic resources, and by connecting them with other key departments across campus. The Pathfinders will play a key role in fulfilling the academic mission of the Housing and Residence Life department. It is important that Pathfinders develop and maintain open lines of communication with faculty and staff involved in LLC and Housing and Residence Life. To achieve these goals, the Pathfinders must be actively engaged with students in their LLC and with various campus departments. This person will report directly to the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. In addition, the Pathfinders will work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Community Development Responsibilities • Assist residents in formulating academic objectives concurrent with their individual interests and potential skill levels. • Provide residents with information regarding registration, drop/add, and curricular requirements. • Facilitate opportunities for residents to develop in the areas of learning styles, study skills, and test-taking. • Facilitate review sessions, study hours, and other academic support activities for students on the floor. • Establish and maintain appropriate relationships with students in the LLC for the purpose of facilitating the transition to university life and ensuring academic success. • Provide opportunities for developing skills in choosing an academic major and planning a career. • Act as a referral agent by directing students, when appropriate, to various academic support services such as Academic Advising, the Writing Center, the Math Lab, and the Student Success Center. Administrative Responsibilities • Participate in training workshops prior to the beginning of each semester and throughout the academic year. • Help run events during Week Zero. • Attend and participate in staff meetings and one-on-ones. • Facilitate LLC educational programming for residents monthly. • Create and maintain one bulletin board in the building, changing it monthly. • Provide assistance to, and communicate with, faculty, staff members, and LLC Coordinators. • Become knowledgeable about academic services available to students and make appropriate referrals. • Actively participate in LLC floor, university/college programs, and activities, and facilitate residents’ involvement with the same programs and activities. • Work closely with the LLC Coordinators to build community and accomplish academic initiatives. • Work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement to accomplish residence life goals and to ensure that the interests of participating students are integrated into the program. • Serve as a liaison between residents in LLC and other departments, specifically within the Division of Campus Life, Academics, and LLC Coordinators. • Assume other responsibilities related to the LLC floor and residence life programs as directed by the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements • May carry a maximum academic course load of 16 hours during each semester of employment. Any exception must be approved in writing by the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement. • Be available for training the week before move-in. • Must maintain a minimum cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 during the period of employment. • Attend and participate in one-on-ones with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. • Attend and participate in staff meetings. • May not engage in additional part-time or full-time work, student teaching, internship, or assistantship without prior written approval from the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications • Possess a motivating interest in working with the students in Shocker Hall. • Have a minimum cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 on a 4.0 scale. • Be available to serve on the staff for two (2) consecutive semesters (Fall & Spring). • Have lived in a WSU residence hall for at least one (1) semester. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) ad1dce45 Last Name (required) b6914d2a Email (required) 766ccedd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) adcb9b26 Last Name (required) 6655c6fe Email (required) 2d21eef2 Job Alert e241722f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Student Academic/Student Support Student Department(s) Student Affairs (College) Student Affairs (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 5a698b5f Last Name (required) 4ca0c9a3 Email (required) 2fc4285e Send This Job To: 0474ddd4 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Student Assistant/Student Adminstrative Assistant The TRIO SSS STEM Program is seeking a detail-oriented and organized student to serve as a Student Administrative Assistant. This position will play an important role in supporting program operations and helping develop administrative processes for a growing federally funded student success program serving STEM majors. This position is ideal for a student interested in organizational leadership, business administration, project management, communications, higher education, nonprofit management, or related fields who would like practical experience supporting program operations and student services. Director Academic Advising - College of Engineering Solving problems is what we do, what this position does & what this program is known for! The field of study was established for just that purpose, covering so many aspects of life. The arsenal of skills you need for success: detail focused, follow through, respect & empathy, efficiency, & professional communication to lead a team of professional advisors delivering superior service to engineering students. Postdoctoral Researcher, Forensic Psychology The Forensic Psychology Postdoctoral Residency Program offers a comprehensive, clinically intensive structured training experience designed for clinical psychology doctoral graduates who are committed to specializing in the application of psychological science to legal questions. Grounded in scientist-practitioner principles, the residency integrates advanced forensic assessment, empirical research, professional mentorship, and engagement with the legal and justice communities. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 312f8c38 Last Name (required) de86ff78 Email (required) 4149dc95 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
