    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/nbe-student-assistant-wsu-0350r-wichita-kansas-united-states-4935fac6-a37c-404e-ab62-f089dbd896ef": {
      "title": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R",
      "description": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R 499875 Student Department TRIO Talent Search-South Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $10.00/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Mon-Fri 8:00am-5:30pm, Flexible Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Seeking motivated students currently enrolled at WSU who are interested in tutoring middle/high students during the academic year. Eligibility requirements include a 3.0 GPA or higher, valid driver's license and reliable transportation, good verbal and written communication skills, and ability to use Microsoft Word, Excel, and Access. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Tutoring middle/high students in math, science, and other subjects during the school year. Document tutoring sessions with students. Perform other duties as required by their supervisor. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements 1. Undergraduate or graduate standing at WSU with a 3.0 or better grade point average 2. Ability to tutor language arts, math, science and/or study skills to middle and high school students 3. Strong time management and organizational skills 4. Strong oral and written communication skills 5. Commitment to working with eligible student populations 6. Knowledge of problems facing low-income and potential first generation college students Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 623f9e36 Last Name (required) 76eddf23 Email (required) f4193c25 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 45ab125c Last Name (required) f17df2a3 Email (required) 8ca250c1 Job Alert 5c74e9bc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) dbe79440 Last Name (required) e1fd7114 Email (required) 92d4d24b Send This Job To: 209fd209 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs